WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.460
An SCP Foundation researcher sits at a table
inside of a standard containment cell.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:11.280
These are often dangerous places to be, especially
when the SCP you’re supposed to be studying

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.900
is one that you can’t see.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.240
The researcher is taking notes, unsure of
exactly what’s going to happen next.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:24.180
He can hear the sounds of knives scraping
behind, of flesh sizzling and searing from

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:24.840
high heat.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:30.180
He braces himself as a burst of heat hits
the back of his head, as if a fireball has

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:30.637
erupted.

00:00:30.637 --> 00:00:34.380
Just then it happens - an object floats through
the air and settles in front of him on the

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.040
table.
It’s a plate of food, and it looks delicious.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:43.320
It may surprise you to learn that there is
no rule that the SCP Foundation must deal

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.260
exclusively with violent and vicious creatures.

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:51.840
Not every SCP held in containment shares the
same malevolence and contempt for humanity

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:58.500
as SCP-682, or the world-ending threat posed
by the likes of SCP-2317.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:05.700
Some - perhaps not many, but some - are benign
and might even seem outwardly friendly, but

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:10.620
you’d still be taking a huge risk to assume
that anything contained by the SCP Foundation

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.060
is completely harmless.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:15.600
Such is the case with SCP-5031.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.940
As per the Foundation’s containment procedures,
this quasi-humanoid – meaning it appears

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:26.280
to have some vaguely human features - is held
in an airtight cell that is regularly checked

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:28.980
by Foundation personnel on a bi-weekly basis.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:35.160
SCP-5031 has no need for regular nutrition
or regular interactions from staff.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:41.820
The trick with SCP-5031, is not being eaten
by it, since though it doesn’t need food,

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:47.400
it does still hunt and consume anything it
encounters - human or otherwise.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:53.820
Avoiding being eaten is hard enough with creatures
that can actually be seen, but like so many

00:01:53.820 --> 00:02:00.180
other creatures the Foundation keeps contained,
SCP-5031 has developed an almost-perfect defense

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:05.100
mechanism - which is that when observed, it
will literally cease to exist.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:10.860
Some might choose to refer to this as a ‘quantum
lock’, however it is worth noting that traces

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:16.560
left by SCP-5031 still remain observable when
the creature has temporarily disappeared.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:23.040
For example, trails of blood and scratch marks
left behind by SCP-5031 still exist when the

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.660
SCP itself does not.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:30.660
Naturally, this makes both avoiding the creature
and capturing it using cameras difficult.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:36.540
However, when SCP-5031’s existence ceases
it still casts a shadow.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:41.460
From this, researchers have been able to determine
several of the creature’s physical traits.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:47.700
Based on its silhouette, it has been deduced
that SCP-5031 levitates about half a meter

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:52.980
above ground level, it sports an abnormally
small, neckless head atop an elongated torso

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:59.340
- approximately 1.9 meters long - with three
sets of spindly lower arms that branch outwards.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:05.460
Using these arms and its loosely hanging body,
SCP-5031 will lower itself to hunt any human

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:10.620
or animal that draws near to it and uses the
bladelike tail to cut up food.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:18.180
Perhaps the most interesting facet of SCP-5031
beyond its defensive capabilities and apparent

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:23.940
physical attributes, are the series of nine
tests conducted by Senior Researcher Stanley

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:24.480
Huxtable.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:29.040
Appalled by the conditions that the creature
was being kept in, Huxtable took over the

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.400
role of HCL Supervisor for SCP-5031.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.400
Having grown increasingly&nbsp;
frustrated and empathetic&nbsp;

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.740
towards the creature, listening to its screams

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:43.860
from inside its iron containment unit, Huxtable
devised a series of tests to introduce SCP-5031

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:48.900
to various different stimuli as a way to better
understand the creature and hopefully keep

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:52.320
it contained in a way that didn’t seem to
cause so much suffering.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:57.900
It's worth remembering that the SCP Foundation
makes it its mission to be cold, not cruel,

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:03.360
in performing their duties to protect normality
and many of the researchers and staff are

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:08.040
just as capable of having empathy for creatures
as you might for a stray animal at a shelter.

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:14.460
The first of Huxtable’s tests involved installing
speakers in SCP-5031’s cell, through which

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:18.540
a variety of different ambient and popular
pieces of music were played to see if they

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:21.000
had any effect on reducing the creature’s
stress.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:26.760
By judging SCP-5031’s stress levels based
on how much it screamed when compared to normal,

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:31.380
Huxtable was able to determine how to best
to use music to calm the creature.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:36.780
SCP-5031 seemed to convey higher levels of
stress when listening to ‘Morning Forest’,

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:42.180
‘Deep Grotto’ and ‘Seaside Paradise’
ambience, as well as the best of late 60s

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:43.860
British rock band Jethro Tull.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:49.380
However, the best of Mozart, Enya, KISS and
Ben Folds produced dramatically different

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:53.100
results, decreasing SCP-5031’s apparent
stress.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:58.980
Following this test, Senior Researcher Huxtable
compiled a playlist featuring SCP-5031’s

00:04:58.980 --> 00:04:59.700
favorite music.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:06.120
Over time, the stress-reducing effects of
music on SCP-5031 seemed to decrease, but

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:10.080
keeping the playlist on shuffle seemed to
keep the creature consistently calmer than

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.220
it had been previously.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:18.180
The next test involved introducing inanimate
objects into SCP-5031’s enclosure to monitor

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.940
its reactions and how its stress levels were
affected.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:27.000
When a softball was thrown into the enclosure,
SCP-5031 immediately sliced the ball in two

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.220
with its tail in one swift motion.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:33.960
A similar result occurred when researchers
threw the creature a basketball, which was

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:37.800
quickly punctured and sliced open by SCP-5031’s
tail.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:42.060
Its stress levels first seemed to diminish
when the creature was offered a bowling ball,

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:46.680
which it rolled around the enclosure and then
later knocked against a second bowling ball.

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:53.520
However, when one of the balls chipped, rendering
it unable to roll properly, SCP-5031’s stress

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.820
increased dramatically, until a replacement
was offered.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:02.820
Researcher Huxtable noted that SCP-5031 seemed
to possess a similar level of motor skills

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:07.680
to an average human toddler, with similarly
explosive emotional reactions to match.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:13.200
Next, when given the choice between two food
sources at opposite ends of its enclosure,

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.800
SCP-5031 seemed to gravitate&nbsp;
towards higher-quality&nbsp;

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.560
food, most notably favoring cooked rotisserie

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.180
chickens over animal carcasses.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.300
It even chose this option over a live chicken,&nbsp;

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:27.120
using its tail to cut its&nbsp;
food into more manageable

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:31.860
bite-sized portions, rather than ripping its
meat with its hands or teeth like many of

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.060
its fellow SCPs.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:39.720
Researcher Huxtable recorded these findings
and highlighted that, even though SCP-5031

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:44.520
didn’t need to eat in order to survive,
providing the creature with food of a better

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:47.100
quality marginally reduced its stress.

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:53.580
Senior Researcher Huxtable next attempted
to test SCP-5031’s coexistence with other

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:59.400
living subjects, each time making sure that
the creature had been adequately fed to avoid

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:01.020
any unseemly incidents.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:03.960
First, a live chicken was introduced.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:09.840
SCP-5031 rolled its bowling ball at high speed
towards the chicken, increasing both its and

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:13.500
the chicken’s stress levels, and inadvertently
killing the chicken in the process.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:20.400
When a second chicken was introduced, SCP-5031
gently rolled a basketball towards it but

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:24.120
ceased any further engagement after the chicken
squawked from being hit by the ball.

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:29.400
Next to be introduced into the enclosure was
a blindfolded D Class staff member, who was

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:33.420
instructed to sit down and roll the basketball
towards SCP-5031.

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:38.700
After doing so for several minutes, the creature
began to approach the D class subject, who

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:42.600
was instructed to remove their blindfold to
cease the creature’s existence and prevent

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:44.280
any potentially deadly incidents.

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:50.760
Finally, Researcher Huxtable had another Class-D
engage in a game of catch with SCP-5031 while

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:52.140
facing away from the creature.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:59.040
This test proceeded successfully, and Senior
Researcher Huxtable remarked how SCP-5031’s

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.360
motor skills were improving.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:03.420
Albeit gradually, and with&nbsp;
some gentle encouragement,&nbsp;

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:06.960
through Huxtable’s tests the creature was

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:07.460
learning.

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:14.700
The next test, focused on teaching SCP-5031
linguistic symbols, utilized LCD displays

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:16.800
and buttons connected to a food dispenser.

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:21.180
One display showed an image of a rock, and
the other an image of a rotisserie chicken.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:26.940
After some brief probing, SCP-5031 was quickly
able to understand that pressing the button

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:30.600
under the correct display would dispense a
rotisserie chicken for it to eat.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:35.580
The creature was later able to adapt when,
the following day, the screen displays and

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:39.960
materials dispensed were swapped, and then
later set to swap at random intervals.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:44.040
When additional rock-dispensing stations were
introduced, this time displaying the word

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:50.040
‘rock’ as opposed to an image, SCP-5031
was able to determine which station dispensed

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:52.320
‘chicken’ through a process of elimination.

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:58.020
Whenever the functions and displays were swapped,
SCP-5031 would find whichever displayed the

00:08:58.020 --> 00:08:59.640
word ‘chicken’ to receive its food.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:05.940
The final phase of this test presented SCP-5031
with a single station, displaying the word

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:10.260
‘chicken’, but with a button that would
remain inactive unless the creature spelled

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:14.160
out the same word with a collection of lettered
blocks it was provided with.

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:19.140
After some initial confusion and frustration
as to why the button would not dispense food

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:25.800
when pressed, SCP-5031 was able to assemble
the word correctly, not only activating the

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:30.420
button and dispensing food, but proving to
Researcher Huxtable that the creature was

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:32.220
capable of learning language.

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:35.640
Huxtable continued to test&nbsp;
the creature, encouraging&nbsp;

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:37.920
it to spell words using lettered blocks as

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:39.000
a method of communicating.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:44.640
By increasing SCP-5031’s vocabulary and
the amount of human interaction it received,

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:48.780
Senior Researcher Huxtable observed that SCP-5031&nbsp;

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:52.156
was gradually learning to&nbsp;
sing - albeit nonverbally

00:09:52.156 --> 00:09:54.840
- as well as to juggle with its six hands&nbsp;

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.420
and was even communicating&nbsp;
its own food preferences

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:58.440
and dish pairings.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:06.900
Later, another Class-D, D-52125, was introduced
to SCP-5031’s enclosure to aid in further

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:07.320
testing.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:13.260
Through D-52125’s instructions, the creature
quickly learned to draw using crayons, and

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:20.160
created artworks depicting itself, its newfound
friend D-52125, Researcher Huxtable, a cat

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:21.720
and a rotisserie chicken.

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:28.020
SCP-5031’s new creative side didn’t stop
there though, as the creature quickly learned

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:32.820
to play Chopsticks in only two days once a
piano was introduced into the enclosure.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:39.420
SCP-5031 even managed to start creating its
own original, admittedly crude, compositions.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:42.780
Next, a spice rack was&nbsp;
placed inside the creature’s&nbsp;

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:46.080
cell and D-52125 demonstrated how to season

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:46.620
meat.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:49.920
This proved to be SCP-5031’s new favorite&nbsp;

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:52.920
hobby, as it spent the next&nbsp;
three days experimenting

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:58.170
with different combinations of foods and spices,
using its letter blocks to request ‘more,

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:00.540
more, more’ garlic powder.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:07.380
Interestingly, the creature only created artwork
or music when D-52125 was present, but seemed

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:10.740
to thoroughly enjoy its experimentation with
food when left alone.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:17.160
Following this development, Senior Researcher
Huxtable devised a new test for SCP-5031.

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:24.120
Providing the creature with cooking utensils
and using D-52125 to demonstrate, 5031 was

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:29.220
shown how to prepare a variety of different
dishes, from hamburgers and tacos, to Mongolian

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:32.400
Beef, steak, clam chowder and profiteroles.

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:39.120
In addition to a small peanut allergy, this
eighth test revealed SCP-5031 to be a phenomenal

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:43.320
chef, possessing culinary skills far beyond
the average person.

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:48.420
The creature quickly and enthusiastically
embraced its newfound talents, concocting

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:54.600
its very own brand-new recipes, with D-52125
even volunteering to be the first to taste

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:56.340
test 5031’s dishes.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:12:04.080
It was shortly after this test that SCP-5031
spoke its very first word, and it should come

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:07.200
as no surprise that the word was ‘salt’.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:11.940
Naturally, Senior Researcher Huxtable was
very proud of the progress the creature had

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.200
made with its development.

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:17.040
The final test almost seemed to be what the
creature was born for.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:22.620
Over the course of two months, SCP-5031 was
tasked with creating a full three-course meal

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:25.800
which would then be served to Foundation staff
for Thanksgiving.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:32.160
SCP-5031 not only rose to the task, but exceeded
all of Researcher Huxtable’s expectations,

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:36.660
creating a meal that even Gordon Ramsey would
be hard pressed to find fault with.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:42.780
The creature created a first course consisting
of sweet potato miso soup seasoned with turmeric.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:48.060
Next came a beautiful duck confit, glazed
luxuriously with apple cider and topped generously

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:52.620
with sweet cranberry compote, paired with
a side of butternut squash gnocchi and served

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:54.900
on a bed of kale seasoned with truffle salt.

00:12:54.900 --> 00:13:00.720
The grand finale of the exquisite meal was
a spiced cassava pie for dessert, complemented

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:04.440
with the finest French vanilla ice cream and
a maple-hazelnut syrup.

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:09.000
And SCP-5031 didn’t stop there, the creature&nbsp;

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.880
also debuted one of its&nbsp;
original musical compositions

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:14.220
to compliment the decadent meal it had created.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:20.820
As the staff enjoyed the food, SCP-5031 performed
live from its enclosure the deeply moving

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:27.600
Piano Concerto for Six Hands, to an overwhelmingly
positive response from not only Senior Researcher

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:30.240
Huxtable, but the entire Foundation staff.

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:35.220
As a fitting end to the creature’s tale,
Huxtable reported that, during the Thanksgiving

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:40.560
banquet it had created, SCP-5031’s stress
levels reduced entirely.

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:46.680
New kinder containment measures that would
keep 5031 safer but also far more contented

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.120
were submitted for approval.

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:53.580
Perhaps some of you may find it refreshing
to learn that SCP-5031 isn’t simply just

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:57.780
another malicious, malevolent monster that
the Foundation has to keep under lock and

00:13:57.780 --> 00:13:59.280
key for the safety of the world.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:06.540
Instead, SCP-5031 is a gentle – if a little
frightening at first creature - that just

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:12.180
requires careful and considered guidance instead
of a cold iron cage and around-the-clock armed

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:12.780
guards.

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:18.420
Through testing, Senior Researcher Stanley
Huxtable and his fellow Foundation staff were

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:23.700
not only able to help the creature develop,
but also found what makes it tick; and not

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:25.620
just for the purposes of containing it.

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:32.580
Instead, it is hoped that SCP-5031’s creativity
and flair for culinary and musical masterpieces

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:37.380
can continue to thrive and grow, under the
proud watch of Researcher Huxtable.

00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:43.200
A veteran worker of the SCP Foundation sits
at his terminal, performing one of the most

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:48.780
critical tasks in the entire organization
- creating a file for an as yet undescribed

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:49.560
SCP.

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:51.660
But there’s something terribly wrong.

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:58.440
His eyes are glazed over, his mouth hangs
open - is this a zombie or a trained foundation

00:14:58.440 --> 00:14:59.160
researcher?

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:00.960
What is going on?

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:06.180
Like any large international organization,
it takes more than just the exciting, action

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:09.660
filled jobs to keep the wheels turning at
the SCP Foundation.

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:14.880
Sure, the head researchers, guards, mobile
task force soldiers, and members of the O5

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:20.340
Command get all the praise, but a legion of
number crunchers, cleaners, and paper pushers

00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:21.780
are equally important.

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:27.420
One such person was archivist Walter Bainbridge,
who had been tasked with digitizing some of

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:30.120
the older records that the Foundation had
on file.

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:37.980
It was when he was innocently recording the
details on SCP - 050 through 060 that he first

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:42.720
came under the strange and startling effects
of SCP - 055.

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:46.680
But, the most peculiar&nbsp;
part, as with all incidences&nbsp;

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:49.740
of SCP - 055’s anomalous effects taking

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:54.180
hold, is that Walter had no idea any of it
was happening.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:59.760
In his new digitized filing system, he first
took note of SCP - 053.

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:05.400
Euclid Class, also known as the Young Girl,
this anomaly was a seemingly normal human

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:10.440
female child who provoked homicidal insanity
in those directly exposed to her.

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:12.660
Then SCP - 054.

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:19.380
Safe Class, a non-aggressive humanoid female
made entirely of, as well as biologically

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:22.440
and chemically identical to regular spring
water.

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:25.140
Next, SCP - 056.

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:31.140
Euclid Class, a being that changes form to
suit its environment, but only when all observers

00:16:31.140 --> 00:16:32.340
lose focus on it.

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:35.460
And then SCP - 057.

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:40.920
Safe Class, an underground chamber that crushes
the humans who walk within.

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:45.060
It was at this point that Walter received
a concerned message from one of his superiors

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:47.220
at Site-19, Mr. Kovach.

00:16:47.220 --> 00:16:51.900
The message praised the thorough digitization
of the other anomalies’ records, but was

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:56.280
confused about why Walter had left out any
mention of SCP - 055.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:58.620
Immediately, Walter was embarrassed.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:01.740
How could he have forgotten SCP - 055?

00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:08.460
That iconic anomaly known for...Well, he couldn’t
quite say, off the top of his head, but he’d

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:09.660
be sure to look into it.

00:17:09.660 --> 00:17:14.340
A quick trip to the Site 19 Archives showed
him that there was actually quite a hefty

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:20.580
file on the nature of SCP - 055, which must
have been the result of a huge number of studies.

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:25.620
What struck him as strange was that all the
files were filled out in pen rather than being

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:27.540
typed up, like a traditional file.

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:32.340
The majority of these notes were written in
short-hand, too, as though they were frantically

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:35.700
taken during the tests themselves on extremely
short notice.

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:38.520
There weren’t even any redactions.

00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:43.440
Walter made a mental note of what he had seen,
put the file back in its proper place, and

00:17:43.440 --> 00:17:44.940
headed back to his computer terminal.

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:50.100
However, after writing in an almost trancelike
state, he looked back on his work to see that

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:57.600
he had written an entry on SCP - 058, a giant,
evil bovine heart with insect legs and a scorpion

00:17:57.600 --> 00:17:58.140
stinger…

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:00.240
Strange, he thought.

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:05.280
That’s when Walter got a call from Mr. Kovach
on his Foundation-issue phone, and he didn’t

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:06.000
sound happy.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:12.360
He’d given Walter direct instructions to
go back and digitize the files on 055, and

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.520
instead, he’d been working on 058.

00:18:14.520 --> 00:18:15.960
What was the meaning of this?

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:21.120
Walter was typically an extremely loyal and
diligent employee, but the verbal barrage

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:26.400
from his supervisor had him considering talking
back, just this once, and hoping it didn’t

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:30.960
get him demoted to D-Class and thrown into
682’s acid bath for play time.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:36.240
Walter gulped, picked up some courage, and
interrupted Mr. Kovach’s rant to ask if

00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:40.320
he had any idea what SCP - 055 actually was.

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:46.560
The line went silent for a moment, then the
supervisor spoke again, this time with less

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:47.040
confidence.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:51.120
“Of course I can tell you about SCP - 055.

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:54.360
It’s a classic, one of the first hundred.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:19:01.860
How could you forget its...Or, um, you know,
its...I think it’s the one with the...”

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:08.760
Another long pause, as Mr. Kovach seemed to
search for the words, but instead just trailed

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:09.720
off into silence.

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:14.580
Knowing that some of the anomalies on file
were dangerous memetic hazards, Walter was

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:19.080
worried for a moment that he may have accidentally
killed his boss by getting him to think too

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:21.180
hard about SCP - 055.

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:25.740
He asked if Mr. Kovach was okay, and finally
got a reply.

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:28.800
“I’m sorry, I seem to have zoned out for
a second there.

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:30.300
What were we talking about, again?”

00:19:30.840 --> 00:19:33.600
But this time, it was Walter who couldn't
answer.

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:38.220
He had no idea at all what the two of them
were discussing just moments ago.

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:43.500
He felt disoriented and kind of sick, like
they’d taken some low-level amnestics.

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:47.880
Mr. Kovach told Walter to get back to his
filing duties and they’d speak later.

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:52.800
Walter then checked the messages he’d received
from Mr. Kovach earlier, and there it was,

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:55.620
plain as day: “You missed 055.

00:19:55.620 --> 00:19:58.290
Go back and digitize that before proceeding.

00:19:58.290 --> 00:19:59.520
- Mr. K.”

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:05.460
But Walter had never even heard of an SCP
- 055, if such an anomaly even existed!

00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:07.500
What was going on here?

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:12.900
In that moment, Walter realized he was dealing
with something much stranger than just a standard

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:14.040
digitization job.

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:20.340
After all, how could he properly complete
his duties if SCP - 055 seemed to be impossible

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:26.040
to speak, write, or even think about, unless
you were directly observing it at that moment?

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:32.640
Walter had to know, and ask around the entirety
of Site 19 to find the answers if he had to.

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:38.640
Sadly for Walter, he was about to embark on
a much more challenging task than he could

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:39.660
have ever imagined.

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:44.820
To paraphrase a supposed quote from Socrates,
“All I know is that I know nothing.”

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:51.000
And that’s also about the extent of the
knowledge we have on SCP - 055, also known

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:53.640
as The Anti-Meme and the Self-Keeping Secret.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:55.020
What does it look like?

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:58.020
When and how was it obtained by the Foundation?

00:20:58.020 --> 00:20:59.940
What are its anomalous abilities?

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:01.800
Is this thing dangerous?

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:08.220
We may never know, because the only anomalous
ability of SCP - 055 that we’re aware of

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:12.420
is the fact that nobody is capable of retaining
any information about it.

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:19.200
It’s crucial to note that, whatever 055
is, it isn’t invisible, or indescribable.

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:24.600
Foundation personnel are perfectly capable
of entering its containment chamber and observing

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:26.880
it without incident, but mere minutes after&nbsp;

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:29.940
leaving the chamber, any&nbsp;
memories of the particulars

00:21:29.940 --> 00:21:33.420
of 055 seem to spontaneously erase themselves.

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:36.600
Hence, the Self-Keeping Secret.

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:38.580
But this didn’t deter Walter.

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:42.540
Perhaps his greatest advantage was that he
didn’t know enough about the thing he was

00:21:42.540 --> 00:21:45.480
investigating to know how futile his mission
was.

00:21:45.480 --> 00:21:50.760
He wanted to know the unknowable, and a pesky
issue like “impossibility” wouldn’t

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:51.420
stop him.

00:21:51.420 --> 00:21:56.160
He’d get to whoever he needed to at Site
19 to get the answers he needed.

00:21:56.160 --> 00:21:59.940
Of course most people had no knowledge of
the mysterious anomaly.

00:21:59.940 --> 00:22:02.700
The common response he got&nbsp;
back from his colleagues&nbsp;

00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:04.260
was, “055?

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:05.940
Do we even have an 055?”

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:11.160
While the realization of sudden memory loss
- or the realization of 055’s existence

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:17.220
- has been known to cause momentary stress,
there are no known long term physical or mental

00:22:17.220 --> 00:22:19.800
effects from 055’s anomalous abilities.

00:22:19.800 --> 00:22:25.440
It’s a fleeting idea in its purest form
- like forgetting why you walked into a room.

00:22:25.440 --> 00:22:32.040
055 could be the most harmless object on the
Foundation’s roster, or the most deadly.

00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:34.920
Either way, we just don’t know.

00:22:35.580 --> 00:22:38.280
At times, Walter worried he was going insane.

00:22:38.280 --> 00:22:42.360
055, and everything related to it, was gaslighting
him.

00:22:42.360 --> 00:22:44.580
Was 055 even real?

00:22:44.580 --> 00:22:49.920
The one thing that proved to him that 055
must have existed is that its containment

00:22:49.920 --> 00:22:51.420
chamber existed.

00:22:51.960 --> 00:22:56.280
According to the official records kept by
the Foundation on the Site 19 Containment

00:22:56.280 --> 00:23:03.540
Facilities, 055 is kept in a “five by five
by two point five meter square room constructed

00:23:03.540 --> 00:23:07.980
of fifty-foot-thick cement, with a Faraday
cage surrounding the cement walls.”

00:23:07.980 --> 00:23:13.800
The report continues that, “Access is via
a heavy containment door measuring two by

00:23:13.800 --> 00:23:19.320
two point five meters constructed on bearings
to ensure door closes and locks automatically

00:23:19.320 --> 00:23:20.940
unless held open deliberately.”

00:23:21.600 --> 00:23:27.120
055’s cell is one of the few to have no
posted security guards, and any personnel

00:23:27.120 --> 00:23:32.280
working on other SCPs in the area are ordered
to remain at least fifty feet from the geometric

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:36.720
center of 055’s cell, where the anomaly
itself is kept.

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:41.700
When he tried to explore further why the cell
was constructed in this manner, he found that

00:23:41.700 --> 00:23:44.700
- surprise, surprise - nobody knew.

00:23:44.700 --> 00:23:51.360
055 was an anomaly whose containment requirements
were so mysterious that it automatically netted

00:23:51.360 --> 00:23:53.040
itself a Keter Class designation.

00:23:53.040 --> 00:23:58.560
After all, how can you properly contain something
you can’t even hope to comprehend?

00:23:58.560 --> 00:24:02.160
There were plenty of rumors about the true
nature of 055.

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:09.420
Some of the more conspiratorial minds at Site
19 theorized that 055 was actually an autonomous

00:24:09.420 --> 00:24:15.540
or remotely controlled spy inserted into the
site to observe Foundation operations - or

00:24:15.540 --> 00:24:17.220
even humanity as a whole.

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:21.900
If you’re on the more paranoid end of the
psychological spectrum, this theory makes

00:24:21.900 --> 00:24:22.680
total sense.

00:24:22.680 --> 00:24:27.180
An anomaly that’s physically impossible
to remember, even when writings and pictures

00:24:27.180 --> 00:24:30.360
on the subject exist, would be a perfect spy.

00:24:30.360 --> 00:24:34.140
However, this was all ultimately little more
than speculation.

00:24:34.140 --> 00:24:37.860
Walter was barely any further along than when
he started.

00:24:37.860 --> 00:24:42.660
There were multiple points in his investigation
where Walter seriously considered giving up,

00:24:43.320 --> 00:24:46.320
until, finally, he had a major breakthrough.

00:24:46.320 --> 00:24:52.140
Dr. Bartholomew Hughes and Dr. John Marachek
were two scientists that had performed extensive

00:24:52.140 --> 00:24:57.960
research into 055, and who - Walter hoped
- might have the answers he sought about the

00:24:57.960 --> 00:24:59.040
Self-Keeping Secret.

00:24:59.040 --> 00:25:04.920
These scientists were the first to discover
the “Anti-Memetic” nature of 055, performing

00:25:04.920 --> 00:25:09.540
numerous tests on D-Class personnel to see
if it was possible to create feasible written

00:25:09.540 --> 00:25:15.300
records, sketches, or any other records or
impressions that could bypass its anomalous

00:25:15.300 --> 00:25:15.780
effects.

00:25:15.780 --> 00:25:22.500
The disorienting, memory-ruining effects of
055 also extend to any materials concerning

00:25:22.500 --> 00:25:23.520
055.

00:25:23.520 --> 00:25:29.280
It seemed to be a truly uncrackable code,
but Dr. Hughes may have finally found some

00:25:29.280 --> 00:25:30.420
cracks in the armor.

00:25:31.080 --> 00:25:37.200
For starters, the fact we’re able to remember
that 055 is Anti-Memetic is an ironic exception

00:25:37.200 --> 00:25:38.880
to its Anti-Memetic qualities.

00:25:38.880 --> 00:25:45.540
This revelation also inspired another realization
from Dr. Hughes: Would it be possible to discover

00:25:45.540 --> 00:25:50.940
more about 055 from the process of deduction
rather than the typical induction?

00:25:50.940 --> 00:25:57.060
In other words, could they possibly learn
about 055 by figuring out all the things it

00:25:57.060 --> 00:25:59.400
isn’t rather than what it is?

00:25:59.400 --> 00:26:04.140
Dr. Marachek designed an experiment with Dr.
Hughes to explore this theory.

00:26:04.140 --> 00:26:09.840
They designed the experiment around a simple
question: Is 055 not spherical?

00:26:09.840 --> 00:26:15.600
In designing the question to specifically
find out what 055 isn’t, they hoped to subvert

00:26:15.600 --> 00:26:17.580
the anomaly’s Anti-Memetic Powers.

00:26:17.580 --> 00:26:21.540
Walter was fascinated by this potential method
of getting answers.

00:26:21.540 --> 00:26:26.400
Marachek and Hughes found that, while the
questioning process for those exposed was

00:26:26.400 --> 00:26:33.780
often arduous and frustrating, they could
now definitely say that 055 is not a sphere.

00:26:33.780 --> 00:26:40.140
It is theoretically possible to discover the
true nature of 055 by an almost endless barrage

00:26:40.140 --> 00:26:45.600
of deductive questions, though whether command
would authorize the resources for such extensive

00:26:45.600 --> 00:26:47.820
testing is still an open question.

00:26:47.820 --> 00:26:54.060
Walter, in his desperation, begged Marachek
and Hughes for clearance to view 055 himself.

00:26:54.060 --> 00:26:59.280
The curiosity had become too great during
his search to just walk away with the single

00:26:59.280 --> 00:27:01.680
fact that 055 wasn’t spherical.

00:27:01.680 --> 00:27:03.720
He needed to see this thing.

00:27:03.720 --> 00:27:09.540
And after several weeks of filling out forms
and cutting red tape, his wish was finally

00:27:09.540 --> 00:27:10.260
granted.

00:27:10.260 --> 00:27:17.820
Walter Bainbridge was allowed a private audience
with SCP - 055, the subject of his months-long

00:27:17.820 --> 00:27:18.300
obsession.

00:27:18.300 --> 00:27:23.580
Outsiders observed that Walter spent just
over an hour in the containment chamber, taking

00:27:23.580 --> 00:27:29.160
photos, drawing sketches, writing down notes,
recording audio logs, and reciting memory

00:27:29.160 --> 00:27:29.700
mnemonics.

00:27:29.700 --> 00:27:35.040
He was pulling out every stop to counteract
the anti-memetic effects of the Self-Keeping

00:27:35.040 --> 00:27:35.340
Secret.

00:27:35.340 --> 00:27:41.640
He was adamant that he would not be defeated
by his non-spherical nemesis, not after all

00:27:41.640 --> 00:27:42.720
this time and effort.

00:27:42.720 --> 00:27:48.300
Once his time in the 055 containment chamber
was over, he retired back to his office to

00:27:48.300 --> 00:27:53.640
finally digitize his exhaustive findings,
so that his supervisor, Mr. Kovach, would

00:27:53.640 --> 00:27:54.960
finally get off his back.

00:27:54.960 --> 00:27:59.160
Walter smiled, took a deep breath, and began
to type.

00:27:59.160 --> 00:28:01.440
“SCP - 059.

00:28:01.440 --> 00:28:02.460
Keter Class.

00:28:02.460 --> 00:28:07.680
This anomaly is a radioactive mineral that
emits a unique radiation known as Delta Radiation.

00:28:07.680 --> 00:28:12.180
Exposure to this radiation has caused strange
fungal growths on the infected...”

00:28:12.180 --> 00:28:15.060
Wait, what was this supposed to be about again?

00:28:15.060 --> 00:28:17.580
Oh well, it couldn’t have been that important.

00:28:17.580 --> 00:28:19.980
Does the Black Moon Howl?

00:28:19.980 --> 00:28:21.900
No. Not yet.

00:28:21.900 --> 00:28:27.960
See the boy. He was born in a time before
names; there weren’t enough humans around

00:28:27.960 --> 00:28:34.680
to need them back then. He was one of a handful
occupying a coastal village, using a tongue

00:28:34.680 --> 00:28:41.700
long since dead. They eked out a simple life
- hunting, gathering, fishing. The only thing

00:28:41.700 --> 00:28:48.060
on most of their minds was surviving to see
the next sunrise. Yes, a simple life, free

00:28:48.060 --> 00:28:49.320
of complications.

00:28:49.320 --> 00:28:51.960
Until The Hermit appeared.

00:28:51.960 --> 00:28:58.680
The Boy would remember this man for an eternity.
Haggard and thin; skin weathered by time and

00:28:58.680 --> 00:29:05.100
pain. A man that, emaciated, walking with
a long, gnarled cane that honestly looked

00:29:05.100 --> 00:29:11.160
healthier than he did, shouldn’t be alive.
Even the Boy, who had scarcely seen beyond

00:29:11.160 --> 00:29:17.880
the bounds of his village, knew that the Hermit
was unnatural. An aberration. An anomaly.

00:29:17.880 --> 00:29:24.180
He walked into the center of the village,
sat down on a large stone, and waited. Nobody

00:29:24.180 --> 00:29:28.020
dared ask his business, nor what the Hermit
waited for.

00:29:28.020 --> 00:29:32.640
Then, a few days later, the Black Moon howled.

00:29:32.640 --> 00:29:37.680
The Boy saw the village’s youngest hunter
freeze one evening while out on a walk. Not

00:29:37.680 --> 00:29:44.820
simply stand still, but freeze. Then, for
an instant, he became solid black. A coal

00:29:44.820 --> 00:29:51.240
statue. And as soon as he’d changed, he
was gone. Obliterated. Not a trace of him

00:29:51.240 --> 00:29:52.080
remained.

00:29:52.080 --> 00:29:58.320
Such is the power of the Black Moon. It can
make any conscious being disappear in an instant.

00:29:58.320 --> 00:30:04.860
Turned black, then wiped from our plane of
existence, never to be seen again. Its choice

00:30:04.860 --> 00:30:10.440
of victim seemed, at each instance, to be
utterly random, but it would come for all

00:30:10.440 --> 00:30:16.080
who lived eventually. This is known to some
as the howling of the Black Moon.

00:30:16.080 --> 00:30:22.140
Later that same night, the Boy found himself
talking to the Hermit, who asked with small,

00:30:22.140 --> 00:30:28.140
frantic eyes what he had seen. When the Boy
told him, he let out a deep, rattling sigh.

00:30:28.140 --> 00:30:34.140
The Boy, curious, asked him if he knew about
the nightmare he’d just witnessed. The Hermit

00:30:34.140 --> 00:30:39.240
looked up. He’d been the first one, in the
Hermit’s millennia of pursuit, that had

00:30:39.240 --> 00:30:45.300
ever asked. In that moment, he knew he had
found his successor in the hunt for the Death

00:30:45.300 --> 00:30:46.080
of Ages.

00:30:46.080 --> 00:30:53.220
The Hermit told the Boy it went by many names.
The Great Finale, the Pale King, but most

00:30:53.220 --> 00:30:59.700
common of all was the Black Moon. The entity
existed beyond the veil of our reality, a

00:30:59.700 --> 00:31:05.760
creature of pure energy, though nobody could
really be sure of its true nature. The Hermit

00:31:05.760 --> 00:31:11.340
had been tracking it, learning about it, and
trying to destroy it for thousands of years.

00:31:11.340 --> 00:31:17.100
And yet, it only took him four pathetic minutes
to tell the Boy everything he knew.

00:31:17.100 --> 00:31:22.440
The Boy, knowing still that something about
the Hermit was unnatural, asked how he came

00:31:22.440 --> 00:31:29.280
to be in this position. The Hermit told the
boy he was the Counterbalance, a kind of chosen

00:31:29.280 --> 00:31:34.980
one, destined to face and perhaps even defeat
the Black Moon someday. The Counterbalance

00:31:34.980 --> 00:31:40.440
receives a number of truly extraordinary gifts
for inheriting the responsibility: Eternal

00:31:40.440 --> 00:31:44.400
life, eternal youth, near physical immortality.

00:31:44.400 --> 00:31:50.580
But they will be haunted by their purpose,
doomed to watch everyone they love die around

00:31:50.580 --> 00:31:57.300
them, as they continue to hunt their only
true equal and opposite, the Black Moon itself.

00:31:57.300 --> 00:32:03.240
The Hermit, in his own eyes, had failed at
his duty. He had grown weary, and now, he

00:32:03.240 --> 00:32:08.820
needed to pass the duty of Counterbalance
onto another. That other would be the Boy.

00:32:08.820 --> 00:32:13.800
He felt a sudden and profound change, along
with the knowledge that nothing would ever

00:32:13.800 --> 00:32:21.000
be the same again. He was no longer just the
Boy. Now, he was the Counterbalance.

00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:25.920
He watched the Hermit give him a slight nod
out of respect, and then crumble into dust

00:32:25.920 --> 00:32:32.460
before his eyes. The Boy, the Counterbalance,
looked up at the sky and saw the stars twinkling.

00:32:32.460 --> 00:32:39.000
So bright, so beautiful. Little did he know,
his battle with the Black Moon would outlast

00:32:39.000 --> 00:32:40.680
every single one of them.

00:32:40.680 --> 00:32:44.880
Does the Black Moon howl? Not without blood.

00:32:44.880 --> 00:32:51.300
The Boy grew into a man, as his village aged
and then died around him. Decades passed,

00:32:51.300 --> 00:32:57.840
then centuries, then millennia. Tens of thousands
of years, watching humanity develop and grow

00:32:57.840 --> 00:33:02.160
around him as he continued his pursuit of
that one elusive foe.

00:33:02.160 --> 00:33:07.320
As science and diagnostic technology gained
ground, absorbing and then evolving beyond

00:33:07.320 --> 00:33:12.180
all the old superstitions, the Counterbalance
gained a better understanding of the Black

00:33:12.180 --> 00:33:18.960
Moon - though even then, it still remained
essentially a stranger. The entity was entropic,

00:33:18.960 --> 00:33:25.200
a being of pure randomness and chaos without
consistent form. It didn’t exist in our

00:33:25.200 --> 00:33:30.540
universe, but it could exercise its influence
here with so-called “Obliteration Events”

00:33:30.540 --> 00:33:34.920
- much like the horrible fate that befell
the young hunter from the village.

00:33:34.920 --> 00:33:38.820
But that was only the proverbial tip of the
iceberg.

00:33:38.820 --> 00:33:44.940
The Counterbalance tracked and noted obliteration
events. They were exceedingly rare, at first.

00:33:44.940 --> 00:33:50.580
Something that occurred once every thousand
years or so, like a terrible curse. But he

00:33:50.580 --> 00:33:52.620
couldn’t help but notice a concerning trend&nbsp;

00:33:52.620 --> 00:33:56.040
emerging. It started happening&nbsp;
once a century...then

00:33:56.040 --> 00:34:01.200
once a decade. He could feel the terrible
future stretching out in front of him. How,

00:34:01.200 --> 00:34:06.480
over their shared eternity, the Black Moon
would gain more and more ground.

00:34:06.480 --> 00:34:13.080
Would there come a day where it took someone
once a year? One a month? A week, a day, an

00:34:13.080 --> 00:34:19.740
hour, a minute, a second? It’d spell the
end of all conscious life. A total victory

00:34:19.740 --> 00:34:27.120
for the Black Moon, the End of the Universe,
the Death of Ages. A complete existential

00:34:27.120 --> 00:34:28.200
obliteration.

00:34:28.200 --> 00:34:32.940
He was swept up in a sobering realization:
He couldn’t win this fight alone.

00:34:32.940 --> 00:34:38.340
However, while his hunt for the Black Moon
had been largely fruitless, the Counterbalance

00:34:38.340 --> 00:34:44.340
had discovered many other things along the
way, Strange creatures, objects with extraordinary

00:34:44.340 --> 00:34:49.980
powers, and events that couldn’t be explained
with rational science. Perhaps something among

00:34:49.980 --> 00:34:57.480
these oddities, these anomalies, would hold
the key to defeating his timeless enemy. And

00:34:57.480 --> 00:35:03.120
it hadn’t just been these objects, entities,
and events, he’d also discovered some truly

00:35:03.120 --> 00:35:08.940
exceptional people on his travels. Minds and
skills that rivaled even his own, despite

00:35:08.940 --> 00:35:09.660
his age.

00:35:09.660 --> 00:35:12.660
Perhaps they would be the ones to help him
win.

00:35:12.660 --> 00:35:17.640
With the thirteen most brilliant and trusted
people the Counterbalance ever met, he decided

00:35:17.640 --> 00:35:23.820
to form a Council. And from this Council,
they forged and directed an organization dedicated

00:35:23.820 --> 00:35:29.520
to understanding and counteracting the strange
in all its forms, with the secret hope that

00:35:29.520 --> 00:35:34.080
their search into darkness would yield the
answer to the Black Moon’s downfall.

00:35:34.080 --> 00:35:40.800
He called it the SCP Foundation. They would
Secure the anomalous, Contain it, and Protect

00:35:40.800 --> 00:35:43.980
all of humanity from its&nbsp;
influence. The Counterbalance&nbsp;

00:35:43.980 --> 00:35:46.980
also took on a new title, befitting of his

00:35:46.980 --> 00:35:53.040
new role: The Administrator. And even the
Black Moon itself was given a moniker, in

00:35:53.040 --> 00:35:55.800
hopes of robbing it of some of its frightening
power.

00:35:55.800 --> 00:35:58.620
SCP-001.

00:35:58.620 --> 00:36:03.000
Does the Black Moon howl? Only at the blind.

00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:09.540
The year was now 1987. The SCP Foundation
had been operating for over a century, and

00:36:09.540 --> 00:36:14.220
thanks to their secret possession of anomalous
wisdom and technology, their own advancement

00:36:14.220 --> 00:36:18.840
was thousands of years ahead of the rest of
humanity. While there still wasn’t a silver

00:36:18.840 --> 00:36:23.820
bullet solution to the Black Moon, and its
deadly howls were becoming all the more frequent

00:36:23.820 --> 00:36:28.920
as the decades went on, the Foundation did
have some irons in the fire to combat it.

00:36:28.920 --> 00:36:34.020
Their ability to gather intel on both the
entity itself and its obliteration events

00:36:34.020 --> 00:36:39.600
had improved considerably, thanks to their
new global information network. Their top

00:36:39.600 --> 00:36:44.760
minds were also working on a highly classified
device known as the Singular Conceptual Bunker,

00:36:44.760 --> 00:36:50.640
which may one day come in handy for combating
the extra-dimensional entity directly. But

00:36:50.640 --> 00:36:55.080
the most valuable piece of information they
ever gathered about the Black Moon was this:

00:36:55.080 --> 00:37:01.920
It couldn’t howl when it was being watched.
The very act of engaged observation defanged

00:37:01.920 --> 00:37:02.160
it.

00:37:02.160 --> 00:37:07.620
The problem is, how can you observe something
that doesn’t technically exist inside your

00:37:07.620 --> 00:37:13.080
own reality? In order to pull this off, the
Foundation would need to get extremely creative.

00:37:13.080 --> 00:37:18.240
Thankfully, creative solutions to strange
problems are the Foundation’s specialty.

00:37:18.240 --> 00:37:25.440
Flash forward to 1993. Enter Dr. Moto, a brilliant
young scientist and conceptual engineer working

00:37:25.440 --> 00:37:30.840
for the SCP Foundation. With The Administrator’s
consultation, he started the KEY Project,

00:37:30.840 --> 00:37:37.020
an arm of the wider Project Oromasdes - the
umbrella initiative for using modified anomalous

00:37:37.020 --> 00:37:39.420
objects in the battle against the Black Moon.

00:37:39.420 --> 00:37:44.580
The goal of the KEY Project was relatively
simple: If people couldn’t observe the Black

00:37:44.580 --> 00:37:49.620
Moon directly, then the Foundation could make
proxies of the Black Moon that could be observed,

00:37:49.620 --> 00:37:55.260
almost like a kind of voodoo doll. These new
anomalies would only need to satisfy three

00:37:55.260 --> 00:38:01.320
criteria: The inability to operate when being
observed, a hostility to conscious life, and

00:38:01.320 --> 00:38:06.180
the ability to end conscious life of their
own volition when not being observed. Through

00:38:06.180 --> 00:38:11.280
conceptual engineering, a link theoretically
could be forged between these objects and

00:38:11.280 --> 00:38:15.960
the Black Moon, allowing observation of them
to stop the obliteration events.

00:38:15.960 --> 00:38:21.240
However, despite being a good idea in theory,
Dr. Moto’s efforts were marred with errors

00:38:21.240 --> 00:38:26.040
and tragedies. One object wasn’t deadly
enough, simply appearing behind people in

00:38:26.040 --> 00:38:30.300
a threatening pose when they weren’t looking.
Another one killed purely through collateral

00:38:30.300 --> 00:38:34.920
damage - a giant sculpture of a human head
that immediately attempted escape by barging

00:38:34.920 --> 00:38:40.800
through Site-01 - the center for Anti-Black
Moon operations - and killing nineteen people

00:38:40.800 --> 00:38:46.800
in the process. Another one of Moto’s objects,
a huge black sphere, simply immediately exploded,

00:38:46.800 --> 00:38:48.120
killing twelve people.

00:38:48.120 --> 00:38:53.640
And in the most horrific misstep of all, one
of Moto’s objects caused a mass death event

00:38:53.640 --> 00:38:58.140
in a nearby hotel, where 142&nbsp;
people were spontaneously&nbsp;

00:38:58.140 --> 00:39:00.900
incinerated when the object - a series of

00:39:00.900 --> 00:39:07.320
interlocking stalactites and stalagmites - was
left unobserved for 0.2 seconds. Almost all

00:39:07.320 --> 00:39:12.000
of Moto’s objects were terminated in the
aftermath, either being too useless or too

00:39:12.000 --> 00:39:17.040
dangerous to keep around. The young scientist
felt a deep shame, but forged on.

00:39:17.040 --> 00:39:23.700
He made one truly brilliant creation that
satisfied all the criteria: A sculpture, incapable

00:39:23.700 --> 00:39:28.320
of moving while being watched, but would snap
the neck of the nearest conscious entity if

00:39:28.320 --> 00:39:33.360
left unobserved for even a fraction of a second.
Its relatively minimal killing left it easy

00:39:33.360 --> 00:39:38.460
to contain without causing mass deaths, and
despite all the other deaths that had sadly

00:39:38.460 --> 00:39:43.320
occurred during the KEY Project, Dr. Moto
believed that the lives saved in the long

00:39:43.320 --> 00:39:47.220
run by stopping the Black Moon’s howls would
justify the sacrifice.

00:39:47.220 --> 00:39:51.720
The problem is...the KEY Project didn’t
stop anything.

00:39:51.720 --> 00:39:57.240
Not long after this, there was the first recorded
double obliteration event in Rome, where a

00:39:57.240 --> 00:40:02.340
young tourist couple had both been obliterated
simultaneously. All the deaths in the KEY

00:40:02.340 --> 00:40:07.260
Project had been for nothing. The Black Moon
was only getting more powerful.

00:40:07.260 --> 00:40:12.420
The shame and the guilt was too much for Dr.
Moto. He left a note in his office, reading,

00:40:12.420 --> 00:40:17.220
“We've been looking at nothing. I'm sorry,
Administrator. I've failed you, sir.”

00:40:17.220 --> 00:40:22.980
Moto’s corpse was later found in the sculpture’s
temporary containment chamber, his neck snapped.

00:40:22.980 --> 00:40:28.320
The KEY Project was, in summary, shut down
and its one surviving creation transported

00:40:28.320 --> 00:40:36.900
to Site-19 in late 1993, where it was designated
as SCP-173. Another painful failure for the

00:40:36.900 --> 00:40:39.900
Administrator. Back to the drawing board once
more.

00:40:39.900 --> 00:40:44.100
Does the Black Moon howl? Not while stars
shine.

00:40:44.100 --> 00:40:49.440
millennia stretched on. Almost everyone died,
except The Administrator, thanks to his gift

00:40:49.440 --> 00:40:55.800
- or perhaps curse - as the Counterbalance
to the Black Moon. Science marched on, the

00:40:55.800 --> 00:40:59.100
SCP Foundation marched on, but all this progress,&nbsp;

00:40:59.100 --> 00:41:02.940
all this power, was nothing&nbsp;
against the incomprehensible

00:41:02.940 --> 00:41:09.780
influence of SCP-001. The Black Moon was howling
more frequently than ever, all the way up

00:41:09.780 --> 00:41:15.420
to the year 3156, when the Foundation launched
the SEEK Project under the support of Project

00:41:15.420 --> 00:41:16.440
Oromasdes.

00:41:16.440 --> 00:41:21.480
As more and more people were wiped out in
frequent obliteration events, the Administrator

00:41:21.480 --> 00:41:26.340
became painfully aware that perhaps the answers
to the Black Moon problem wouldn’t be found

00:41:26.340 --> 00:41:31.500
on earth. Using state of the art technology,
with a little help from the anomalous, the

00:41:31.500 --> 00:41:36.420
SCP Foundation began work on an autonomous
space-faring vessel that could search the

00:41:36.420 --> 00:41:43.500
stars for the key to the Black Moon’s destruction.
It was an awe-inspiring creation, a huge craft

00:41:43.500 --> 00:41:49.200
powered by artificial intelligence, with a
universal translator, cryogenic units, and

00:41:49.200 --> 00:41:52.680
hundreds of autonomous drones to perform more
targeted searches.

00:41:52.680 --> 00:41:58.140
SEEK was waved off into the unforgiving depths
of space. The Administrator could only hope

00:41:58.140 --> 00:42:00.720
that it would come back with worthwhile answers.

00:42:00.720 --> 00:42:05.760
The first of the three notable planets SEEK
arrived on was one theoretically capable of

00:42:05.760 --> 00:42:11.640
supporting human life, except for its brutal
and constant blizzards and snowstorms. When

00:42:11.640 --> 00:42:16.740
SEEK’s drones were deployed, they did discover
signs of civilization, based around sentient

00:42:16.740 --> 00:42:22.500
spherical creatures, but no signs of actual
life remained. Records and statues found across

00:42:22.500 --> 00:42:26.460
the planet seemed to indicate that the Black
Moon was responsible for the destruction of

00:42:26.460 --> 00:42:31.260
the planet’s civilization, causing so many
obliteration events that the remaining survivors

00:42:31.260 --> 00:42:37.020
went mad from the fear and stress, leading
to mass death in the ensuing chaos.

00:42:37.020 --> 00:42:42.960
The next planet was discovered centuries later,
in the year 3499. While this planet could

00:42:42.960 --> 00:42:47.460
also theoretically support human life, it
suffered from frequent volcanic eruptions

00:42:47.460 --> 00:42:52.320
that rendered much of its surface a flaming
mess. However, there were still the dormant

00:42:52.320 --> 00:42:57.900
ruins of a once advanced civilization of conscious
beings. Much like the prior planet, they’d

00:42:57.900 --> 00:43:03.060
been driven extinct by Black Moon obliteration
events a century before the SEEK even arrived.

00:43:03.060 --> 00:43:08.400
Unlike the last planet, however, it seems
that they accepted their fate, and went gently

00:43:08.400 --> 00:43:13.440
into the night. The planet was now overrun
by billions of armored, bat-like creatures

00:43:13.440 --> 00:43:18.540
that operated on pure instinct, and thus,
were not considered conscious enough to be

00:43:18.540 --> 00:43:19.140
obliterated.

00:43:19.140 --> 00:43:25.620
The final planet was reached in 3764, and
was the most fruitful of the three discoveries.

00:43:25.620 --> 00:43:31.380
This planet was hyper-advanced, fully urbanized
and covered in sprawling megacities, with

00:43:31.380 --> 00:43:36.000
records and technology over a thousand years
ahead of Earth. Before the Black Moon killed

00:43:36.000 --> 00:43:41.040
almost all of them, they were a species of
humanoid telepathic fungi, and had developed

00:43:41.040 --> 00:43:45.060
an awareness of the Black Moon’s existence
that was on par with that of humanity’s.

00:43:45.060 --> 00:43:47.580
They even had their own equivalent of the&nbsp;

00:43:47.580 --> 00:43:50.580
SCP Foundation actively&nbsp;
working on countermeasures.

00:43:50.580 --> 00:43:56.100
And most amazingly of all, SEEK found one
surviving member of the species on the planet,

00:43:56.100 --> 00:44:01.320
cryogenically frozen. The craft was immediately
instructed to collect the survivor and return

00:44:01.320 --> 00:44:06.000
home for interrogation. The Administrator
was preparing for what could have been the

00:44:06.000 --> 00:44:10.980
most important conversation since he met the
Hermit, all those thousands of years ago.

00:44:10.980 --> 00:44:15.180
Does the Black Moon howl? Only when waning.

00:44:15.180 --> 00:44:20.520
When the surviving creature, codenamed SAGE,
was returned to Earth, The Administrator was

00:44:20.520 --> 00:44:26.040
eager to finally speak with it. Like the rest
of its now-extinct species, SAGE spoke through

00:44:26.040 --> 00:44:30.780
powerful telepathic mindwaves, which only
The Administrator - thanks to his Counterbalance

00:44:30.780 --> 00:44:34.680
abilities - was able to receive at close range
without being harmed.

00:44:34.680 --> 00:44:39.540
Incidentally, it wasn’t long until the very
fact of the Administrator’s nature as a

00:44:39.540 --> 00:44:45.300
Counterbalance came up in the mental conversation.
SAGE could tell, just by being in his presence.

00:44:45.300 --> 00:44:50.400
They discovered a number of vital truths over
their brief time communicating: That SAGE’s

00:44:50.400 --> 00:44:54.960
survival had been pure luck, for starters.
The Black Moon is still very much capable

00:44:54.960 --> 00:45:00.540
of obliterating conscious beings in an unconscious
state. The Administrator also learned that

00:45:00.540 --> 00:45:06.060
he was merely the latest in an extremely long
line of Counterbalances across time, space,

00:45:06.060 --> 00:45:11.580
and species, though everyone but him had waived
the duty, passed it on.

00:45:11.580 --> 00:45:19.200
SAGE had one question to ask the Administrator
in turn, “What is SCB?” The Singular Conceptual

00:45:19.200 --> 00:45:24.000
Bunker, being worked on and perfected for
thousands of years by now, by the Foundation’s

00:45:24.000 --> 00:45:26.520
top scientists and conceptual engineers.

00:45:26.520 --> 00:45:30.000
The Administrator replied, “Victory. But&nbsp;

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:33.840
it will take a very, very&nbsp;
long time.” Specifically,

00:45:33.840 --> 00:45:39.900
so long that he would see the stars go out
around him, one by one. Shocked, SAGE asked

00:45:39.900 --> 00:45:44.940
him what good victory would do him then. Rather
than say it aloud, he replied with a thought.

00:45:44.940 --> 00:45:50.580
SAGE paused, and said, “I see. How blasphemous
of you. Hopefully it works.”

00:45:50.580 --> 00:45:55.260
After this, the Administrator proceeded to
the Singular Conceptual Bunker and entered

00:45:55.260 --> 00:46:00.780
it, leaving instructions for the Foundation
to be run by a newly formed O5 Council in

00:46:00.780 --> 00:46:07.080
his indefinite absence. Thousands of years
later, in the year 5011, SAGE spoke one more

00:46:07.080 --> 00:46:13.620
time, repeating the words, “Hopefully, hopefully”
before turning solid black, and disappearing.

00:46:13.620 --> 00:46:19.500
The Black Moon had claimed one more victim,
but billions more had gone in the interim.

00:46:19.500 --> 00:46:25.380
The Administrator had no more answers to give.
At least, no more answers that anyone but

00:46:25.380 --> 00:46:31.080
him would understand. He was inside the Singular
Conceptual Bunker now, loaded into a device

00:46:31.080 --> 00:46:37.260
known as TOME - an experimental memorial module,
meant to pick up and record all the last messages

00:46:37.260 --> 00:46:43.740
of every dying civilization across the universe,
when the time finally came. All he could do

00:46:43.740 --> 00:46:47.460
was wait. And wait was exactly what we did.

00:46:47.460 --> 00:46:49.860
Does the Black Moon howl?

00:46:49.860 --> 00:46:52.020
Yes. Yes it does.

00:46:52.020 --> 00:46:58.560
Years pass. Too many to count. It’s a time
after names now, and TOME sits in the very

00:46:58.560 --> 00:47:03.720
center, drinking in the end of the universe.
The last of all the human colonies across

00:47:03.720 --> 00:47:10.740
the universe were obliterated by the Black
Moon back in the year 7329, so, so, so long

00:47:10.740 --> 00:47:17.280
ago, but some of the final messages of fear,
panic, and distress still echoed around the

00:47:17.280 --> 00:47:18.600
Administrator’s mind.

00:47:18.600 --> 00:47:24.600
"Hello, is there anyone here? We — we require
assistance! There's … it's … it's taking

00:47:24.600 --> 00:47:29.940
people every day! We need help! There's barely
anyone left! We need help! Hello? Hello?!"

00:47:29.940 --> 00:47:35.940
"Cabal 09:43! We have abandoned the false
flesh! We have abandoned the false flesh!

00:47:35.940 --> 00:47:43.740
The shepherds crook broken 'neath my knee!
Cabal 09:43! Cabal 09:43! Forgive us! Forgive

00:47:43.740 --> 00:47:43.980
us!"

00:47:43.980 --> 00:47:49.350
"We're going to leave this on. It's so dark
outside now. It's blotting out the sun. It's

00:47:49.350 --> 00:47:50.760
… I have to go now."

00:47:52.560 --> 00:47:56.940
"RESPOND•FIRST•CONVENIENCE&nbsp;
EMERGENCY•SITUATION•DEVELOPING&nbsp;

00:47:56.940 --> 00:47:59.460
REQUIRE•ADDITIONAL•RESOURCES."

00:47:59.460 --> 00:48:04.961
"My fault. Your fault. Our fault. My fault.
Your fault. Our fault. My fault. Your fault.

00:48:04.961 --> 00:48:07.560
Our fault. Rip out my brain now. Rip out my
brain now!"

00:48:07.560 --> 00:48:15.120
And a small child, the last on Earth, simply
asking, “Hello?” into an indifferent microphone.

00:48:15.120 --> 00:48:21.420
But the Administrator had to wait, as the
Singular Conceptual Bunker became the Solitary

00:48:21.420 --> 00:48:27.120
Conceptual Bunker. He was the last conscious
being in the universe, and still, he needed

00:48:27.120 --> 00:48:33.420
to wait, as the stars went dark outside. Only
when there was nothing outside but black was

00:48:33.420 --> 00:48:37.200
it finally time for the Counterbalance’s
long game to pay off.

00:48:37.200 --> 00:48:43.200
There was nothing left of our universe. The
only thing here was the SCB, and the Black

00:48:43.200 --> 00:48:49.020
Moon itself. With everything else gone, the
Black Moon only had one conscious being left

00:48:49.020 --> 00:48:54.240
to obliterate. It opened the door to the Solitary
Conceptual Bunker, and stepped inside.

00:48:54.240 --> 00:49:01.440
This...this doesn’t make sense. How can
the Black Moon, an entity beyond our dimension,

00:49:01.440 --> 00:49:08.340
beyond physical form, take a step? Good question.
The same question, incidentally, that was

00:49:08.340 --> 00:49:12.780
going through the Black Moon’s mind as it
entered the bunker. It didn’t look at all

00:49:12.780 --> 00:49:18.840
how the entity expected: It was like a bar,
a counter with rows of bottles behind it,

00:49:18.840 --> 00:49:24.000
a jukebox playing in the corner. A man stood
behind the bar, cleaning glasses.

00:49:24.000 --> 00:49:27.600
The Counterbalance. The Administrator.

00:49:27.600 --> 00:49:33.180
He said, "Well, there you are! Certainly took
your time. Can I pour you a little something?"

00:49:33.180 --> 00:49:39.840
This only served to increase the Black Moon’s
confusion. It had form here, dark smoke compressed

00:49:39.840 --> 00:49:47.160
into a vaguely humanoid shape. It could speak?
It could think? None of this made any sense.

00:49:47.160 --> 00:49:52.080
The being that’d just wiped out all conscious
life and seen the very death of the universe

00:49:52.080 --> 00:49:55.080
was truly and utterly confused.

00:49:55.080 --> 00:50:00.240
The Administrator just seemed to be enjoying
himself, preparing for a confrontation hundreds

00:50:00.240 --> 00:50:05.760
of billions of years in the making. The Singular
Conceptual Bunker - or perhaps, the Singular

00:50:05.760 --> 00:50:12.540
Containment Bunker - was a truly ingenious
creation. A place of pure ideas, where everything

00:50:12.540 --> 00:50:20.400
inside was on the same level. Here, there
were no immortals. No Gods. Just ideas, on

00:50:20.400 --> 00:50:26.520
the same level playing field. And it was time
for the Black Moon’s idea to come to an

00:50:26.520 --> 00:50:26.700
end.

00:50:26.700 --> 00:50:30.780
It was a trap, and the entire universe was
the bait.

00:50:30.780 --> 00:50:34.980
Without warning, the Administrator pulled
up a shotgun from underneath the table, and

00:50:34.980 --> 00:50:37.680
unleashed both barrels into the Black Moon’s
chest.

00:50:37.680 --> 00:50:41.760
The creature took the hit and fought back,
dragging the Administrator to the ground,

00:50:41.760 --> 00:50:47.040
beating him, strangling him. He could feel
the light fading under the monster’s relentless

00:50:47.040 --> 00:50:52.320
assault, until he managed to get his desperate
hands on a glass ashtray. He beat the monster

00:50:52.320 --> 00:50:56.400
over the head with it until its grip loosened,
and he was able to slide out.

00:50:56.400 --> 00:51:00.840
There, the killer of the universe was on the
ground before him. He grabbed the monster,

00:51:00.840 --> 00:51:06.780
held it in place, and beat it to death. He
was gravely injured by the battle, but The

00:51:06.780 --> 00:51:12.960
Black Moon was no more. Here, in the Singular
Conceptual Bunker, he had won.

00:51:12.960 --> 00:51:17.940
The Administrator, no longer the counterbalance
in the absence of the Black Moon, hobbled

00:51:17.940 --> 00:51:23.640
over to the jukebox, producing a single, beautiful
coin from his pocket. He pushed the coin into

00:51:23.640 --> 00:51:26.520
the slot, wheezed a pained breath, and said:

00:51:26.520 --> 00:51:35.160
“The thing is … this place is only information.
T-There's nothing else out there. Not even

00:51:35.160 --> 00:51:40.920
matter. The universe closed its doors a long
time ago. But this place can go from information

00:51:40.920 --> 00:51:47.640
back to matter with just the press of a button.
L-Let's see what happens when we introduce

00:51:47.640 --> 00:51:49.140
something to nothing…”

00:51:49.140 --> 00:51:54.660
For a second, it looks as though he might
fall, but he doesn’t. Instead, he slams

00:51:54.660 --> 00:52:00.000
the button on the jukebox and, with a relieved
laugh, says, “Let there be light.”

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:02.460
And there was light.

00:52:02.460 --> 00:52:08.580
The fabric of our world is littered with doorways&nbsp;
if you know where to look for them. Tears,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:08.580 --> 00:52:16.020
portals, anomalies, all leading to places and&nbsp;
planes beyond human imagining and understanding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:16.020 --> 00:52:22.800
and SCP-2317, otherwise known as A Door to&nbsp;
Another World, certainly fits that description.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:23.460 --> 00:52:29.700
Contained and kept at all times under the watch&nbsp;
of armed guards, SCP-2317 appears to be a simple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:29.700 --> 00:52:34.980
and unsuspecting wooden door in its frame.&nbsp;
It hardly looks like it requires such extreme&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:34.980 --> 00:52:40.320
round-the-clock security or needs a strange,&nbsp;
secretive ritual that the Foundation performs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:40.320 --> 00:52:46.380
presumably to keep the door closed. But, of&nbsp;
course, sometimes the most interesting thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:46.380 --> 00:52:50.820
about a closed doorway isn’t where&nbsp;
it leads, it’s what it keeps out.&nbsp;

00:52:51.840 --> 00:52:57.540
Even by the Foundation’s already-high standards,&nbsp;
the requirements and regulations for personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:57.540 --> 00:53:04.500
who are assigned to SCP-2317 seem oddly specific.&nbsp;
Psychological testing is standard practice for to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:04.500 --> 00:53:09.120
work for the Foundation, but an additional&nbsp;
hurdle that anyone has to clear before even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:09.120 --> 00:53:13.980
getting to glimpse at this unassuming wooden&nbsp;
door is having a score of at least seventy-two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:13.980 --> 00:53:20.040
on the Milgram Obedience Examination. It is also&nbsp;
mandatory that personnel assigned to maintaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:20.040 --> 00:53:25.200
it are both unmarried, with no children&nbsp;
or next-of-kin, as well as an unwavering,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:25.200 --> 00:53:30.900
unquestioning loyalty to the Foundation,&nbsp;
pure devotion to its code and objectives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:31.740 --> 00:53:38.760
These may seem like strange requirements,&nbsp;
after all, SCP-2317 is just a door…isn’t it?&nbsp;

00:53:39.780 --> 00:53:45.060
Perhaps there’s a reason that the Foundation&nbsp;
keeps so much of the information about SCP-2317&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:45.060 --> 00:53:50.940
buried deep under layers upon layers of security,&nbsp;
with only the Overseer Council privy to the full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:50.940 --> 00:53:58.320
details of its strange nature. Knowledge, as they&nbsp;
say, is power - but maybe knowing too much about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:58.320 --> 00:54:05.580
whatever is behind that door can prove deadly.&nbsp;
Still, if SCP-2317 is a Door to Another World,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:05.580 --> 00:54:11.520
an alternate dimension or parallel reality,&nbsp;
it must be safe enough to visit. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:11.520 --> 00:54:16.380
the Foundation has been sending personnel&nbsp;
in there on a regular basis. Daily, in fact.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:17.340 --> 00:54:21.420
According to the O5 Council, this&nbsp;
is done as part of a procedure to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:21.420 --> 00:54:27.360
maintain Active Containment of…something&nbsp;
lurking beyond that old wooden doorframe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:28.020 --> 00:54:31.380
But what could possibly warrant such&nbsp;
constant maintenance and surveillance?&nbsp;

00:54:33.060 --> 00:54:37.860
In accordance with the Foundation’s guidelines,&nbsp;
all staff are required to rotate out of observing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:37.860 --> 00:54:43.800
SCP-2317 after every two months and spend the&nbsp;
following third month in full psychological&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:43.800 --> 00:54:48.600
counselling before they are permitted to return to&nbsp;
the containment unit housing the Door to Another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:48.600 --> 00:54:54.000
World. It was after one of these month-long&nbsp;
periods of evaluation that a Foundation guard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:54.000 --> 00:54:58.680
was informed that his security clearance&nbsp;
had been raised to Level 3 and that he’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:58.680 --> 00:55:03.660
been selected for the duty of carrying out&nbsp;
220-Calabasas. He knew the name instantly;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:04.320 --> 00:55:09.420
this was the title given to the daily containment&nbsp;
procedure that absolutely had to be carried out.&nbsp;

00:55:10.440 --> 00:55:14.880
The guard didn’t question these orders, after&nbsp;
all, he’d been selected precisely because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:14.880 --> 00:55:19.920
his loyalty to the Foundation. He did make one&nbsp;
request to his commanding officer, however:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:20.520 --> 00:55:24.300
he wanted to know what had happened to the&nbsp;
last guard that had performed the procedure.&nbsp;

00:55:25.200 --> 00:55:29.340
“Didn’t make it out of psychological&nbsp;
evaluation,” the officer replied.&nbsp;

00:55:30.240 --> 00:55:35.700
Not letting this affect his dedication, the guard&nbsp;
was told to prepare for Procedure 220-Calabasas.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:36.300 --> 00:55:41.400
Along with a fellow member of Foundation security&nbsp;
personnel, the guard was instructed to gather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:41.400 --> 00:55:47.340
everything on a strange list. The first was&nbsp;
a pre-selected member of Class-D Personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:47.340 --> 00:55:52.440
specifically a convicted murderer. Class-D&nbsp;
refers to ‘Disposable Class’ personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:52.980 --> 00:55:58.080
expendable individuals recruited by the&nbsp;
Foundation for the sole purpose of testing SCPs.&nbsp;

00:55:59.100 --> 00:56:04.260
Class-Ds were usually prison inmates&nbsp;
repurposed for SCP testing, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:04.260 --> 00:56:09.780
one chosen for 220-Calabasas was no exception,&nbsp;
serving multiple life sentences for murders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:09.780 --> 00:56:13.620
or at least that was what the guard&nbsp;
had been told. A Foundation personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:13.620 --> 00:56:18.000
member instructed him to refer to the Class-D&nbsp;
solely as the ‘assistant’ from that point on.&nbsp;

00:56:18.720 --> 00:56:22.620
Next, the guard collected a live&nbsp;
chicken, an obsidian-edged knife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:22.620 --> 00:56:28.620
a silver aspergillum and aspersorium, to be&nbsp;
filled with 500ccs of Holy Water that had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:28.620 --> 00:56:34.920
been blessed by a priest of the Abrahamic faith,&nbsp;
and finally a one-kiloton nuclear device, which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:34.920 --> 00:56:39.120
according to instructions, was to only&nbsp;
be detonated in the unlikely event of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:39.120 --> 00:56:42.900
catastrophic containment failure.&nbsp;
In other words, the last resort.&nbsp;

00:56:44.520 --> 00:56:49.680
After following his instructions to the letter and&nbsp;
without question, the guard and his colleague were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:49.680 --> 00:56:54.240
briefed. The Foundation personnel member informed&nbsp;
them that he’d be joining and leading them in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:54.240 --> 00:56:59.400
procedure. The staff member also specified that&nbsp;
henceforth he be referred to as the ‘celebrant’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:59.400 --> 00:57:05.100
until the completion of 220-Calabasas. The&nbsp;
guard was acutely aware of how specific these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:05.100 --> 00:57:10.140
instructions were, but trusted in the Foundation,&nbsp;
knowing that if they wanted this procedure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:10.140 --> 00:57:14.880
performed a certain way, then it was in everyones’&nbsp;
best interest to carry out the orders to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:14.880 --> 00:57:21.840
letter. But what the celebrant then went on to&nbsp;
explain, raised far more questions about SCP-2317&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:21.840 --> 00:57:29.940
and the nature of Procedure 220-Calabasas. The&nbsp;
Class-D joining them, wasn’t actually a Class-D.&nbsp;

00:57:30.600 --> 00:57:35.400
The assistant, as they were now referred to,&nbsp;
was in reality another Foundation staff member,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:35.400 --> 00:57:42.600
with a Level 4 security clearance, specifically&nbsp;
tailored to SCP-2317. Every member of staff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:42.600 --> 00:57:49.200
entering through SCP-2317 and taking an active&nbsp;
role in 220-Calabasas needed to be informed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:49.200 --> 00:57:54.780
this assistant was not to be harmed or treated&nbsp;
as a member of Disposable Class. Fighting back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:54.780 --> 00:58:00.120
the nagging question of why the Foundation would&nbsp;
employ this subterfuge, the guard, along with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:00.120 --> 00:58:04.980
his fellow security officer, the celebrant and&nbsp;
assistant, prepared for their departure through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:04.980 --> 00:58:13.020
the Door to Another World at solar noon, when&nbsp;
the sun was highest over SCP-2317. Solar noon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:13.020 --> 00:58:18.840
chickens and holy water, this all seemed like&nbsp;
an oddly-occult combination for the Foundation.&nbsp;

00:58:19.740 --> 00:58:24.540
As they entered the old wooden door, beyond&nbsp;
lay a barren salt plane, stretching out for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:24.540 --> 00:58:29.760
kilometers in every direction. This alternate&nbsp;
dimension, according to the briefing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:29.760 --> 00:58:36.000
was designated SCP-2317-Prime. The guard&nbsp;
immediately noticed a ring of seven pillars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:36.000 --> 00:58:41.280
directly ahead of the group as they entered, each&nbsp;
of them bearing intricately-detailed engravings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:41.280 --> 00:58:48.000
unlike anything from any era of ancient history.
Procedure 220-Calabasas was carried out quickly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:48.000 --> 00:58:53.280
but carefully, the guard watching as the celebrant&nbsp;
and assistant were careful not to miss a step.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:54.180 --> 00:58:57.720
First, the celebrant scattered Holy Water&nbsp;
into the center of the pillars with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:57.720 --> 00:59:02.940
aspergillum and aspersorium, looking down&nbsp;
at his feet and keeping a steady pace as he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:02.940 --> 00:59:08.280
stepped counter-clockwise around them. The guard&nbsp;
watched intently as the celebrant completed his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:08.280 --> 00:59:13.200
circuit around the pillars and turned to the&nbsp;
assistant, anointing his head with Holy Water.&nbsp;

00:59:13.860 --> 00:59:20.760
“Seven Seals, Seven Rings, Seven Thrones&nbsp;
for the Scarlet King,” he said aloud.&nbsp;

00:59:21.600 --> 00:59:25.800
The assistant, with the obsidian blade in&nbsp;
his hand, took the chicken and dispatched it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:25.800 --> 00:59:31.680
in sacrifice, letting its blood mix with the&nbsp;
Holy Water. He then repeated the celebrant’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:31.680 --> 00:59:35.580
circuit in the opposite direction, before&nbsp;
stepping into the center of the stone pillars.&nbsp;

00:59:36.420 --> 00:59:42.720
“Blood for the Old Gods, Water for the New King,”&nbsp;
the assistant recited, pouring the remaining mix&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:42.720 --> 00:59:46.860
of blood and Holy Water over a patch of&nbsp;
salt in the middle of the seven pillars.&nbsp;

00:59:47.820 --> 00:59:52.740
Even though he knew it wasn’t his place to&nbsp;
question the Foundation, as the 220-Calabasas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:52.740 --> 00:59:57.600
procedure took place, the guard couldn’t&nbsp;
help but wonder what all this was for.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:58.320 --> 01:00:05.160
It seemed so…ritualistic, like something&nbsp;
deeply religious or even magical. He’d never&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:05.160 --> 01:00:08.940
bought into all that occult mumbo-jumbo,&nbsp;
even while working for the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:08.940 --> 01:00:15.120
but he had learned not to question anything, even&nbsp;
the strangest and most inexplicable of sights.&nbsp;

01:00:16.260 --> 01:00:23.940
Little did he know that beneath his feet, was an&nbsp;
ancient and unknowable horror. A beast, chained&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:23.940 --> 01:00:29.940
and lying in wait. Contained in a chamber directly&nbsp;
underneath the pillars, sat an impossibly-large&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:29.940 --> 01:00:35.880
creature. Humanoid and obese, its body covered&nbsp;
entirely in scales thicker than armour plating.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:36.480 --> 01:00:41.640
Branch-like horns protruded from its jawless&nbsp;
head, pointing up to chains that hung from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:41.640 --> 01:00:48.480
seven pillars above, each one hooked into the&nbsp;
entity’s back. All but one of the chains was&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:48.480 --> 01:00:54.420
broken, a final, withering shackle keeping the&nbsp;
Devourer of Worlds in its underground prison.&nbsp;

01:00:55.260 --> 01:01:01.740
Ever since 1894 BCE, when Erikeshan mystics&nbsp;
imprisoned it, the Devourer has been waiting&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:01.740 --> 01:01:07.140
patiently for its inevitable freedom. It knows,&nbsp;
as well as the Foundation, that nothing can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:07.140 --> 01:01:13.440
done to prevent the final chain from one day&nbsp;
breaking. Even Procedure 220-Calabasas won’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:13.440 --> 01:01:19.440
keep the creature contained, it’s nothing more&nbsp;
than a smokescreen, an act, designed to create&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:19.440 --> 01:01:25.020
an illusion of active containment and maintain&nbsp;
Foundation morale until a permanent solution&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:25.020 --> 01:01:33.780
can be devised to keep SCP-2317 imprisoned.
Of course, if the guard had known this, it would&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:33.780 --> 01:01:38.340
have also explained the need for a one-kiloton&nbsp;
nuclear device as part of this staged ritual.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:39.060 --> 01:01:44.580
Procedure 220-Calabasas has all the components&nbsp;
to trick everyone below the O5 Council,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:44.580 --> 01:01:49.680
emulating religious and occult rituals, the&nbsp;
increased level of security surrounding the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:49.680 --> 01:01:55.380
procedure and its purpose, and telling staff&nbsp;
that any failure to correctly, and completely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:55.380 --> 01:02:02.400
perform the 220-Calabasas procedure will result&nbsp;
in an XK-Class End of the World Scenario.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:03.300 --> 01:02:08.580
All these elements work together to conceal&nbsp;
the truth: that one day, the Devourer will&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:08.580 --> 01:02:15.780
escape and lay waste to our dimension.
Knowledge is power, and maybe knowing too&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:15.780 --> 01:02:21.480
much truly is deadly. Perhaps if the guard had&nbsp;
learned any of this, he’d have understood why&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:21.480 --> 01:02:26.880
his predecessor never made it out of psychological&nbsp;
evaluation. Maybe if he had questioned the purpose&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:26.880 --> 01:02:34.260
of Procedure 220-Calabasas, he'd have learned the&nbsp;
true nature of SCP-2317, and what that doorway&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:34.260 --> 01:02:40.800
kept out. But he was loyal to the Foundation,&nbsp;
through and through. As the team finished&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:40.800 --> 01:02:46.500
performing 220-Calabasas and returned though the&nbsp;
wooden door, the guard took one last glance over&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:46.500 --> 01:02:53.940
his shoulder at the vast salt plane. The entire&nbsp;
dimension was calm, silent, but not peaceful:&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:53.940 --> 01:03:00.720
it was patient. The entity had waited centuries&nbsp;
for its time, and now all it would take was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:00.720 --> 01:03:08.160
breaking of the seventh and final chain. One day.
The door was closed behind the guard as he,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:08.160 --> 01:03:12.780
the celebrant, the assistant and his fellow&nbsp;
security officer stepped back through,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:13.800 --> 01:03:19.200
their work done and, as far as they knew,&nbsp;
preventing catastrophe for another day.&nbsp;

01:03:20.160 --> 01:03:25.320
Only the Foundation higher-ups, the Overseer&nbsp;
Council, are aware of the true danger posed&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:25.320 --> 01:03:32.520
by SCP-2317 and its sole inhabitant. Current&nbsp;
predictions are that at some point within the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:32.520 --> 01:03:38.580
next thirty years, the Devourer of Worlds will&nbsp;
be freed. Any and all attempts to repair or&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:38.580 --> 01:03:45.360
recreate the chains holding it in place have so&nbsp;
far failed. As such, the O5 Council has elected&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:45.360 --> 01:03:51.180
to continue providing Foundation personnel with&nbsp;
the ignorant hope that Procedure 220-Calabasas&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:51.180 --> 01:03:57.720
is an effective strategy for containment.
As we’ve said, sometimes the most interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:57.720 --> 01:04:04.980
thing about a closed door isn’t where it leads,&nbsp;
it’s what it keeps out. In the case of SCP-2317,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:04.980 --> 01:04:09.840
the unassuming wooden door holds at bay&nbsp;
an ancient creature of untold power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:10.500 --> 01:04:16.920
that will one day break free and wreak havoc in&nbsp;
our dimension. Nothing the Foundation does can&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:16.920 --> 01:04:22.560
prevent it, or keep it contained behind the&nbsp;
Door to Another World, and only the Overseer&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:22.560 --> 01:04:28.860
Council knows that any and all efforts to&nbsp;
do so are futile. With all that in mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:28.860 --> 01:04:37.020
we can only hope that the doorway of SCP-2317&nbsp;
stays closed, at least for a little while longer.

01:04:37.800 --> 01:04:43.800
It was July of 2004, and Bill Murray was enjoying
the peak of an extremely successful career.

01:04:44.400 --> 01:04:49.080
Not only had the iconic actor starred in some
of the most beloved comedies of the 20th Century,

01:04:49.080 --> 01:04:51.600
including Ghostbusters and Groundhog Day,&nbsp;

01:04:51.600 --> 01:04:54.540
he’d voiced the main character&nbsp;
of the recently-released

01:04:54.540 --> 01:04:56.160
live action Garfield movie.

01:04:56.160 --> 01:04:59.700
It’d been a financial success, but it was
a critical flop.

01:04:59.700 --> 01:05:04.800
Not that this bothered Bill – he was happy
with the performance... and the paycheck.

01:05:04.800 --> 01:05:10.260
What he wouldn’t be quite as happy about
was the horrifying encounter he was about

01:05:10.260 --> 01:05:13.920
to have with SCP – 3166.

01:05:15.060 --> 01:05:19.740
On July 8th, Bill was enjoying a cold drink
on the porch of his luxurious Beverly Hills

01:05:19.740 --> 01:05:20.040
home.

01:05:20.040 --> 01:05:23.460
The sky was beginning to darken as the sun
set in the west.

01:05:23.460 --> 01:05:25.140
It was a blissful evening.

01:05:25.140 --> 01:05:28.140
His wife, Jennifer, was inside, watching TV.

01:05:28.140 --> 01:05:33.660
Nothing seemed particularly out of the ordinary,
until he noticed a quick flash of orange in

01:05:33.660 --> 01:05:34.020
the distance.

01:05:34.020 --> 01:05:39.660
It was almost too fast to register, this large,
orange shape darting past the corner of his

01:05:39.660 --> 01:05:39.840
eye.

01:05:39.840 --> 01:05:44.160
For a second, he entertained the thought that
it might have been an escaped tiger, but it

01:05:44.160 --> 01:05:46.020
was gone too fast to really tell.

01:05:46.020 --> 01:05:48.240
Bill finished his drink and headed inside.

01:05:48.240 --> 01:05:50.160
He’d had enough for one night.

01:05:50.160 --> 01:05:55.140
The next morning, he got up to read the paper,
and found the Garfield movie getting slaughtered

01:05:55.140 --> 01:05:55.800
by the critics.

01:05:55.800 --> 01:06:01.380
One review stated “no one can accuse Garfield:
The Movie of infidelity to its source: It

01:06:01.380 --> 01:06:06.240
faithfully conveys the banality of Jim Davis's
cartoon” Another called it“a film without

01:06:06.240 --> 01:06:07.800
energy and without spirit.”

01:06:07.800 --> 01:06:10.380
He put the paper down and ate his breakfast.

01:06:10.380 --> 01:06:15.780
A few blows to the ego were worth it for the
paydays that came with big budget family films.

01:06:15.780 --> 01:06:20.760
Just then his wife came to him with a strange
question: Were you walking around downstairs

01:06:20.760 --> 01:06:22.020
in the middle of the night?

01:06:22.020 --> 01:06:25.200
No, he hadn’t, he’d been sleeping like
a baby.

01:06:25.200 --> 01:06:26.700
Why did she ask?

01:06:26.700 --> 01:06:27.480
“Well…”

01:06:27.480 --> 01:06:28.680
Jennifer said.

01:06:28.680 --> 01:06:31.020
“I heard some rustling downstairs last night.

01:06:31.020 --> 01:06:32.880
It sounded like something big.”

01:06:33.480 --> 01:06:37.440
He hadn’t heard anything though and told
her it was probably just her imagination.

01:06:37.440 --> 01:06:40.680
He put it out of his mind and continued about
his day.

01:06:40.680 --> 01:06:44.520
He decided he would keep his eyes peeled for
that orange blur again though.

01:06:44.520 --> 01:06:49.560
Bill didn’t see anything peculiar the rest
of the morning and went to a local café for

01:06:49.560 --> 01:06:49.800
lunch.

01:06:49.800 --> 01:06:54.480
He ordered a coffee and a cream cheese bagel,
then made a quick trip to the bathroom while

01:06:54.480 --> 01:06:55.560
his food was prepared.

01:06:55.560 --> 01:06:59.160
When Bill returned to his table though, he
was something strange.

01:06:59.700 --> 01:07:04.260
Instead of a bagel, there was a large heaping
of lasagna on the table.

01:07:04.260 --> 01:07:05.580
What was going on?

01:07:05.580 --> 01:07:07.680
This café didn’t even serve lasagna.

01:07:07.680 --> 01:07:10.800
Bill knew something was terribly wrong.

01:07:10.800 --> 01:07:16.620
Things only got stranger when Bill came home
to find a small tuft of orange fur snagged

01:07:16.620 --> 01:07:18.000
on the frame of his front door.

01:07:18.000 --> 01:07:22.260
And it wasn’t synthetic fur like you see
on plush toys or stuffed animals.

01:07:22.260 --> 01:07:25.800
No, this was real animal fur.

01:07:25.800 --> 01:07:31.440
Maybe someone was just goofing off or trying
to play some weird prank on him, but it didn’t

01:07:31.440 --> 01:07:32.160
feel like it.

01:07:32.760 --> 01:07:36.300
Deep down, Bill Murray knew that he was in
grave danger.

01:07:36.300 --> 01:07:42.240
Whoever, or whatever, was behind this… it
wanted to hurt him.

01:07:42.240 --> 01:07:45.300
That night, his worst fears were realized.

01:07:45.300 --> 01:07:49.080
Bill’s wife had left town for the week and
he was heading to the kitchen in the middle

01:07:49.080 --> 01:07:53.880
of the night for a glass of water, when he
saw something - A huge figure moving up against

01:07:53.880 --> 01:07:55.920
the glass door leading to his backyard.

01:07:55.920 --> 01:08:02.280
The thing was huge, nearly seven feet tall,
with a bloated, fur-covered, misshapen body

01:08:02.280 --> 01:08:04.320
that was pressed up against the door.

01:08:04.320 --> 01:08:09.360
Its fur was bright, garish orange – a cartoon
orange.

01:08:10.260 --> 01:08:12.960
Strangest of all though was the sound it was
making.

01:08:13.740 --> 01:08:16.080
It sounded like it was purring.

01:08:16.080 --> 01:08:19.860
Bill backed away from the door and then ran
back to his room to hide.

01:08:19.860 --> 01:08:24.960
The whole night, he sat cowering as he heard
scratching against the walls, like something

01:08:24.960 --> 01:08:26.400
was trying to get in.

01:08:26.400 --> 01:08:30.240
He was terrified and too scared to do anything,
even move.

01:08:30.240 --> 01:08:33.960
Finally, as morning broke, the noises seemed
to stop.

01:08:33.960 --> 01:08:35.400
Bill had to do something.

01:08:35.400 --> 01:08:38.040
He couldn’t let this nightmare go on another
night.

01:08:38.040 --> 01:08:39.540
What if things got worse?

01:08:39.540 --> 01:08:42.360
What if that thing managed to get inside?

01:08:43.320 --> 01:08:48.060
He called the local police and when they arrived,
he explained the incredibly strange situation

01:08:48.060 --> 01:08:49.020
as best he could.

01:08:49.020 --> 01:08:54.000
He told them he was being stalked by some
kind of huge cat, or at least someone dressed

01:08:54.000 --> 01:08:54.840
like a huge cat.

01:08:54.840 --> 01:08:57.180
Also there was lasagna involved.

01:08:57.180 --> 01:09:01.020
The officers interviewing him could barely
contain their laughter as he told them his

01:09:01.020 --> 01:09:02.940
story.
A giant orange cat?

01:09:02.940 --> 01:09:08.220
Perhaps, one of them theorized, he’d angered
some kind of obsessive Garfield fan through

01:09:08.220 --> 01:09:10.200
his involvement in the live action movie.

01:09:10.200 --> 01:09:15.360
After all, the original comic had been running
for years and had been extremely popular.

01:09:15.360 --> 01:09:20.820
Who knows what kind of nut jobs were obsessed
with seeing only a faithful adaptation of

01:09:20.820 --> 01:09:21.780
the source material?

01:09:21.780 --> 01:09:26.700
As the officers departed, Bill was confident
that they weren’t taking him seriously.

01:09:26.700 --> 01:09:29.100
He couldn’t rely on any of them for protection.

01:09:29.100 --> 01:09:34.680
Thankfully, from a multi-decade movie career,
he had plenty of disposable income, and decided

01:09:34.680 --> 01:09:38.760
to hire a private security team to protect
him while he looked into this mystery.

01:09:38.760 --> 01:09:43.560
He had two trained bodyguards positioned around
his home at all times for the next month.

01:09:43.560 --> 01:09:47.760
They were armed, and given the cryptic orders
to fire on anything orange.

01:09:47.760 --> 01:09:51.720
Meanwhile, Bill began to fall down a Garfield
rabbit hole.

01:09:51.720 --> 01:09:57.000
He felt strangely compelled to research all
the Garfield media he could find, as though

01:09:57.000 --> 01:10:01.020
the answer to his terrifying situation was
somehow hidden between the lines.

01:10:01.020 --> 01:10:04.920
Bill explored the entire backlog of thousands
of comic strips.

01:10:04.920 --> 01:10:07.680
He read the books and interviews with Jim
Davis.

01:10:07.680 --> 01:10:11.100
He watched the cartoons and straight-to-DVD
animated movies.

01:10:11.100 --> 01:10:16.680
Ironically for a guy who’d recently portrayed
the lasagna-loving orange cat, Bill had never

01:10:16.680 --> 01:10:19.140
felt quite so immersed in the character before.

01:10:20.100 --> 01:10:25.920
He found a strange pathos in the routine of
Garfield and his friends.One particular comic

01:10:25.920 --> 01:10:27.660
really piqued his interest, though.

01:10:27.660 --> 01:10:33.360
Originally published in October of 1989, the
comic began with Garfield being woken up by

01:10:33.360 --> 01:10:35.880
a strange chill, an almost eerie sensation.

01:10:35.880 --> 01:10:39.540
The character observed aloud that he didn’t
feel like he was in his own home.

01:10:39.540 --> 01:10:44.400
He explored his little home further, trying
to find his owner Jon or his housemate and

01:10:44.400 --> 01:10:47.940
sometimes nemesis, Odie, but found nothing.

01:10:47.940 --> 01:10:53.100
As Garfield remarked on feeling alone, a purple
speech box delivered the sinister message:

01:10:54.060 --> 01:10:58.440
“You have no idea how alone you are, Garfield.”

01:10:59.220 --> 01:11:02.520
He then finds that his home looks like it’s
been abandoned for years.

01:11:03.420 --> 01:11:06.540
The “For Sale” sign outside is practically
ancient.

01:11:07.200 --> 01:11:14.100
Garfield slowly comes to a horrifying revelation:
Everyone really is gone, and his adventures

01:11:14.100 --> 01:11:16.620
and friends now exist only in his imagination.

01:11:16.620 --> 01:11:21.540
He’s trapped in a prison of his own creation,
trying to stave off his endless loneliness,

01:11:21.540 --> 01:11:24.480
in denial about the reality of his situation.

01:11:24.480 --> 01:11:30.000
The comic ended with a quote directly from
Jim Davis himself, saying “An imagination

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:31.800
is a powerful tool.

01:11:31.800 --> 01:11:34.860
It can tint memories of&nbsp;
the past, shade perceptions&nbsp;

01:11:34.860 --> 01:11:37.740
of the present, or paint a future so vivid

01:11:37.740 --> 01:11:43.680
that it can entice... or terrify, all depending
upon how we conduct ourselves today...”

01:11:43.680 --> 01:11:47.880
As he read those words, Bill Murray felt a
chill down his spine.

01:11:47.880 --> 01:11:51.420
Why had he wanted to get involved in the Garfield
movie in the first place?

01:11:51.420 --> 01:11:53.280
What had he gotten himself into?

01:11:53.280 --> 01:11:55.680
Before he could slip any deeper into his own&nbsp;

01:11:55.680 --> 01:11:59.040
mind, Bill heard a faint,&nbsp;
choked scream downstairs.

01:11:59.660 --> 01:12:02.520
He felt his breath catch in his throat.

01:12:02.520 --> 01:12:05.520
He was terrified but he needed to see what
was happening.

01:12:06.300 --> 01:12:09.900
He carefully and quietly began to creep down
the stairs.

01:12:09.900 --> 01:12:14.100
At the bottom, he poked his head around a
corner, and that’s when he saw a member

01:12:14.100 --> 01:12:16.380
of his security detail lying dead on the floor.

01:12:16.380 --> 01:12:21.600
His face was blue from asphyxiation, his mouth
was stuffed with lasagna.

01:12:22.200 --> 01:12:24.480
It looked like he had been force-fed to death.

01:12:25.680 --> 01:12:29.580
Bill wanted to scream but he couldn’t, or
maybe knew he shouldn’t.

01:12:29.580 --> 01:12:34.320
Just then he heard a soft, meaty thumping
noise coming from the nearby living room.

01:12:34.320 --> 01:12:40.560
He didn’t know why, but he felt compelled
to approach as if by forces beyond his control.

01:12:40.560 --> 01:12:46.860
He made his way to the living room, and when
he got there, he saw where the noise was coming

01:12:46.860 --> 01:12:47.220
from.

01:12:47.220 --> 01:12:50.040
Bill’s jaw dropped in pure horror.

01:12:50.040 --> 01:12:54.780
There was the other member of his security
detail, lying limp and lifeless under a giant

01:12:54.780 --> 01:12:55.560
orange figure.

01:12:55.560 --> 01:13:00.600
It was a grotesquely huge creature, wearing
what looked to be a kind of crude Garfield

01:13:00.600 --> 01:13:03.300
outfit made of sewn-together cat pelts.

01:13:03.300 --> 01:13:06.060
It stank of pasta and rotten meat.

01:13:06.060 --> 01:13:12.060
In its giant paw, it held a golden trophy,
which it was using to pound the security guard’s

01:13:12.060 --> 01:13:16.440
head into mush while making quiet, cat-like
purring noises.

01:13:16.440 --> 01:13:21.000
The creature suddenly stopped and looked up,
locking eyes with Bill.

01:13:21.000 --> 01:13:23.400
The fear of death came over him.

01:13:23.400 --> 01:13:29.820
He froze, as the giant, freakish Garfield
stepped over Donny’s corpse, and began to

01:13:29.820 --> 01:13:30.540
come towards him.

01:13:30.540 --> 01:13:33.480
Bill turned and ran, but Garfield was gaining
on him.

01:13:33.480 --> 01:13:36.780
Before he could make it to the front door,
the creature knocked him over.

01:13:36.780 --> 01:13:41.700
He was laid out on the ground, looking up
at it, as it reached into its own body cavity

01:13:41.700 --> 01:13:44.280
and began to pull out handfuls of lasagna.

01:13:44.280 --> 01:13:49.200
He was just about to shove a wad of the horrible
decaying pasta into Bill’s mouth, when suddenly,

01:13:49.200 --> 01:13:51.660
a DING was heard and the creature stopped.

01:13:51.660 --> 01:13:57.600
It looked up, as if sniffing the air, and
then suddenly turned and lumbered towards

01:13:57.600 --> 01:13:58.100
the kitchen.

01:13:59.460 --> 01:14:04.680
Bill watched as the Garfield monster entered
the kitchen where, somehow, there was a steaming

01:14:04.680 --> 01:14:07.080
hot fresh lasagna sitting in the open oven.

01:14:07.080 --> 01:14:12.420
The creature had sensed the presence of external
lasagna, and felt the compulsion to integrate

01:14:12.420 --> 01:14:16.380
it into its body, grabbing fistfulls and shoving
it into itself.

01:14:17.340 --> 01:14:20.340
Just then, a group of highly&nbsp;
trained SCP Foundation&nbsp;

01:14:20.340 --> 01:14:22.500
personnel burst into the room and subdued

01:14:22.500 --> 01:14:23.040
the creature.

01:14:23.940 --> 01:14:25.080
It had been an ambush.

01:14:25.080 --> 01:14:29.040
The Foundation had been tipped off to the
presence of the creature by monitoring the

01:14:29.040 --> 01:14:33.240
local police department dispatches, and the
report of a seven foot tall comic book cat

01:14:33.240 --> 01:14:36.840
terrorizing a Hollywood actor was definitely
worth looking into.

01:14:36.840 --> 01:14:43.920
The monster that had almost taken Bill Murray’s
life was SCP – 3166, a deadly pataphysical

01:14:43.920 --> 01:14:48.840
being that tends to manifest around people
somehow involved in the Garfield intellectual

01:14:48.840 --> 01:14:49.380
property.

01:14:49.380 --> 01:14:53.820
It appears whenever the public perception
of Garfield falls out of favor, and because

01:14:53.820 --> 01:14:58.380
Bill had starred in the critically-panned
Garfield movie, he was currently at the very

01:14:58.380 --> 01:15:01.560
top of SCP – 3166’s hit list.

01:15:02.460 --> 01:15:07.620
Thankfully, he managed to survive his terrifying
ordeal, and was administered amnestics by

01:15:07.620 --> 01:15:10.680
Foundation personnel so he could return to
his normal life.

01:15:10.680 --> 01:15:16.140
This frightening and mysterious creature has
been around since 1989, appearing after the

01:15:16.140 --> 01:15:20.040
publication of the haunting Garfield comic
that Bill had read that very night.

01:15:21.060 --> 01:15:25.320
It appeared in the office of United Media,
who were the publishers of the Garfield comic

01:15:25.320 --> 01:15:28.440
strip at the time, and began wreaking havoc.

01:15:28.440 --> 01:15:33.180
Since then, the creature’s manifestation
has been a constant threat whenever Garfield

01:15:33.180 --> 01:15:35.280
loses its popularity or audience.

01:15:35.280 --> 01:15:40.080
As a result, the Foundation has spent years
as the funding source behind all Garfield

01:15:40.080 --> 01:15:44.760
media, and even planting hypnotic memetics
into the comic strips to ensure that there

01:15:44.760 --> 01:15:46.740
is always a loyal fanbase.

01:15:47.280 --> 01:15:53.820
The fur is indeed real, organic cat fur, albeit
an unnaturally orange color, and instead of

01:15:53.820 --> 01:15:57.120
organs, the creature is filled with lasagna.

01:15:57.120 --> 01:16:02.400
Worst of all though, is that testing has revealed
that the meat in the lasagna is genetically

01:16:02.400 --> 01:16:06.240
identical to the flesh of Garfield’s creator,
Jim Davis.

01:16:06.240 --> 01:16:08.820
How did this thing come into existence?

01:16:08.820 --> 01:16:13.320
Perhaps it was Jim’s sheer force of imagination
that dragged it into being.

01:16:13.320 --> 01:16:18.300
As he himself said, “An imagination is a
powerful tool.”

01:16:18.300 --> 01:16:22.560
All in all, it’s lucky that Bill Murray
was able to survive his encounter, and return

01:16:22.560 --> 01:16:26.820
to his normal life – well, as normal as
life can be for Bill Murray.

01:16:26.820 --> 01:16:31.740
And if you see Bill Murray, don’t bother
asking him about SCP – 3166.

01:16:32.760 --> 01:16:38.820
The amnestics were quite effective, and just
as he’s fond of saying himself, no one will

01:16:38.820 --> 01:16:39.780
ever believe you.

01:16:39.780 --> 01:16:46.080
If there’s anything that recent years have sadly&nbsp;
taught us, it’s that diseases are an insidious&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:46.080 --> 01:16:51.900
and formidable enemy that can take you by&nbsp;
surprise. Whether it’s bacterial, a virus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:51.900 --> 01:16:58.200
a fungal infection, or even an unfortunate genetic&nbsp;
mutation like cancer, Alzheimer’s, or Multiple&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:58.200 --> 01:17:03.540
Sclerosis, sometimes dealing with a dangerous&nbsp;
pathogen could leave you praying for a run-in with&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:03.540 --> 01:17:10.260
SCP-682 after all, at least getting devoured&nbsp;
by a giant, evil reptile is a quick death.

01:17:10.260 --> 01:17:14.820
But take a page out of the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation’s book: Sometimes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:14.820 --> 01:17:19.980
the best response to an imminent threat is&nbsp;
containment and research. One of the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:19.980 --> 01:17:25.200
rules of combat is to know your enemy.&nbsp;
It may seem like a tall order to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:25.200 --> 01:17:30.240
to write the book on dangerous diseases, but&nbsp;
thankfully, that book has already been written:&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:30.240 --> 01:17:38.100
it’s SCP-1025 The Encyclopedia of Common Diseases.&nbsp;
This handy, reader-friendly volume will tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:38.100 --> 01:17:42.240
you everything you need to know about all the&nbsp;
common maladies you may find yourself facing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:42.240 --> 01:17:49.740
and a whole lot more. From the sniffles to lung&nbsp;
cancer, from a cold sore to necrotizing fasciitis.

01:17:49.740 --> 01:17:54.540
You may be thinking, “Why would I need some&nbsp;
dusty old book to tell me about diseases? I&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:54.540 --> 01:18:00.000
can always just go to WebMD.” But you don’t want&nbsp;
that. You know what the internet is like: They’ll&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:04.200
just tell you you’re sick, and you don’t want&nbsp;
them putting silly ideas in your head like that.

01:18:04.200 --> 01:18:10.500
How about you open up to a random page and we’ll&nbsp;
take a look. There, see? The Common Cold. Classic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:10.500 --> 01:18:15.840
Let’s see the description: “The Common Cold is a&nbsp;
virus that affects the upper respiratory tract.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:15.840 --> 01:18:21.180
Its duration is typically a maximum of two weeks,&nbsp;
and its primary symptoms include headaches, muscle&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:21.180 --> 01:18:27.000
aches, a cough, a runny nose, raised temperature,&nbsp;
pressure in the ears or face, and a loss of taste&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:27.000 --> 01:18:31.920
or smell.” See? Simple, straightforward,&nbsp;
and objective. Exactly what you need.&nbsp;

01:18:32.880 --> 01:18:39.060
Did you just cough? That’s strange. Hmm, and come&nbsp;
to think of it, your nose is looking a little red.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:39.060 --> 01:18:45.360
Do you need a tissue? Or perhaps a throat lozenge?&nbsp;
Your voice seems a little hoarse. Perhaps you&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:45.360 --> 01:18:50.220
ought to take a break and lay down. You really&nbsp;
don’t look so good. Seems like the common cold&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:50.220 --> 01:18:54.720
to us. Thankfully, you shouldn’t have to&nbsp;
worry about it for more than two weeks. Oh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:54.720 --> 01:19:00.660
and that reminds me: There is a certain anomalous&nbsp;
effect to the Encyclopedia of Common Diseases.

01:19:00.660 --> 01:19:06.420
Whenever you read about a pathogen in the&nbsp;
Encyclopedia of Common Diseases, you catch it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:06.420 --> 01:19:12.540
manifesting even its most severe symptoms in&nbsp;
an extremely brief period of time. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:12.540 --> 01:19:15.840
this isn’t that much of a problem if&nbsp;
you just read the article about having&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:15.840 --> 01:19:20.640
a sore throat or a stomach bug, but what&nbsp;
if you read the page for Ebola? Suddenly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:20.640 --> 01:19:25.260
you’re half-dead and bleeding from the&nbsp;
eyes. Or the Bubonic Plague? Or a disease&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:25.260 --> 01:19:31.260
that humanity has never even faced before?&nbsp;
And what if, worst of all, the people who&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:31.260 --> 01:19:36.540
catch the diseases from this book continue to&nbsp;
be contagious to others? It could be the basis&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:36.540 --> 01:19:42.600
for a world-destroying biological weapon and at&nbsp;
the very least, a bonafide Keter-Class anomaly.

01:19:42.600 --> 01:19:47.280
When the SCP Foundation got their hands on&nbsp;
this little hardcover anomalous nightmare,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:47.280 --> 01:19:51.000
the researchers handling this thing&nbsp;
realized it needed to be kept under&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:51.000 --> 01:19:55.740
lock and key. A new provisional site was&nbsp;
created just to contain and research it&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:55.740 --> 01:20:00.180
without the risk of its anomalous effects&nbsp;
starting an unstoppable global pandemic.

01:20:00.180 --> 01:20:04.440
The base was an isolated underground&nbsp;
bunker, containing an even more&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:04.440 --> 01:20:09.360
high-security containment unit to store the&nbsp;
book itself: A vault surrounded by at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:09.360 --> 01:20:15.000
ten armed guards at any given time, rotated&nbsp;
twice weekly and checked for any infectious&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:15.000 --> 01:20:20.580
agents. There was even a powerful thermite bomb
stored beneath the vault, set to go off and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:20.580 --> 01:20:25.560
annihilate the entire chamber if the plausible&nbsp;
risk of a containment breach was detected.

01:20:25.560 --> 01:20:31.500
It may seem insane to put in this many security&nbsp;
fail-safes for a simple anomalous book, but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:31.500 --> 01:20:38.340
SCP Foundation has dealt with dangerous books&nbsp;
before. Take SCP-140, also known as an Incomplete&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:38.340 --> 01:20:43.200
Chronicle. This dangerous historical volume&nbsp;
chronicles the living history of the Daevites,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:43.200 --> 01:20:48.120
an extinct culture of sadistic sorcerers&nbsp;
closely tied to the mythos of the Scarlet&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:48.120 --> 01:20:53.760
King. Whenever ink or blood is brought into the&nbsp;
presence of this book, it absorbs the material,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:53.760 --> 01:20:59.340
expanding the Daevite’s history and bringing their&nbsp;
terrifying rule ever closer to the modern day.

01:20:59.340 --> 01:21:06.360
Or take SCP-3512, “The More You Know: A Pick-Up&nbsp;
Artist’s Bible”, a deadly instruction manual made&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:06.360 --> 01:21:11.640
by a mind-controlling group of interest known&nbsp;
as the Fifthists. This book gave its sinister&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:11.640 --> 01:21:16.980
practitioners the tools to control the minds of&nbsp;
their potential romantic partners, often leading&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:16.980 --> 01:21:24.300
to their deaths. While it may not be quite as&nbsp;
apocalyptic as SCP-1025 or SCP-140, the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:24.300 --> 01:21:30.480
that there are so many in circulation still makes&nbsp;
it a dangerous threat. Point is, a book can be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:30.480 --> 01:21:37.560
dangerous thing, especially if its pages have the&nbsp;
potential to unlock deadly diseases like SCP-1025.

01:21:37.560 --> 01:21:43.500
As you can expect with an infectious Keter-Class&nbsp;
anomaly of this magnitude, procedures around this&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:43.500 --> 01:21:49.200
one were rigorous. The site staff was a skeleton&nbsp;
crew, observing strict quarantine procedures to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:49.200 --> 01:21:54.240
prevent any potential infection from leaking out&nbsp;
into the wider world. Research into the history&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:54.240 --> 01:21:59.640
of the book was inconclusive, despite a bevy of&nbsp;
Foundation resources being poured into finding&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:59.640 --> 01:22:06.120
any worthwhile leads on the author or publisher&nbsp;
of the book. Nothing. It was an absolute mystery&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:06.120 --> 01:22:12.540
who or what had put this XK-Class End of the World&nbsp;
Scenario waiting to happen here on earth. But now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:12.540 --> 01:22:18.120
it was the job of these intrepid researchers to&nbsp;
discover the full extent of its potential dangers.

01:22:18.120 --> 01:22:22.740
27 D-Class subjects were allocated&nbsp;
to the base for testing. By the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:22.740 --> 01:22:27.180
the process was over, none of these&nbsp;
unlucky prisoners would remain alive.

01:22:27.180 --> 01:22:32.160
The tests started much like this video: The&nbsp;
Researchers forced a D-Class to read the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:32.160 --> 01:22:37.620
section on the Common Cold. Within two hours,&nbsp;
the subject began coughing. Upon being asked,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:37.620 --> 01:22:41.760
they also reported feeling physically achey,&nbsp;
though they attributed the ache to sleeping on&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:41.760 --> 01:22:46.200
an uncomfortable D-Class cot every night.&nbsp;
The researchers were concerned already:&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:46.200 --> 01:22:51.240
The incubation period for the common cold -&nbsp;
meaning the period a person is infected before&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:51.240 --> 01:22:56.880
showing active symptoms - can be as long&nbsp;
as three days. Two hours is unprecedented.

01:22:56.880 --> 01:23:02.940
Next, a D-Class was told to read the section on&nbsp;
Chicken Pox, a common childhood malady that can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:02.940 --> 01:23:08.520
considerably more dangerous in adulthood. Within&nbsp;
an hour of being exposed, the D-Class repeatedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:08.520 --> 01:23:13.380
scratched no less than five points on her body&nbsp;
repeatedly. While she claimed this was because&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:13.380 --> 01:23:19.980
of the itchy D-Class jumpsuits, it was too eerily&nbsp;
close to a symptom of Chicken Pox to be ignored.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:19.980 --> 01:23:24.960
The medical history of this D-Class also showed&nbsp;
that she’d suffered Chicken Pox in childhood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:24.960 --> 01:23:30.660
suggesting that SCP-1025 infections have&nbsp;
the power to override previous immunities.

01:23:30.660 --> 01:23:35.880
Next, things got a little more serious:&nbsp;
They tested the section on lung cancer&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:35.880 --> 01:23:40.080
on a D-Class with no family history&nbsp;
of lung conditions. Not long after,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:40.080 --> 01:23:46.140
the researchers noted that the D-Class coughed&nbsp;
an unusual number of times. Not only that, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:46.140 --> 01:23:51.000
picked up irregularities in the D-Class’ breathing&nbsp;
that appeared to be characteristic of lung cancer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:51.000 --> 01:23:56.100
While the D-Class did not report any feelings&nbsp;
of chest pain or discomfort, the researchers&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:56.100 --> 01:24:02.160
had him terminated and dissected. No tumors were&nbsp;
found. A researcher noted that they didn’t wait&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:02.160 --> 01:24:08.100
long enough for proper tumor manifestation -&nbsp;
They knew they heard that D-Class coughing.

01:24:08.100 --> 01:24:11.820
The researchers were so concerned&nbsp;
by the results of the previous test,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:11.820 --> 01:24:17.160
they repeated it exactly with another D-Class,&nbsp;
who they then observed over a period of seven&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:17.160 --> 01:24:22.560
days to track tumor manifestation. Researchers&nbsp;
made a note of an unusual amount of coughing&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:22.560 --> 01:24:28.200
and wheezing from the subject over this period&nbsp;
of time. The D-Class was then terminated and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:28.200 --> 01:24:35.280
dissected - But surprise, surprise, no tumors.&nbsp;
Researchers began to consider the frightening&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:35.280 --> 01:24:41.100
possibility that signs of SCP-1025-induced&nbsp;
illness disappear after the victims die,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:41.100 --> 01:24:49.020
meaning that a pandemic started by SCP-1025 would&nbsp;
be impossible to properly track and respond to.

01:24:49.020 --> 01:24:54.240
Things were only getting scarier and&nbsp;
scarier for the SCP-1025 researchers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:54.240 --> 01:24:58.260
sequestered away in that&nbsp;
isolated Foundation bunker.

01:24:58.260 --> 01:25:03.240
Researchers continued to delve further into the&nbsp;
lung cancer rabbit hole: This time, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:03.240 --> 01:25:07.140
they didn’t wait for the subject to die&nbsp;
before looking at their insides. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:07.140 --> 01:25:10.980
instead performed a vivisection on the&nbsp;
subject, only to find that despite the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:10.980 --> 01:25:14.820
victim still being alive and displaying&nbsp;
some of the key symptoms of lung cancer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:14.820 --> 01:25:21.000
there were no tumors. What could this mean?&nbsp;
These diseases weren’t behaving like any of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:21.000 --> 01:25:26.160
non-anomalous counterparts. What other differences&nbsp;
could we be dealing with here? Infectious lung&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:26.160 --> 01:25:30.960
cancer? And what if there are more books out&nbsp;
there, like time bombs, just waiting to go off?

01:25:30.960 --> 01:25:37.680
The tests continued, getting more isolated&nbsp;
and more intense. In the end, the SCP-1025&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:37.680 --> 01:25:43.800
site was staffed by only three researchers and&nbsp;
two agents acting as guards. D-Classes were sent&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:43.800 --> 01:25:49.140
in one by one to minimize ration requirements.&nbsp;
It seemed they could have been dealing with one&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:49.140 --> 01:25:53.760
of the most dangerous anomalies of all time&nbsp;
- even working with it could be a trigger&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:53.760 --> 01:25:59.220
for the apocalypse, if the proper containment&nbsp;
and quarantine procedures weren’t observed.

01:25:59.220 --> 01:26:03.360
Things got so out of hand that a D-Class&nbsp;
without an appendix was told to read the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:03.360 --> 01:26:08.040
section on Appendicitis, and researchers&nbsp;
still observed him exhibiting symptoms of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:08.040 --> 01:26:13.500
the condition. He was vivisected, and while the&nbsp;
appendix was still not present, the organs in&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:13.500 --> 01:26:19.200
the area where the appendix would have been seemed&nbsp;
redder than usual. Where would this nightmare end?

01:26:19.200 --> 01:26:24.420
Well, it would actually end much sooner than&nbsp;
anyone involved would anticipate. Despite never&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:24.420 --> 01:26:30.900
even reading SCP-1025 himself, a researcher&nbsp;
developed a strange persistent cough and was&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:30.900 --> 01:26:36.000
quarantined in a containment chamber by his&nbsp;
concerned colleagues. On the seventh day of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:36.000 --> 01:26:43.200
his confinement, he seemed to be slightly taller&nbsp;
than before - a symptom of SCP-016, a deadly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:43.200 --> 01:26:47.700
anomalous blood-borne pathogen that multiplies&nbsp;
wildly and rewrites the genetic structure of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:47.700 --> 01:26:53.940
its host if placed into a high-stress situation.&nbsp;
This led to a number of terrifying revelations:&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:53.940 --> 01:26:58.800
Not only did the book have the potential&nbsp;
to inflict a number of anomalous diseases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:58.800 --> 01:27:05.160
but it could also potentially do so by pure&nbsp;
proximity, even if you don’t actually read it.

01:27:05.160 --> 01:27:10.140
What other anomalous diseases could be&nbsp;
on the table now? What about SCP-008,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:10.140 --> 01:27:18.720
a terrifying prion with both 100% virality and&nbsp;
100% lethality? Or SCP-742, a retrovirus that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:18.720 --> 01:27:24.060
slowly but surely transforms its victims&nbsp;
into cannibalistic monsters? Or even the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:24.060 --> 01:27:30.660
horrifying SCP-217, the disease that slowly&nbsp;
converts your entire body into a mechanical&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:30.660 --> 01:27:36.120
nightmare? There would be no limit to&nbsp;
the horrors SCP-1025 could unleash on&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:36.120 --> 01:27:42.180
the world if ever it got out. They needed&nbsp;
to keep this thing locked up at any cost.

01:27:42.180 --> 01:27:47.220
That’s when the infected researcher&nbsp;
escaped, and all hell broke loose.

01:27:47.220 --> 01:27:53.040
The isolated facility went dark for 72 hours.&nbsp;
After not being able to get into contact with&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:53.040 --> 01:27:57.900
any other Foundation bases during that time,&nbsp;
a recovery team was sent to investigate the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:57.900 --> 01:28:02.040
mystery. One agent and one researcher&nbsp;
were found in the observation booth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:02.040 --> 01:28:06.960
wearing biological containment suits. Another&nbsp;
agent was found crawling through the air ducts&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:06.960 --> 01:28:12.420
with his handgun drawn, a crazed look in his&nbsp;
eye. An additional researcher had locked himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:12.420 --> 01:28:17.700
in the barracks with a homemade flamethrower,&nbsp;
paranoid about infection. And the final agent&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:17.700 --> 01:28:23.340
was found dead in a storage locker with some&nbsp;
empty bottles and ration packages, after having&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:23.340 --> 01:28:29.040
given the door an airtight seal to prevent&nbsp;
infection - then dying of suffocation inside.

01:28:29.040 --> 01:28:36.300
The O5 Council shuttered the entire investigation.&nbsp;
SCP-1025 was downgraded from Keter to Safe Class,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:36.300 --> 01:28:41.640
then placed in a storage locker. The&nbsp;
whole thing was considered a wash. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:41.640 --> 01:28:46.080
know what you’re probably wondering: Why!?&nbsp;
If this anomaly was so incredibly dangerous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:46.080 --> 01:28:50.940
why on earth would the O5 Council and the rest&nbsp;
of the Foundation be dealing with it so casually?

01:28:50.940 --> 01:28:56.760
Well, that’s simple: The initial batch of&nbsp;
researchers had grievously misjudged the actual&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:56.760 --> 01:29:04.140
anomalous effect of SCP-1025. It doesn’t give&nbsp;
diseases to those who read its text - instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:04.140 --> 01:29:09.660
it induces a form of “hypochondria by proxy”&nbsp;
to those around the reader. In other words,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:09.660 --> 01:29:15.900
while SCP-1025 has no effect on the reader, it&nbsp;
makes everyone around them merely believe that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:15.900 --> 01:29:21.180
they’ve come down with a terrible illness. The&nbsp;
few members of staff in that isolated site had&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:21.180 --> 01:29:27.180
been killing and dissecting D-Classes for no&nbsp;
reason. In effect, they’d all effectively gone&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:27.180 --> 01:29:34.560
mad due to the anomalous effects of SCP-1025 and&nbsp;
the paranoia induced by pressure and isolation.

01:29:34.560 --> 01:29:39.300
Much like your average hypochondriac,&nbsp;
they’d warped the data to fit the worst&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:39.300 --> 01:29:44.880
possible outcome rather than the more mundane&nbsp;
and likely. As an old medical expression goes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:44.880 --> 01:29:50.160
“When you see hoofprints, think&nbsp;
horses, not zebras.” The entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:50.160 --> 01:29:54.840
thing had been a terrifying waste&nbsp;
of time, money, and human life.

01:29:54.840 --> 01:29:59.940
So perhaps, in the end, the Encyclopedia&nbsp;
of Common Diseases is a lot more like WebMD&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:59.940 --> 01:30:04.680
than we thought. It’s not nearly as useful as&nbsp;
getting a consultation with an actual doctor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:04.680 --> 01:30:10.980
and of course, it’s liable to put some&nbsp;
very strange ideas in your head...

01:30:10.980 --> 01:30:14.460
There is something so captivating about ice.

01:30:14.460 --> 01:30:21.180
It can be beautiful, a shimmering cast of
frost over a meadow or twinkling icicles on

01:30:21.180 --> 01:30:22.140
a cottage roof.

01:30:22.140 --> 01:30:28.440
It can also be deadly: A slick of slippery
glass on a dark road, or that same icicle

01:30:28.440 --> 01:30:32.820
from before, knocked loose and careening toward
your head like a falling dagger.

01:30:32.820 --> 01:30:38.100
It can be a sleet storm or a mighty glacier
with secrets buried beneath its core.

01:30:38.100 --> 01:30:44.760
In a remote part of Alaska, the SCP Foundation
discovered a particularly unusual kind of

01:30:44.760 --> 01:30:50.040
ice, with a vivid red hue and some incredibly
deadly potential.

01:30:50.040 --> 01:30:56.040
The Foundation investigated reports in a remote
area on the Alaskan coastline after a tribe

01:30:56.040 --> 01:31:01.440
of local natives came across the mangled bodies
of shipwrecked hunters in the area, encased

01:31:01.440 --> 01:31:03.240
in a block of strange red ice.

01:31:03.240 --> 01:31:09.420
Mobile Task Force Beta-7, also known as The
Haz-Matters, was sent in to the site to determine

01:31:09.420 --> 01:31:14.280
what exactly had occurred and take samples
of any anomalous materials to be brought back

01:31:14.280 --> 01:31:16.500
to the nearest Foundation research site.

01:31:16.500 --> 01:31:21.600
Agent Bryce made the initial visual inspection
of the site and spotted three middle-aged

01:31:21.600 --> 01:31:22.320
male bodies.

01:31:22.320 --> 01:31:27.600
Further examination determined that one of
the bodies, referred to as Subject Zero, was

01:31:27.600 --> 01:31:33.240
the original point of contamination for whatever
comprised the red ice and caused the men’s

01:31:33.240 --> 01:31:33.840
deaths.

01:31:33.840 --> 01:31:38.580
It has been posited by the investigative team
that the other men were infected when they

01:31:38.580 --> 01:31:40.980
attempted to help Subject Zero reach their
boat.

01:31:40.980 --> 01:31:44.760
Sadly, kindness can sometimes be a killer
like that.

01:31:44.760 --> 01:31:49.740
While sweeping the perimeter, Agent Hewes
spotted human footprints leading to the Northeast.

01:31:49.740 --> 01:31:55.020
A three-man team consisting of Agents Hewes,
Whitmore, and Cassidy was permitted to follow

01:31:55.020 --> 01:32:01.260
those tracks and determine if any survivors,
or something worse, had escaped the site.

01:32:01.260 --> 01:32:07.920
Exploration Log A009 1 allows us to determine
what happened next, and what the three agents

01:32:07.920 --> 01:32:08.280
found.

01:32:08.280 --> 01:32:13.200
Hewes and his team followed the footprints
to the entrance of a cave, with the tracks

01:32:13.200 --> 01:32:14.400
appearing to lead inside.

01:32:14.400 --> 01:32:19.680
The entrance of the cave was covered with
an almost solid sheet of ice, save for a crack

01:32:19.680 --> 01:32:21.600
in the ice about one meter tall.

01:32:21.600 --> 01:32:27.780
Beyond this wall, Agent Whitmore spotted the
body of a young man, frozen solid in the midst

01:32:27.780 --> 01:32:32.340
of crawling away from something, covered in
crystals of red ice.

01:32:32.340 --> 01:32:37.560
With him was a frozen spear gun that appeared
to have been fired just before the young man’s

01:32:37.560 --> 01:32:37.740
death.

01:32:37.740 --> 01:32:42.180
They could not touch the body to perform a
full investigation, but the way in which he

01:32:42.180 --> 01:32:46.260
was gripping his chest indicated he might
have been fatally stabbed there.

01:32:46.260 --> 01:32:51.840
As the agents moved further into the cave,
they discovered a chamber about 5 or 6 meters

01:32:51.840 --> 01:32:54.900
in diameter, filled with red ice with a pool
in the middle.

01:32:54.900 --> 01:32:58.500
The pool was three meters wide and of an unknown
depth.

01:32:58.500 --> 01:33:02.040
As they pushed further, the agents came across
a polar bear.

01:33:02.040 --> 01:33:06.240
Startled, they fired once at it, before realizing
it was already dead.

01:33:06.240 --> 01:33:12.120
Its fur was dotted with crystals of red ice,
creeping its way across the bear’s body.

01:33:12.120 --> 01:33:17.580
Beyond the polar bear, the agents spotted
dozens of bodies, all dead animals.

01:33:17.580 --> 01:33:25.140
There were seals, a snow fox, and finally…a
giant spider, with a leg span of over a meter.

01:33:25.140 --> 01:33:29.700
At first, the spider appeared to be frozen
like the other creatures, but upon further

01:33:29.700 --> 01:33:33.240
investigation, it appeared to be made of red
ice.

01:33:33.240 --> 01:33:39.540
Agent Cassidy recognized the spider as SCP-3023
but was told it was impossible.

01:33:39.540 --> 01:33:44.820
When she pressed for further answers, she
was told to ignore it and continue the sweep.

01:33:44.820 --> 01:33:49.560
Agent Whitmore checked the collection of bodies
in the chamber, looking for any humans among

01:33:49.560 --> 01:33:49.740
them.

01:33:49.740 --> 01:33:54.780
Meanwhile, Hewes spotted a spear sticking
out of the enormous spider, indicating a struggle

01:33:54.780 --> 01:33:58.740
that took place before it and the young man
at the cave’s entrance froze.

01:33:58.740 --> 01:34:02.940
Hewes was interrupted in his task as Agent
Cassidy called out from deeper in the cave,

01:34:02.940 --> 01:34:05.940
saying: “I think I know where the spider
came from.”

01:34:05.940 --> 01:34:10.200
When Hewes followed the sound of her voice,
he found something troubling.

01:34:10.200 --> 01:34:15.960
An aperture, about a meter in diameter, absolutely
covered in red ice.

01:34:15.960 --> 01:34:21.660
It looked like a tunnel, with no ice at all
past its entrance, with a dim light coming

01:34:21.660 --> 01:34:23.220
from somewhere deep inside.

01:34:23.220 --> 01:34:27.600
He lost sight of Agent Cassidy and realized
she must have gone inside of it.

01:34:27.600 --> 01:34:31.980
Upon further observation, Hewes determined
that the walls and the floor of the tunnel

01:34:31.980 --> 01:34:34.980
were wet, with a red puddle about a meter
in.

01:34:34.980 --> 01:34:40.140
Hewes and Whitmore called to Cassidy, attempting
to lead her back out of the tunnel, but received

01:34:40.140 --> 01:34:41.100
no response.

01:34:41.100 --> 01:34:46.080
Hewes attempted to go in and retrieve her,
but Control forbade him from going any further.

01:34:46.080 --> 01:34:51.060
After a conversation with Control that has
been stricken from the official file, Hewes

01:34:51.060 --> 01:34:54.900
relented and agreed to withdraw his remaining
team and exit the site.

01:34:54.900 --> 01:34:59.880
Hewes and Whitmore left the cave without further
incident and returned to Foundation headquarters.

01:34:59.880 --> 01:35:04.800
In spite of a D-Class recovery team being
sent into the cave to search for her, Agent

01:35:04.800 --> 01:35:06.780
Cassidy’s body was never found.

01:35:06.780 --> 01:35:11.280
The cave was blocked off from the public,
in order to avoid further civilian contact

01:35:11.280 --> 01:35:13.680
with the red ice and red water inside.

01:35:13.680 --> 01:35:18.960
Though the origin of the red ice in Alaska
is not known for sure, this cave, and the

01:35:18.960 --> 01:35:23.460
pool deep within it, are thought to be the
source of this particular infestation.

01:35:23.460 --> 01:35:28.260
The official cause of death listed on record
for the bodies found in Alaska was internal

01:35:28.260 --> 01:35:32.820
bleeding, but what really happened to them
was something much, much worse.

01:35:32.820 --> 01:35:38.580
These men had transformed and frozen from
the inside out, their blood turning to ice

01:35:38.580 --> 01:35:41.460
and their cells going solid one at a time.

01:35:41.460 --> 01:35:45.660
The low ambient temperatures in the area are
thought to have slowed the freezing process

01:35:45.660 --> 01:35:46.080
down.

01:35:46.080 --> 01:35:51.840
You heard that right, the cold kept them from
freezing faster, as counterintuitive as it

01:35:51.840 --> 01:35:52.020
sounds.

01:35:52.020 --> 01:35:56.400
This prolonged their deaths and kept them
conscious up until the very end.

01:35:56.400 --> 01:36:01.800
Even as their bodies were freezing solid,
their very cells turning against them, they

01:36:01.800 --> 01:36:03.720
were awake and aware of it all.

01:36:03.720 --> 01:36:09.300
These unfortunate men came into contact with
and lost their lives to a substance known

01:36:09.300 --> 01:36:11.460
as SCP-009.

01:36:11.460 --> 01:36:18.420
SCP-009 in its liquid form, maintained at
temperatures between -100 and 0 degrees Celsius,

01:36:18.420 --> 01:36:22.920
resembles ordinary distilled water aside from
its bright red color.

01:36:22.920 --> 01:36:28.980
It behaves opposite of water, reaching a frozen
solid state at higher temperatures, and vaporizing

01:36:28.980 --> 01:36:32.520
into a steam-like gas at temperatures below
-100 degrees.

01:36:33.120 --> 01:36:39.060
An attempt to examine SCP-009’s atomic structure
was unable to achieve conclusive results.

01:36:39.060 --> 01:36:44.520
The substance looks as if it is made up of
normal water molecules, though obviously,

01:36:44.520 --> 01:36:46.800
it is much more than simple water.

01:36:46.800 --> 01:36:53.220
SCP-009 appears relatively harmless at first
glance, but its real dangerous potential lies

01:36:53.220 --> 01:36:58.440
in its ability to contaminate water-based
solutions, transferring its properties to

01:36:58.440 --> 01:36:58.680
them.

01:36:58.680 --> 01:37:05.100
A contaminated liquid begins to exhibit the
same unusual behavior as SCP-009, freezing

01:37:05.100 --> 01:37:09.780
at temperatures above 0 degrees and vaporizing
at temperatures below -100.

01:37:09.780 --> 01:37:16.800
It has been shown to effectively contaminate
ice, steam, tea, fruit juice, seawater, and

01:37:16.800 --> 01:37:20.820
blood, in a process taking between three minutes
and several hours.

01:37:20.820 --> 01:37:27.060
These concerning properties raised questions
about what SCP-009, and liquids contaminated

01:37:27.060 --> 01:37:30.240
by it, might do if they make contact with
a human body.

01:37:30.240 --> 01:37:36.900
Several D-Class Personnel were used as test
subjects, exposed to SCP-009 in a controlled

01:37:36.900 --> 01:37:39.360
environment and observed from a safe distance.

01:37:39.360 --> 01:37:46.740
When first exposed to SCP-009, the test subjects
reported nothing unusual except a slight sensation

01:37:46.740 --> 01:37:48.780
of warming on the surface of their skin.

01:37:48.780 --> 01:37:53.640
Then, frost began to form across the surface
of the exposed area as the subject’s body

01:37:53.640 --> 01:37:55.620
heat raised the substance’s temperature.

01:37:55.620 --> 01:38:01.320
This process took between a minute and a few
hours, during which ice crystals began to

01:38:01.320 --> 01:38:03.180
form along the top layer of the skin.

01:38:03.180 --> 01:38:06.240
This stage is known as “Surface Conversion.”

01:38:06.240 --> 01:38:12.180
In the next stage, “Deep Tissue Conversion,”
the continued increase in SCP-009’s temperature

01:38:12.180 --> 01:38:16.920
causes a ripple effect of reactions through
the subject’s body, ice crystals forming

01:38:16.920 --> 01:38:18.840
in the cells and throughout the blood.

01:38:18.840 --> 01:38:22.200
The subject remained alive and conscious during
this stage.

01:38:22.200 --> 01:38:26.280
Details about the fourth stage of the process
have been expunged from the official record,

01:38:26.280 --> 01:38:29.760
but it is safe to say that something horrible
happened.

01:38:29.760 --> 01:38:35.280
After several of these experiments were conducted,
testing on living D-class subjects was officially

01:38:35.280 --> 01:38:36.120
discontinued.

01:38:36.120 --> 01:38:41.880
There was a possibility of experimentation
on SCP-009 regarding its potential application

01:38:41.880 --> 01:38:47.100
to cold fusion, but this was also eventually
discontinued following a disastrous accident

01:38:47.100 --> 01:38:49.500
at an unnamed Foundation test site.

01:38:49.500 --> 01:38:55.380
The site was completely destroyed, and pieces
of the lead Agent conducting the cold fusion

01:38:55.380 --> 01:38:57.600
research have still not been recovered.

01:38:57.600 --> 01:39:04.500
For now, SCP-009 is kept under strict containment
and only tested under particular, highly regulated

01:39:04.500 --> 01:39:05.400
circumstances.

01:39:05.400 --> 01:39:10.800
SCP-009 is kept in a sealed storage tank of
heat-resistant alloy.

01:39:10.800 --> 01:39:16.020
It is not to be exposed to any temperatures
higher than zero degrees Celsius unless there

01:39:16.020 --> 01:39:18.720
is official, Foundation-sanctioned testing
being done.

01:39:18.720 --> 01:39:22.800
No water-based liquids are allowed within
30 meters of the containment area.

01:39:22.800 --> 01:39:27.720
The storage tank is outfitted with temperature
sensors that are to be monitored at all times

01:39:27.720 --> 01:39:32.580
in order to prevent the temperature within
from rising and is kept cold by three different

01:39:32.580 --> 01:39:33.720
cooling units.

01:39:33.720 --> 01:39:38.940
If the sensors or cooling units malfunction
for any reason, they must be fixed immediately

01:39:38.940 --> 01:39:40.080
to prevent disaster.

01:39:40.080 --> 01:39:46.680
When testing is done on SCP-009, the containment
area is kept in a vacuum and the personnel

01:39:46.680 --> 01:39:49.080
working with it must wear protective gear.

01:39:49.080 --> 01:39:53.700
After testing, all involved personnel must
quarantine for at least 12 hours.

01:39:53.700 --> 01:39:59.460
Any living organisms contaminated by SCP-009
must be terminated promptly.

01:39:59.460 --> 01:40:06.240
While the exact origins of SCP-009 are unclear,
it clearly does not follow the laws of nature

01:40:06.240 --> 01:40:07.560
as we understand them.

01:40:07.560 --> 01:40:13.380
A Foundation expert in Xenospatial Physics
suggested that SCP-009 may have come from

01:40:13.380 --> 01:40:18.900
a universe with alternate laws of physics,
explaining its reversal of the ordinary conditions

01:40:18.900 --> 01:40:19.980
for states of matter.

01:40:19.980 --> 01:40:26.280
During an instance of SCP-507 - The reluctant
dimension hopper - shifting into an alternate

01:40:26.280 --> 01:40:32.940
universe, an instance of SCP-009 was unexpectedly
observed that may help confirm that theory.

01:40:32.940 --> 01:40:38.760
In the test area where SCP-507 appeared, red
snow fell for about 27 minutes.

01:40:38.760 --> 01:40:43.500
Grass touched by this red snow began to react
and freeze over within a few minutes.

01:40:43.500 --> 01:40:48.840
The other plant life touched by the snow turned
bright red and expanded to a larger size.

01:40:48.840 --> 01:40:53.580
It also began to sprout bright blue tentacles
covered with red mucilage.

01:40:53.580 --> 01:41:00.420
Upon closer examination, the mucilage turned
out to be comprised of small amounts of SCP-009.

01:41:00.420 --> 01:41:06.120
This raised additional questions, for instance:
how are these plants able to survive constant

01:41:06.120 --> 01:41:08.400
exposure to SCP-009?

01:41:08.400 --> 01:41:13.920
This matter is currently under investigation,
but the prevailing theory is that this plant

01:41:13.920 --> 01:41:18.600
is an example of plant life from SCP-009’s
native universe.

01:41:18.600 --> 01:41:23.760
Whatever it is, and wherever it comes from,
it should not be allowed to come into contact

01:41:23.760 --> 01:41:26.160
with earth-based organic life forms.

01:41:26.160 --> 01:41:30.900
Well, not unless being horrifically frozen
to death by your own body feels like an appealing

01:41:30.900 --> 01:41:31.980
experience to you.

01:41:31.980 --> 01:41:37.860
The coastline where SCP-009 was initially
discovered, and its first victims on record

01:41:37.860 --> 01:41:40.740
were found, was located very close to the
ocean.

01:41:40.740 --> 01:41:45.660
Thankfully, the exact area of contamination
was dry and cold enough to keep the red ice

01:41:45.660 --> 01:41:50.460
from spreading, but if it had been even a
few meters closer to the water it could have

01:41:50.460 --> 01:41:52.380
spread into the North Pacific Ocean.

01:41:52.380 --> 01:41:57.240
With contamination of that scale, it could
have very easily infected thousands of people,

01:41:57.240 --> 01:42:02.100
perhaps spreading into other bodies of water
and triggering a global extinction event.

01:42:02.100 --> 01:42:08.160
Because of this threat, several members of
the SCP Foundation proposed that SCP-009 be

01:42:08.160 --> 01:42:12.480
upgraded to Keter class in order to reflect
its danger to humanity.

01:42:12.480 --> 01:42:17.340
However, this request was denied due to the
currently effective containment measures in

01:42:17.340 --> 01:42:17.520
place.

01:42:17.520 --> 01:42:23.040
The red ice is unable to spread to new hosts,
infecting the water supply and turning all

01:42:23.040 --> 01:42:25.320
living things into frozen husks.

01:42:25.320 --> 01:42:26.160
For now.

01:42:26.160 --> 01:42:30.720
Let’s just hope we don’t see any red snowstorms
any time soon.

01:42:30.720 --> 01:42:36.060
There is something maddening about a repetitive,
consistent sound, don’t you agree?

01:42:36.060 --> 01:42:41.760
The narrator of Edgar Allen Poe’s The Tell-Tale
Heart is driven mad by the nonstop beating

01:42:41.760 --> 01:42:44.220
of a heart coming from beneath his floorboards.

01:42:44.220 --> 01:42:47.040
But even something less&nbsp;
horrible than a disembodied&nbsp;

01:42:47.040 --> 01:42:49.380
heartbeat can fray a person’s nerves.

01:42:49.380 --> 01:42:51.720
Superficially less horrible, anyway.

01:42:51.720 --> 01:42:56.760
Something as simple as, say, the relentless
ticking of a clock.

01:42:56.760 --> 01:43:02.760
After all, what could be more frightening
than a reminder of the sands of time passing

01:43:02.760 --> 01:43:03.900
through our fingers?

01:43:03.900 --> 01:43:08.400
Of the finite steps on life’s long and winding
road?

01:43:08.400 --> 01:43:15.180
We have the answer to that question: The scariest
thing of all is the monster waiting on the

01:43:15.180 --> 01:43:18.600
other side of the road, twisted and hungry.

01:43:18.600 --> 01:43:23.700
The thing that strikes when the ticking eventually
stops.

01:43:23.700 --> 01:43:26.040
When time is up.

01:43:26.040 --> 01:43:26.940
Tick.

01:43:26.940 --> 01:43:27.660
Tock.

01:43:27.660 --> 01:43:28.440
Tick.

01:43:28.440 --> 01:43:28.940
Tock.

01:43:29.400 --> 01:43:34.860
Many years ago, a clockmaker in the German
town of Freiburg was renowned for his ability

01:43:34.860 --> 01:43:40.680
to produce exquisite personalized clocks for
his clientele all across the town, the country,

01:43:40.680 --> 01:43:42.060
and even beyond.

01:43:42.060 --> 01:43:46.920
His unparalleled constructions made him the
only man to reach out to when it came to getting

01:43:46.920 --> 01:43:52.260
your hands on a beautiful, ornate timepiece
that would ease the anxieties of the passing

01:43:52.260 --> 01:43:56.100
hours.
He ate, slept, and breathed clocks.

01:43:56.100 --> 01:43:57.360
It was his life.

01:43:57.360 --> 01:43:58.620
His calling.

01:43:58.620 --> 01:44:02.820
As such, the clockmaker had grown accustomed
to the sound of ticking.

01:44:02.820 --> 01:44:07.740
He heard it in the morning when he awoke to
the cry of his cuckoo clock, he listened to

01:44:07.740 --> 01:44:12.840
it all day in his workshop as he repaired
and constructed clocks of all shapes and sizes,

01:44:12.840 --> 01:44:17.940
and it was the sound that lulled him to sleep
at night after each long, hard day.

01:44:17.940 --> 01:44:20.880
It gave life a pleasant rhythm.

01:44:20.880 --> 01:44:27.600
One day, however, he noticed a particularly
loud, repetitive sound had permeated his home.

01:44:27.600 --> 01:44:32.520
It was rhythmic, like the ticking of his clocks,
but harsher somehow.

01:44:32.520 --> 01:44:39.240
It did not gently tick, but rather cracked,
like the way his knees popped when a harsh

01:44:39.240 --> 01:44:40.080
winter was coming.

01:44:40.080 --> 01:44:43.560
Something in it made his stomach ache with
dread.

01:44:43.560 --> 01:44:49.980
He began taking apart every clock in his workshop,
looking for the source of the sound, but still,

01:44:49.980 --> 01:44:51.420
it persisted.

01:44:51.420 --> 01:44:58.260
He sat there at his desk, surrounded by gears
and pieces of wood, glass, and metal, and

01:44:58.260 --> 01:45:01.500
still, the sound pounded against his eardrums.

01:45:01.500 --> 01:45:02.460
Tick.

01:45:02.460 --> 01:45:03.240
Tock.

01:45:03.240 --> 01:45:04.200
Tick.

01:45:04.200 --> 01:45:04.800
Tock.

01:45:04.800 --> 01:45:07.920
The clockmaker was stumped by the mysterious
ticking noise.

01:45:07.920 --> 01:45:12.960
It felt too real, too vivid, to be some kind
of hallucination.

01:45:12.960 --> 01:45:18.360
He would have bet every clock he ever made
that the noise was coming from outside of

01:45:18.360 --> 01:45:18.720
his head.

01:45:18.720 --> 01:45:23.640
He was a man so astute in his clock-making
abilities that he could tell his own creations

01:45:23.640 --> 01:45:29.460
apart in the dark from the mere timbre of
their ticking, but here, he was in the presence

01:45:29.460 --> 01:45:31.200
of an alien force.

01:45:31.200 --> 01:45:37.260
This frightening, almost predatory sound that
lingered in his periphery, always somewhere

01:45:37.260 --> 01:45:40.380
but not confined to any fixed point.

01:45:40.380 --> 01:45:43.440
He was reminded, vaguely, of Peter Pan.

01:45:43.440 --> 01:45:49.440
Of the crocodile that’d eaten Captain Hook’s
hand and alarm clock, which survived and continued

01:45:49.440 --> 01:45:51.540
ticking in the literal belly of the beast.

01:45:51.540 --> 01:45:56.520
Hook, a vicious pirate captain, would become
a gibbering wreck when the ticking sound got

01:45:56.520 --> 01:45:57.060
closer.

01:45:57.060 --> 01:46:02.280
Did he fear the predator whom the ticking
foretold or the passage of time that pushed

01:46:02.280 --> 01:46:06.900
him further into the reaper’s fold in the
otherwise immortal plane of Neverland?

01:46:06.900 --> 01:46:07.920
Tick.

01:46:07.920 --> 01:46:08.700
Tock.

01:46:08.700 --> 01:46:09.420
Tick.

01:46:09.420 --> 01:46:10.140
Tock.

01:46:10.140 --> 01:46:12.240
The clockmaker’s search continued.

01:46:12.240 --> 01:46:17.880
He turned his workplace upside down and inside
out in pursuit of the seemingly sourceless

01:46:17.880 --> 01:46:18.480
ticking.

01:46:18.480 --> 01:46:23.940
He checked in every hiding place, every closet,
cupboard, cubby hole, and cabinet.

01:46:23.940 --> 01:46:24.660
Nothing.

01:46:24.660 --> 01:46:29.640
He moved the furniture, tied up the curtains,
rolled up all the carpets.

01:46:29.640 --> 01:46:30.480
Nothing.

01:46:30.480 --> 01:46:36.240
In his desperation, he took a claw hammer
from his toolbox and began prying the rusty

01:46:36.240 --> 01:46:38.880
nails from the ground, before peeling up the&nbsp;

01:46:38.880 --> 01:46:42.120
floorboards and checking&nbsp;
the dusty, spider-infested

01:46:42.120 --> 01:46:43.260
spaces underneath.

01:46:43.260 --> 01:46:49.140
Perhaps some mechanism had fallen down there,
or had always been there, just ticking away.

01:46:49.140 --> 01:46:52.320
There had to be something down there.

01:46:52.320 --> 01:46:53.220
But no.

01:46:53.220 --> 01:46:56.880
Only dirt, insects, and shadows.

01:46:56.880 --> 01:46:58.560
Maybe he was going mad.

01:46:58.560 --> 01:47:04.200
Maybe it was tinnitus, or the indelible impression
that hearing years upon years of ticking had

01:47:04.200 --> 01:47:09.000
left in his mind, the way an image is burned
into a plasma screen if it’s left there

01:47:09.000 --> 01:47:09.660
for too long.

01:47:09.660 --> 01:47:14.640
Maybe it was some shadowy government agency
trying to drive him mad with the use of some

01:47:14.640 --> 01:47:16.200
new sound-based torture device.

01:47:16.200 --> 01:47:18.120
Aural terrorism.

01:47:18.120 --> 01:47:20.880
Selective auditory subliminal mind control.

01:47:20.880 --> 01:47:22.500
Havana Syndrome.

01:47:22.500 --> 01:47:26.040
The fizzling edges of sanity&nbsp;
egged on by invisible,&nbsp;

01:47:26.040 --> 01:47:28.860
long-range CIA telesound beams.

01:47:28.860 --> 01:47:32.220
There had to be some kind of explanation.

01:47:32.220 --> 01:47:35.940
But whatever the case, the sound persisted.

01:47:35.940 --> 01:47:38.700
Tick, Tock, Tick, Tock…

01:47:38.700 --> 01:47:42.780
He couldn’t stay there, in the dismembered
ruins of his prestigious clockmaking shop,

01:47:42.780 --> 01:47:43.560
any longer.

01:47:43.560 --> 01:47:45.840
He was clearly under a lot of stress here.

01:47:45.840 --> 01:47:46.980
Not healthy.

01:47:46.980 --> 01:47:48.360
Not good for the mind.

01:47:48.360 --> 01:47:52.920
He decided to close the shop for a few days
and go visit his daughter and her family.

01:47:52.920 --> 01:47:57.300
Some time with his beloved relatives would
soothe his frayed nerves.

01:47:57.300 --> 01:48:02.880
So he packed his bag and made the trip, hoping
that leaving work behind for a few days would

01:48:02.880 --> 01:48:04.320
also loosen up his mind.

01:48:04.320 --> 01:48:10.050
But the entire drive to his daughter’s house,
he could have sworn he heard the sound still,

01:48:10.050 --> 01:48:13.140
keeping perfect time as it cracked again and
again.

01:48:13.140 --> 01:48:16.440
He shook his head, scolding himself for imagining
things.

01:48:16.440 --> 01:48:19.500
There was nothing in the car that could be
making that noise.

01:48:19.500 --> 01:48:24.180
He’d focused on it too much, surely, that’s
why he was obsessing over it now.

01:48:24.180 --> 01:48:30.720
All of this had a rational explanation; he’d
simply thought himself into a corner on this

01:48:30.720 --> 01:48:32.640
one.
Wouldn’t that explain all of this?

01:48:32.640 --> 01:48:38.400
All just a trick in the mind of an overworked
clockmaker sorely in need of a good sabbatical

01:48:38.400 --> 01:48:39.000
in the country.

01:48:39.000 --> 01:48:41.100
This wouldn’t be forever.

01:48:41.100 --> 01:48:44.520
Tick, Tock, Tick, Tock…

01:48:44.520 --> 01:48:49.080
The clockmaker’s daughter greeted him at
the door with a warm embrace and a hearty

01:48:49.080 --> 01:48:51.720
meal, and for a little while, he relaxed.

01:48:51.720 --> 01:48:56.220
The sound of good company and laughter drowned
out the infernal ticking.

01:48:56.220 --> 01:49:00.060
He began to entertain the notion that, perhaps,
the ticking had been a good thing.

01:49:00.060 --> 01:49:05.160
It’d been a long time since he’d seen
his daughter, and that ticking, as frightening

01:49:05.160 --> 01:49:10.140
as it had been, was also the only thing that
pushed him away from the workshop for a while.

01:49:10.140 --> 01:49:13.800
He was somewhat grateful for a good excuse
to take time off.

01:49:13.800 --> 01:49:16.440
Perhaps that was what all this was about.

01:49:16.440 --> 01:49:18.420
A reminder to take it easy.

01:49:18.420 --> 01:49:21.780
After a weekend off, he’d be right as rain,
surely?

01:49:21.780 --> 01:49:28.140
But that night, as he tried to fall asleep,
the sound was there again.

01:49:28.140 --> 01:49:29.700
Taunting him.

01:49:29.700 --> 01:49:33.240
Keeping his eyes open wide and his heart rate
climbing.

01:49:33.240 --> 01:49:38.700
Was it the dark of the room magnifying his
hearing, intensifying that awful ticking,

01:49:38.700 --> 01:49:42.000
or was it louder and closer than ever before?

01:49:42.000 --> 01:49:48.420
It felt as though an invisible clock, like
so many he’d made before, was hanging over

01:49:48.420 --> 01:49:48.780
him.

01:49:48.780 --> 01:49:50.340
But what was holding it?

01:49:50.340 --> 01:49:53.100
That awful, awful sound.

01:49:53.100 --> 01:49:58.860
Like the bubbles popping in the synovial fluids
of a person’s aged and crumbling joints.

01:49:58.860 --> 01:50:00.120
Too organic.

01:50:00.120 --> 01:50:01.980
Too fleshy.

01:50:01.980 --> 01:50:10.500
And it just kept getting louder and closer,
louder and closer, louder and closer…

01:50:10.500 --> 01:50:17.760
Tick…..Tock….Tick…Tock..Tick, TOCK,
TICK, TOCK, TICK, TOCK…

01:50:18.720 --> 01:50:21.600
Until suddenly…it went silent.

01:50:21.600 --> 01:50:24.960
He breathed a sigh of relief and closed his
eyes.

01:50:24.960 --> 01:50:29.460
The clockmaker’s daughter woke to the sound
of her father’s piercing, guttural screams.

01:50:29.460 --> 01:50:34.560
She ran to his room to find the bed sheets
soaked with blood, the bedroom window shattered,

01:50:34.560 --> 01:50:37.200
and her father gone without a trace.

01:50:37.200 --> 01:50:40.500
She went to the police the next day, but they
could do nothing for her.

01:50:40.500 --> 01:50:46.080
Her father had not been the victim of an ordinary
murderer or thief, but something outside the

01:50:46.080 --> 01:50:47.760
realm of understanding.

01:50:47.760 --> 01:50:55.380
It was something ancient, something monstrous,
something…anomalous.

01:50:55.380 --> 01:51:01.020
Though the police could do nothing, another
organization was secretly on the case: The

01:51:01.020 --> 01:51:02.340
SCP Foundation.

01:51:02.340 --> 01:51:07.800
After the clockmaker’s disappearance, operatives
searched the area and discovered the culprit,

01:51:07.800 --> 01:51:12.480
which they captured and designated SCP-4975.

01:51:12.480 --> 01:51:19.920
SCP-4975 is a humanoid entity with bird-like
features, the most notable of which is a sharp,

01:51:19.920 --> 01:51:20.700
pointed beak.

01:51:20.700 --> 01:51:27.180
Its body is long and thin, with bony limbs
with tapered points, with no discernible digits

01:51:27.180 --> 01:51:28.020
of any kind.

01:51:28.020 --> 01:51:32.580
Its body, including its beak, is covered with
a thick, hard layer of skin.

01:51:32.580 --> 01:51:37.680
The entity’s most notable feature is not
its appearance, however, but in its skeleton,

01:51:37.680 --> 01:51:39.540
particularly its spine.

01:51:39.540 --> 01:51:44.820
The cervical vertebrae of the creature are
not interconnected, and are capable of independent

01:51:44.820 --> 01:51:45.300
movement.

01:51:45.300 --> 01:51:51.720
They rotate, one vertebra at a time, from
back to front in order, all the way up to

01:51:51.720 --> 01:51:54.360
the entity’s head, in a particular rhythm.

01:51:54.360 --> 01:52:00.180
This produces the clicking, or cracking sound
that is so terribly familiar to its intended

01:52:00.180 --> 01:52:00.780
victims.

01:52:00.780 --> 01:52:06.960
It repeats the motion constantly, over and
over again, only stopping when it is preparing

01:52:06.960 --> 01:52:09.000
to attack its chosen prey.

01:52:09.000 --> 01:52:15.300
SCP-4975 does not kill impulsively, simply
selecting a convenient victim.

01:52:15.300 --> 01:52:21.360
Instead, it stalks its prey for months at
a time, sometimes even a year, following them

01:52:21.360 --> 01:52:24.000
in darkness, hiding just out of sight.

01:52:24.000 --> 01:52:31.980
The only sign of its presence is that sound,
the clicking, cracking, tick tock, tick tock

01:52:31.980 --> 01:52:37.920
of its bones as it bides its time, knowing
that it can wait as long as it needs or wants

01:52:37.920 --> 01:52:39.420
to before it strikes.

01:52:39.420 --> 01:52:44.640
When it is ready to feast, it will beat and
tear at the victim’s body with the tapered

01:52:44.640 --> 01:52:50.100
points of its limbs, shredding the flesh and
pecking at it much like a vulture rips at

01:52:50.100 --> 01:52:51.180
a fresh carcass.

01:52:51.180 --> 01:52:57.840
Then, it can savor its meal, using the body
as food for about three months before it needs

01:52:57.840 --> 01:52:58.800
to hunt again.

01:52:58.800 --> 01:53:05.040
Though its exact age is unknown, it is theorized
that the creature is hundreds, if not thousands,

01:53:05.040 --> 01:53:05.760
of years old.

01:53:05.760 --> 01:53:10.860
Written evidence of its existence has been
traced back as far as the 1500s.

01:53:10.860 --> 01:53:17.100
There are mentions of a creature resembling
SCP-4975 throughout German folklore, appearing

01:53:17.100 --> 01:53:21.000
in carvings, paintings, folk tales, and nursery
rhymes.

01:53:21.000 --> 01:53:26.160
One such nursery rhyme was discovered and
translated by the Foundation during the research

01:53:26.160 --> 01:53:26.520
process.

01:53:26.520 --> 01:53:31.560
Though its rhyme scheme was lost when it was
translated to English, the eerie feeling it

01:53:31.560 --> 01:53:32.640
evokes was not.

01:53:32.640 --> 01:53:37.260
The rhyme goes:
“"Tick tock", the cuckoo clock ticks.

01:53:37.260 --> 01:53:40.320
"Cuckoo", the bird inside sings.

01:53:40.320 --> 01:53:45.840
Tick tock tick tock tick tock tick tock.

01:53:45.840 --> 01:53:49.080
As ticks the time, so ticks your heart.

01:53:49.080 --> 01:53:52.080
May you live long as you hear its song.

01:53:52.080 --> 01:53:57.780
Tick tock tick tock tick tock tick tock.

01:53:57.780 --> 01:54:02.760
Listen close, for when it stops
the hatchling comes out of its home.

01:54:02.760 --> 01:54:08.520
Tick tock tick tock tick tock tick-
Did you hear it?

01:54:08.520 --> 01:54:09.660
Did it stop?

01:54:09.660 --> 01:54:13.800
My child, it meant your time was up.”

01:54:13.800 --> 01:54:19.560
The research team theorizes that this nursery
rhyme, and others like it, was used to warn

01:54:19.560 --> 01:54:25.980
children about potential indicators of danger
from SCP-4975, and teach them to be wary of

01:54:25.980 --> 01:54:27.060
its hunting patterns.

01:54:27.060 --> 01:54:31.740
Knowledge, after all, is one of the best weapons
in anyone’s arsenal when it comes to the

01:54:31.740 --> 01:54:32.280
anomalous.

01:54:32.280 --> 01:54:37.320
Without much more knowledge than this little
poem provides, and what they had observed

01:54:37.320 --> 01:54:44.100
prior to SCP-4975’s capture, the SCP Foundation
did its best to create adequate containment

01:54:44.100 --> 01:54:45.300
measures for the creature.

01:54:45.300 --> 01:54:51.360
Currently, SCP-4975 is kept in a standard
steel containment cell, and is prohibited

01:54:51.360 --> 01:54:52.980
from any direct human contact.

01:54:52.980 --> 01:54:58.500
It can be observed via security footage, but
no human beings are permitted to go inside,

01:54:58.500 --> 01:55:01.740
lest they serve as the creature’s next meal.

01:55:01.740 --> 01:55:07.020
If a containment breach occurs, any personnel
that report hearing a repetitive cracking

01:55:07.020 --> 01:55:12.060
or ticking sound are to be isolated until
the entity has been captured and placed back

01:55:12.060 --> 01:55:15.360
in its cell, or until the sound stops.

01:55:15.360 --> 01:55:21.840
Though SCP-4975 is currently contained, there
is a chance that it's captive state does not

01:55:21.840 --> 01:55:23.700
actually make it any less lethal.

01:55:23.700 --> 01:55:26.160
After a harrowing incident that sent many&nbsp;

01:55:26.160 --> 01:55:28.860
attending researchers to&nbsp;
the on-site psychologist’s

01:55:28.860 --> 01:55:33.660
office, the Foundation was given reason to
believe that containing it does not actually

01:55:33.660 --> 01:55:34.980
stop it from hunting.

01:55:34.980 --> 01:55:40.920
On September 16, 2002, something horrible
happened near the Black Forest in Germany.

01:55:40.920 --> 01:55:46.440
A team of Foundation operatives had been placed
in the area to monitor a man from Freiburg

01:55:46.440 --> 01:55:50.760
who had complained to the local police about
a clicking sound that had been following him

01:55:50.760 --> 01:55:52.380
around for quite some time.

01:55:52.380 --> 01:55:57.540
Over the course of four months of being unable
to escape the sound, or the feeling that he

01:55:57.540 --> 01:56:03.060
was being watched no matter where he went,
he had become convinced that someone was stalking

01:56:03.060 --> 01:56:03.240
him.

01:56:03.240 --> 01:56:09.360
It was a bizarre situation, and he wasn’t
certain how his stalker was making this maddening

01:56:09.360 --> 01:56:12.360
sound, but he believed his life to be in danger.

01:56:12.360 --> 01:56:18.330
Concerned that this could be the work of SCP-4975,
the Foundation operatives took him into their

01:56:18.330 --> 01:56:18.900
custody.

01:56:18.900 --> 01:56:23.760
The police were given a cover story, claiming
that the man was experiencing a sense of paranoia

01:56:23.760 --> 01:56:28.620
as well as auditory hallucinations as a result
of side effects from chemotherapy.

01:56:28.620 --> 01:56:33.300
Once the Foundation operatives explained to
the man that they meant him no harm, believed

01:56:33.300 --> 01:56:37.620
him about his fears, and wished to help, he
opened up about his experiences.

01:56:37.620 --> 01:56:42.360
He told the operatives that, in addition to
the sound and the feeling of something following

01:56:42.360 --> 01:56:45.300
him, he had seen a monstrous figure in the
woods.

01:56:45.300 --> 01:56:49.980
He had kept this detail to himself when speaking
to the police, afraid they would have him

01:56:49.980 --> 01:56:51.840
committed rather than listening to him.

01:56:51.840 --> 01:56:56.640
The operatives asked him to lead them to the
place where he had seen the monster, and he

01:56:56.640 --> 01:56:57.060
agreed.

01:56:57.060 --> 01:57:02.040
The man led the team to a densely wooded part
of the forest, trees blocking out the sunlight

01:57:02.040 --> 01:57:06.000
until their surroundings became as dark as
if it were the middle of the night.

01:57:06.000 --> 01:57:10.920
As they walked deeper and deeper into the
forest, the man became increasingly anxious.

01:57:10.920 --> 01:57:16.500
His breath came in short, strained gasps,
his eyes darted from tree to tree, and he

01:57:16.500 --> 01:57:21.300
jumped at the slightest sound of a twig snapping
beneath someone’s foot or branches rustling

01:57:21.300 --> 01:57:22.320
in a gust of wind.

01:57:22.320 --> 01:57:24.780
Suddenly, mid-stride, he froze.

01:57:24.780 --> 01:57:28.200
His eyes were wide, his face white as a sheet.

01:57:28.200 --> 01:57:30.900
With a trembling hand, he pointed toward a
nearby tree.

01:57:30.900 --> 01:57:35.640
In a voice so faint it was almost a whisper,
he said: “There.”

01:57:35.640 --> 01:57:38.940
The operatives turned to look, but saw nothing
there.

01:57:38.940 --> 01:57:41.280
The man repeated, “There!”

01:57:41.280 --> 01:57:43.500
but they couldn’t see anything but the trees.

01:57:43.500 --> 01:57:48.900
The man stumbled back, going weak at the knees
from pure terror, and continued to point at

01:57:48.900 --> 01:57:50.460
the empty space next to the tree.

01:57:50.460 --> 01:57:54.960
Just as one operative was turning to another
to comment that their witness must be out

01:57:54.960 --> 01:57:59.940
of his mind, the man suddenly collapsed onto
the ground, as if an invisible, powerful force

01:57:59.940 --> 01:58:00.900
had thrown him down.

01:58:00.900 --> 01:58:06.900
The man screamed for help, struggling against
the unseen attacker as it slashed at his face

01:58:06.900 --> 01:58:12.120
and his chest, tearing through fabric and
skin, blood spraying across the forest floor.

01:58:12.120 --> 01:58:16.560
Two officers drew their weapons, firing at
where they guessed the assailant might be,

01:58:16.560 --> 01:58:20.340
but their bullets ricocheted uselessly off
of nearby tree trunks.

01:58:20.340 --> 01:58:24.420
Another rushed to the man on the ground, grabbed
him under the arms, and attempted to pull

01:58:24.420 --> 01:58:25.380
him out of harm’s way.

01:58:25.380 --> 01:58:30.540
However, the man would not budge, as the invisible
force held him in place, shredding through

01:58:30.540 --> 01:58:33.000
his stomach as it fought to keep its prey.

01:58:33.000 --> 01:58:38.040
Afraid to rip open the stomach wound any further,
the operative quickly ceased his attempts

01:58:38.040 --> 01:58:38.760
to move the man.

01:58:38.760 --> 01:58:42.840
Instead, he pulled out his weapon and did
the only merciful thing he could think to

01:58:42.840 --> 01:58:47.520
do: he shot the local man in the head, putting
him out of his misery before he was ripped

01:58:47.520 --> 01:58:48.180
to shreds.

01:58:48.180 --> 01:58:53.880
The operatives watched, some in silent shock,
some continuing to fire their weapons, some

01:58:53.880 --> 01:58:58.320
vomiting from sheer disgust, as strips of
the dead man’s flesh ripped off the bone

01:58:58.320 --> 01:59:01.200
and disappeared, one piece at a time.

01:59:01.200 --> 01:59:07.260
Meanwhile, thousands of miles away, surveillance
footage at SCP-4975’s containment site picked

01:59:07.260 --> 01:59:10.200
up some peculiar activity in the creature’s
cell.

01:59:10.200 --> 01:59:16.440
It stopped rotating its neck, which it had
done almost constantly since being captured,

01:59:16.440 --> 01:59:19.380
and stared at the corner of its containment
cell.

01:59:19.380 --> 01:59:24.060
Its eyes were wide, unblinking, and it did
not move a muscle.

01:59:24.060 --> 01:59:29.040
It stayed still for several minutes, until
it eventually broke the unsettling stillness

01:59:29.040 --> 01:59:32.220
to eat, greedily gobbling down slices of meat.

01:59:32.220 --> 01:59:33.960
There was one problem, though.

01:59:33.960 --> 01:59:36.780
The creature had not yet been fed that day.

01:59:36.780 --> 01:59:42.840
All Foundation operatives dispatched to Germany
to investigate SCP-4975 were recalled back

01:59:42.840 --> 01:59:47.640
to their original sites, and additional research
has been suspended until further notice.

01:59:47.640 --> 01:59:52.260
In light of this new information, a motion
has been filed to reclassify the creature

01:59:52.260 --> 01:59:57.480
as Keter, and potentially impossible to contain
with the Foundation’s current resources.

01:59:57.480 --> 02:00:02.880
As terrible as it is to admit, this is one
monster the Foundation has not yet found a

02:00:02.880 --> 02:00:03.660
way to stop.

02:00:03.660 --> 02:00:09.900
They may have it locked in a cage, but it
can still hunt anyone, anywhere, any time

02:00:09.900 --> 02:00:10.740
it wants to.

02:00:10.740 --> 02:00:11.760
Wait a second.

02:00:11.760 --> 02:00:14.460
Shh, be very quiet.

02:00:14.460 --> 02:00:15.660
What’s that sound?

02:00:15.660 --> 02:00:17.580
In your room, right now.

02:00:17.580 --> 02:00:18.420
Listen closely.

02:00:19.380 --> 02:00:19.800
Tick.

02:00:19.800 --> 02:00:20.220
Tick.

02:00:20.220 --> 02:00:20.760
Tick.

02:00:20.760 --> 02:00:21.540
Do you hear it?

02:00:21.540 --> 02:00:24.720
Don’t worry, it’s probably just a clock
or a kitchen timer.

02:00:24.720 --> 02:00:26.700
Maybe it’s just your imagination.

02:00:26.700 --> 02:00:27.840
Tick.

02:00:27.840 --> 02:00:28.500
Tick.

02:00:28.500 --> 02:00:29.220
Tick.

02:00:29.220 --> 02:00:31.320
Whatever it is, I’m sure you’ll be fine.

02:00:31.320 --> 02:00:34.860
There’s nothing dangerous about a weird
sound from time to time.

02:00:34.860 --> 02:00:38.940
You don’t have anything to fear unless it
suddenly goes silent.

02:00:38.940 --> 02:00:44.580
That’s when you’re really in trouble,
when you know what SCP-4975 is about to strike,

02:00:44.580 --> 02:00:46.020
to devour you alive.

02:00:46.020 --> 02:00:47.040
Wait.

02:00:47.040 --> 02:00:47.580
Stop.

02:00:47.580 --> 02:00:49.560
Hold your breath, don’t make a single peep.

02:00:49.560 --> 02:00:50.520
Do you hear it?

02:00:50.520 --> 02:00:51.720
Neither do I.

02:00:51.720 --> 02:00:57.180
You hear their footsteps coming down the&nbsp;
halls. Or are those your own? Can you even&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:57.180 --> 02:01:01.680
tell the difference? You can tell they’re&nbsp;
getting closer and you can feel the hate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:01.680 --> 02:01:06.960
the rage. You turn, shaking, and&nbsp;
finally see them standing right&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:06.960 --> 02:01:12.240
in front of you. But in that moment, you&nbsp;
might as well be looking into a mirror.

02:01:12.240 --> 02:01:18.780
And who knows? Perhaps you are. You just don’t&nbsp;
seem to remember having so many reflections...

02:01:18.780 --> 02:01:22.740
Have you ever heard the saying “You&nbsp;
are your own worst enemy?” Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:22.740 --> 02:01:29.100
it isn’t usually meant literally. But what if it&nbsp;
was? What if you had to fight a monster…that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:29.100 --> 02:01:34.200
you? All of your flaws are reflected back&nbsp;
at you. Your strengths, your weaknesses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:34.200 --> 02:01:39.840
your deepest fears, with no way to escape&nbsp;
except a battle to the death. Either way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:39.840 --> 02:01:45.900
you’re not making it out alive. It’s just a&nbsp;
matter of which version of you survives. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:45.900 --> 02:01:52.440
this isn’t a thought experiment. No, according to&nbsp;
the findings of the SCP Foundation, it’s very much&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:52.440 --> 02:01:59.760
a reality. There is a place where this nightmare&nbsp;
comes to life, and it is known as SCP-1919.

02:01:59.760 --> 02:02:06.420
SCP-1919 is a hotel and converted mansion, built&nbsp;
in the early 20th century. From the outside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:06.420 --> 02:02:09.240
it looks pretty much like it&nbsp;
did when it was first built,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:09.240 --> 02:02:14.040
and it almost looks like a comfortable&nbsp;
place to stay… if you ignore the eastern&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:14.040 --> 02:02:16.920
side of the building that has&nbsp;
sunk partially into the ground.

02:02:16.920 --> 02:02:24.480
The inside, however, is a different story, where&nbsp;
it’s clear the ravages of time have taken their&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:24.480 --> 02:02:30.780
toll. The floorboards and ceilings are rotting,&nbsp;
collapsing in on themselves, and the rooms are&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:30.780 --> 02:02:36.840
filled with debris. It’s deadly enough to explore&nbsp;
the hotel for these reasons alone, but this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:36.840 --> 02:02:42.360
only the beginning of the danger for a person&nbsp;
inside. In order to determine just how dangerous&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:42.360 --> 02:02:48.360
it is for either one person or group to enter the&nbsp;
structure, the SCP Foundation planned a series of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:48.360 --> 02:02:53.640
research expeditions into the abandoned building,&nbsp;
led by Foundation scientist Dr. Limkiewicz.

02:02:53.640 --> 02:02:58.920
The first expedition seemed relatively&nbsp;
normal, at least it did at the start. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:58.920 --> 02:03:04.200
39-year-old Caucasian D-Class male known as&nbsp;
D7 was sent into the structure with a camera&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:04.200 --> 02:03:10.560
and a communications system, guided remotely by&nbsp;
Dr. Limkiewicz, or Dr. L, and another operative,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:10.560 --> 02:03:17.460
a former head of the MTF Tau-11 “Youth Hostiles”&nbsp;
who is referred to in this file only as T11.

02:03:17.460 --> 02:03:22.140
When he arrived at the building, D7 was&nbsp;
unable to get inside through the front&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:22.140 --> 02:03:26.880
door or windows. After several minutes of&nbsp;
trial and error, he was finally able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:26.880 --> 02:03:31.680
get in through the western entrance. Dr. L&nbsp;
picked up a strange, high-pitched whistling&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:31.680 --> 02:03:36.900
noise upon D7’s entrance into the building,&nbsp;
but it quickly faded away and was disregarded&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:36.900 --> 02:03:42.540
by T11. D7 discovered a torn painting, a&nbsp;
portrait of a young woman with red hair.

02:03:42.540 --> 02:03:47.280
Next to the portrait, shallow scratches&nbsp;
could be seen in the wall, the floor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:47.280 --> 02:03:53.280
and parts of the ceiling. Suddenly, D7 ducked&nbsp;
into a hiding place, alarmed. He, and the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:53.280 --> 02:03:59.520
two operatives listening to his audio feed could&nbsp;
hear heavy breathing… and it didn’t belong to D7.

02:03:59.520 --> 02:04:04.140
Dr. L recommended that D7 evacuate the&nbsp;
building at this sign of another entity&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:04.140 --> 02:04:10.020
inside, but T11 overruled, ordering him to&nbsp;
disregard that instruction and continue his&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:10.020 --> 02:04:15.420
investigation. D7 was told to stay at a safe&nbsp;
distance from whatever was inside with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:15.420 --> 02:04:21.000
and attempt to capture it on video. D7 turned&nbsp;
off his flashlight in order to better hide, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:21.000 --> 02:04:26.580
T11 commanded that he turn it back on. Whatever&nbsp;
was caught in its beam of light was difficult for&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:26.580 --> 02:04:32.160
the camera to see, but it threw D7 into a panic&nbsp;
and he began to run in the opposite direction.

02:04:32.160 --> 02:04:37.560
When prompted to explain what he&nbsp;
saw, D7 simply said: “It was me!”

02:04:37.560 --> 02:04:43.260
D7 ran through the dark, panting with fear&nbsp;
and exertion. Unable to see where his feet&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:43.260 --> 02:04:46.800
were landing, he tripped over something&nbsp;
and came crashing onto the ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:46.800 --> 02:04:52.080
dropping the video camera. This allowed the&nbsp;
observing officers to finally see what D7&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:52.080 --> 02:04:57.540
was so frightened by, and it became&nbsp;
clear just why D7 was so terrified.

02:04:57.540 --> 02:05:03.600
A man, identical looking to D7, approached from&nbsp;
the end of the hallway, making its way toward&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:03.600 --> 02:05:08.880
the real D7. It was followed by another&nbsp;
man who also resembled D7, and another,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:08.880 --> 02:05:13.020
all running toward the original.&nbsp;
They all looked exactly like him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:13.020 --> 02:05:16.920
with a few notable differences. They&nbsp;
were dressed in the same uniform,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:16.920 --> 02:05:22.320
with the same build and the same features,&nbsp;
but each had something slightly off about him.

02:05:22.320 --> 02:05:26.160
One was missing eyelids,&nbsp;
another had malformed hands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:26.160 --> 02:05:30.720
and the third had its lips fused together&nbsp;
into a fleshy mass beneath its nose.

02:05:30.720 --> 02:05:36.420
Dr. L moved to cut the camera feed, but T11&nbsp;
demanded that it be kept running. D7 couldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:36.420 --> 02:05:41.880
be seen by the camera, but the microphone picked&nbsp;
up the sounds of flesh and cloth being torn, along&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:41.880 --> 02:05:47.820
with pained, panicked screams as the duplicates&nbsp;
set upon him. After a moment, the screaming&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:47.820 --> 02:05:53.100
stopped. Two hours later, the camera was broken,&nbsp;
and the expedition brought to a troubling end.

02:05:53.100 --> 02:05:58.320
This was the Foundation’s first glimpse&nbsp;
at the creatures inside of SCP-1919,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:58.320 --> 02:06:03.960
and it was not pretty. It did, however, allow them&nbsp;
to begin understanding the nature of the building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:03.960 --> 02:06:09.300
and what happens when a person goes inside.&nbsp;
It appears that when a human enters the hotel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:09.300 --> 02:06:14.520
several humanoid creatures manifest throughout the&nbsp;
building. These creatures look like the subject,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:14.520 --> 02:06:19.800
and are equipped with the same clothing or items&nbsp;
that the subject brought inside with them. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:19.800 --> 02:06:25.380
they are nearly mirror images of the subject, they&nbsp;
are always slightly warped in a variety of ways.

02:06:25.380 --> 02:06:31.020
These have included changes to limb and digit&nbsp;
length, joint mobility, sealed nostrils,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:31.020 --> 02:06:36.060
lengthened jaws hanging loose and limp,&nbsp;
missing eyelids, and lips that are fused&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:36.060 --> 02:06:40.560
together. These creatures are highly aggressive&nbsp;
toward the structure of the building itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:40.560 --> 02:06:46.380
as well as to the subject that they resemble.&nbsp;
They do not, however, attack each other. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:46.380 --> 02:06:51.240
appear to operate with a hive mind, exhibiting&nbsp;
swarm intelligence like that of an ant colony.

02:06:51.240 --> 02:06:53.880
Once they have been spawned by&nbsp;
the entrance of a new person,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:53.880 --> 02:06:58.620
they will not stop until said person&nbsp;
either escapes the building or is killed.

02:06:58.620 --> 02:07:02.280
After the unfortunate end to the first&nbsp;
expedition, the Foundation prepped for&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:02.280 --> 02:07:09.300
a second trip inside. This time, three men were&nbsp;
sent in with Dr. L’s guidance, known as D3, D4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:09.300 --> 02:07:15.240
and D9. Video cameras were sewn into their clothes&nbsp;
to leave their hands free and to help avoid some&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:15.240 --> 02:07:19.740
of the issues that came up during the first&nbsp;
expedition. This small team was sent in with&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:19.740 --> 02:07:25.380
the orders to terminate the remaining copies of&nbsp;
D7, and further examine the hotel’s interior.

02:07:25.380 --> 02:07:30.420
Upon opening the door to the building, they&nbsp;
were immediately attacked by one of D7’s copies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:30.420 --> 02:07:35.100
which D9 was able to quickly dispatch&nbsp;
by firing his weapon at its head. Next,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:35.100 --> 02:07:40.260
after a great deal of reluctance, the three&nbsp;
men entered the building where they spotted&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:40.260 --> 02:07:45.780
something unusual inside. Dr. L was horrified&nbsp;
when the camera feed revealed seventeen&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:45.780 --> 02:07:49.020
discarded video cameras spread across the floor.

02:07:49.020 --> 02:07:51.960
They didn’t have much time to&nbsp;
react to this new discovery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:51.960 --> 02:07:56.940
however, because two doubles, one&nbsp;
mirroring D7 and another mirroring D9,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:56.940 --> 02:08:01.680
emerged from the wall and began to attack.&nbsp;
Dr. L ordered the team to take shelter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:01.680 --> 02:08:05.580
then called the team of guards outside of&nbsp;
the hotel’s perimeter. They were ordered&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:05.580 --> 02:08:10.320
to begin an immediate full perimeter lockdown,&nbsp;
preventing the doubles from leaving the hotel.

02:08:10.320 --> 02:08:15.600
D3, D4, and D9 attempted to make their&nbsp;
way to a safe corner of the building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:15.600 --> 02:08:22.140
but found themselves met with a murderous double&nbsp;
at every turn. At this point, Dr. L began to hear&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:22.140 --> 02:08:26.820
an unusual sound over the microphone feed, a&nbsp;
high-pitched whine like that of a dentist’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:26.820 --> 02:08:32.400
drill. The operatives on the ground couldn’t hear&nbsp;
a thing, but on Dr. L’s end it was deafening.

02:08:32.400 --> 02:08:37.260
As the team proceeded deeper into the hotel,&nbsp;
they became overcome with a strange feeling&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:37.260 --> 02:08:42.120
of foreboding. Dr. L ordered them to turn&nbsp;
on their flashlights, but they refused and&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:42.120 --> 02:08:48.120
begged Dr. L to keep quiet. When prompted&nbsp;
to explain, D9 said: “she can hear you.”

02:08:48.120 --> 02:08:51.720
The operatives stopped responding,&nbsp;
but their camera feeds caught a faint,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:51.720 --> 02:08:55.320
glowing white light coming from&nbsp;
beneath a door. The door opened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:55.320 --> 02:08:59.460
and the light flooded the camera, making&nbsp;
the images it captured hard to decipher.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:59.460 --> 02:09:04.380
Just a few frames of a quick-moving female&nbsp;
silhouette were captured before the cameras&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:04.380 --> 02:09:11.520
cut to static. The bodies of D3, D4, and D9&nbsp;
were never recovered, nor were their cameras.

02:09:11.520 --> 02:09:17.820
A third expedition was also sent into SCP-1919,&nbsp;
but very little is known about what occurred&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:17.820 --> 02:09:22.920
during it. The video transcript is highly&nbsp;
classified and only those present for its events,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:22.920 --> 02:09:30.780
or approved to research SCP-1919, have access&nbsp;
to it. An update to the SCP-1919 file following&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:30.780 --> 02:09:35.280
Expedition Three though, indicates that&nbsp;
new information was revealed about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:35.280 --> 02:09:40.740
hotel during the excursion. According to the&nbsp;
file update, there is some kind of being at&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:40.740 --> 02:09:46.680
the center of the location which is causing all&nbsp;
of the other creatures, the doubles, to appear.

02:09:46.680 --> 02:09:52.080
The only information available about this&nbsp;
being is the use of the word “her” in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:52.080 --> 02:09:57.900
official Foundation log about SCP-1919. This&nbsp;
seems to match up with the last moments of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:57.900 --> 02:10:03.660
the operatives in Expedition Two, when they&nbsp;
told Dr. L that “she can hear you” and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:03.660 --> 02:10:08.160
few frames of a female figure that were&nbsp;
captured by their cameras. Nothing else&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:08.160 --> 02:10:12.480
is known that has been made available&nbsp;
to anyone outside a very select few.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:12.480 --> 02:10:17.820
Only the original report exists, and all&nbsp;
other copies of it have been destroyed.

02:10:17.820 --> 02:10:22.740
The Foundation has undertaken special containment&nbsp;
procedures to make sure that none of the entities&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:22.740 --> 02:10:28.140
from inside the hotel escape, whether they are&nbsp;
the “evil twins” spawned by humans entering&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:28.140 --> 02:10:33.960
the building, or the mysterious female being at&nbsp;
the center of the entire disturbing phenomenon.

02:10:33.960 --> 02:10:39.600
The Foundation has classified SCP-1919&nbsp;
as Euclid and a two kilometer radius&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:39.600 --> 02:10:45.720
must be maintained around SCP-1919, with all&nbsp;
roads leading to the building are blocked or&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:45.720 --> 02:10:50.880
diverted so that no vehicles are able to&nbsp;
reach it. This perimeter is guarded by a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:50.880 --> 02:10:55.920
set of at least forty armed and armored guards&nbsp;
at any given time. As it has been determined&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:55.920 --> 02:11:00.660
that the doubles spawned by 1919 are equipped&nbsp;
with whatever the human they are copying has,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:00.660 --> 02:11:06.120
no one is allowed to enter the hotel&nbsp;
with body armor or weapons of any kind.

02:11:06.120 --> 02:11:11.040
Anyone that approaches the perimeter that is&nbsp;
not part of an official expedition team will&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:11.040 --> 02:11:16.200
be immediately terminated. No new expeditions&nbsp;
teams are allowed to enter the building unless&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:16.200 --> 02:11:21.300
all doubles from the previous expedition&nbsp;
have been exterminated. In the event that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:21.300 --> 02:11:25.920
they cannot be exterminated, enough time&nbsp;
must elapse between expeditions that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:25.920 --> 02:11:29.880
previous doubles have starved to death.&nbsp;
Though they do not seem to feel hunger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:29.880 --> 02:11:34.980
the doubles do need to eat to survive, and&nbsp;
will die when left alone for long enough.

02:11:34.980 --> 02:11:41.580
SCP-1919 has been sealed off from the rest of&nbsp;
the world, so that no hapless civilians can&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:41.580 --> 02:11:47.280
wander inside and find themselves torn to&nbsp;
pieces by warped images of themselves. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:47.280 --> 02:11:52.080
that comfort turns cold when you realize that&nbsp;
the SCP Foundation still does not understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:52.080 --> 02:11:57.960
what causes these doubles to spawn. Is it&nbsp;
scientific? Supernatural? Or something else?

02:11:57.960 --> 02:12:03.720
No one can be certain. Even more inexplicable&nbsp;
is the entity at the center of all this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:03.720 --> 02:12:09.060
an unknown female presence capable of wreaking&nbsp;
frightening amounts of violence by turning&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:09.060 --> 02:12:14.340
victims’ own images against them. What is the&nbsp;
purpose of these funhouse mirror nightmares?&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:14.340 --> 02:12:19.560
Who is she, what is she, and what does she&nbsp;
want? Currently, the doubles have shown no&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:19.560 --> 02:12:24.960
interest in leaving the hotel except to attack&nbsp;
intruders, and thanks to that fact, as well as&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:24.960 --> 02:12:30.660
the reinforced perimeter outside, these copycats&nbsp;
have not appeared outside of the building itself.

02:12:30.660 --> 02:12:34.980
But what happens if they do escape,&nbsp;
or if the entity that controls them&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:34.980 --> 02:12:39.900
decides to make her home elsewhere? There&nbsp;
is no telling what could happen if this&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:39.900 --> 02:12:43.380
dark power is allowed to move&nbsp;
beyond its current containment.

02:12:43.380 --> 02:12:46.440
Are you prepared to fight a vision of yourself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:46.440 --> 02:12:53.580
twisted almost beyond recognition, lunging after&nbsp;
you with wide bulbous eyes, unnaturally long arms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:53.580 --> 02:12:59.880
and a distended jaw hanging down below its&nbsp;
neck? Better hope you never have to find out.

02:12:59.880 --> 02:13:05.940
Like any other area in the United States,
the state of Florida has a healthy share of

02:13:05.940 --> 02:13:07.860
urban legends and local myths.

02:13:07.860 --> 02:13:13.620
Take for example the legendary Swamp Ape,
the region’s bigfoot equivalent, a hulking

02:13:13.620 --> 02:13:18.540
creature said to run amok in the state’s
many swamps and aquatic areas, identified

02:13:18.540 --> 02:13:23.040
by its strong, repugnant odor and deep, guttural
throat-calls.

02:13:23.040 --> 02:13:28.620
Or the ghosts of the St. Augustine lighthouse,
a grizzly tale revolving around two young

02:13:28.620 --> 02:13:33.600
girls who drowned in the nearby sea while
their mother was working the lighthouse, too

02:13:33.600 --> 02:13:38.100
distracted to hear the cries of her children
as they were swallowed by the current and

02:13:38.100 --> 02:13:39.420
returned to the brine.

02:13:39.420 --> 02:13:44.820
It’s rumored that on some nights, the twins'
laughter and cries are heard from the top

02:13:44.820 --> 02:13:45.780
of the lighthouse.

02:13:45.780 --> 02:13:46.920
Not scary enough?

02:13:46.920 --> 02:13:48.660
What about the devil’s chair?

02:13:48.660 --> 02:13:54.540
A seemingly ordinary bench located in the
town of Cassadaga that was supposedly built

02:13:54.540 --> 02:13:55.860
by the devil himself.

02:13:55.860 --> 02:14:03.000
Every night, at midnight, the man in red returns
to his bench, and if you sit beside him, he’ll

02:14:03.000 --> 02:14:08.700
whisper wicked, horrible things into your
ear, leaving you forever scarred and haunted

02:14:08.700 --> 02:14:09.840
by the experience.

02:14:09.840 --> 02:14:15.120
Just don’t leave a drink behind when you
run off the bench in terror though, another

02:14:15.120 --> 02:14:19.920
legend says that any unopened bottles left
on the bench will mysteriously be opened and

02:14:19.920 --> 02:14:20.880
drained by the morning.

02:14:20.880 --> 02:14:25.680
Torturing damned souls for eternity makes
you a thirsty guy, we guess.

02:14:25.680 --> 02:14:32.220
But to a seasoned viewer of SCP Explained,
urban legends and local oddities might seem

02:14:32.220 --> 02:14:38.520
a bit mundane in comparison to the strange,
inexplicable anomalies that the SCP Foundation

02:14:38.520 --> 02:14:40.860
regularly researches and contains.

02:14:40.860 --> 02:14:46.980
After all, the truth is almost always stranger
than fiction, and if an actual anomaly gets

02:14:46.980 --> 02:14:52.200
picked up as an urban legend, the SCP Foundation
is going to do everything in their power to

02:14:52.200 --> 02:14:58.080
shut it down, cover it up, and make the story
a little more digestible for the general public.

02:14:58.080 --> 02:15:03.180
That means relying on the same, tired tropes
and cliches we’ve all heard before.

02:15:03.180 --> 02:15:10.080
Cursed dolls, bigfoot-like creatures, ghost
hitchhikers, we all know them, and as fun

02:15:10.080 --> 02:15:14.940
as they are, the most popular stories aren’t
always the most unique or interesting.

02:15:14.940 --> 02:15:20.280
And if you peer deeper underneath the surface,
you can always find kernels of truth in the

02:15:20.280 --> 02:15:21.780
most commonplace of legends.

02:15:21.780 --> 02:15:28.740
For example, what’s commonly referred to
as bigfoot, or sasquatch, is actually SCP-1000,

02:15:28.740 --> 02:15:34.200
a super-intelligent, prehistoric race of ape
creatures known as the Children of the Night,

02:15:34.200 --> 02:15:39.540
who were slaughtered by early humans and forced
to hide from the world in order to preserve

02:15:39.540 --> 02:15:40.320
their species.

02:15:40.320 --> 02:15:42.060
A cursed object or location?

02:15:42.060 --> 02:15:47.700
The Foundation deals with those all of the
time, and stories of ghosts are as commonplace

02:15:47.700 --> 02:15:51.120
in the anomalous world as they are in the
ordinary one.

02:15:51.120 --> 02:15:57.180
But what about an anomaly that utilizes urban
legends to further its own nefarious goals?

02:15:57.180 --> 02:16:00.600
One that’s lifeblood is localized to a single
area?

02:16:00.600 --> 02:16:03.660
Today on SCP Explained, we’re going to be&nbsp;

02:16:03.660 --> 02:16:08.400
talking about SCP-3640, an&nbsp;
anomaly that capitalizes

02:16:08.400 --> 02:16:12.000
on the interest and intrigue those urban legends
generate.

02:16:12.000 --> 02:16:14.940
Specifically those in the state of Florida.

02:16:14.940 --> 02:16:20.280
We already talked about the variety of weird
and creepy stories the state calls its own,

02:16:20.280 --> 02:16:22.320
but what else is Florida known for?

02:16:22.320 --> 02:16:23.280
Tourism?

02:16:23.280 --> 02:16:24.720
Retirement communities?

02:16:24.720 --> 02:16:26.100
Beautiful, summer weather?

02:16:26.100 --> 02:16:30.180
Slightly crazy individuals making news headlines
for ridiculous reasons?

02:16:30.180 --> 02:16:31.800
How about Disney?

02:16:31.800 --> 02:16:37.740
That’s right, the state of Florida is known
for Walt Disney World, the granddaddy of all

02:16:37.740 --> 02:16:42.599
theme parks that brings in millions of tourist
dollars annually, and the hub for some of

02:16:42.600 --> 02:16:45.840
the most iconic characters and stories in
the world.

02:16:45.840 --> 02:16:50.160
If you’ve ever been to Disney World, then
you know about the costumed characters that

02:16:50.160 --> 02:16:50.939
roam the park.

02:16:50.939 --> 02:16:56.820
Silent, mascot costume renditions of your
favorite TV and movie characters, posing for

02:16:56.820 --> 02:16:58.799
pictures and having fun with children.

02:16:58.800 --> 02:17:01.380
The park is practically infested with them.

02:17:01.380 --> 02:17:03.120
They seem inescapable!

02:17:03.120 --> 02:17:09.000
It’s pretty understandable that some people
are unsettled by mascots, they can sometimes

02:17:09.000 --> 02:17:10.380
be downright creepy.

02:17:10.380 --> 02:17:17.460
With those unmoving expressions, giant heads,
unnatural movements, and the faces of familiar

02:17:17.460 --> 02:17:23.160
fictional characters, in the right context,
a mascot can be just as scary as any horror

02:17:23.160 --> 02:17:25.680
movie monster or urban legend could ever be.

02:17:25.680 --> 02:17:27.540
Here’s a situation for you.

02:17:27.540 --> 02:17:32.880
You just landed at a Florida airport, you’re
ready to go to Disney World and enjoy a vacation

02:17:32.880 --> 02:17:37.439
after you’ve been worked to exhaustion as
a junior researcher at the SCP Foundation.

02:17:37.439 --> 02:17:41.759
You want to get familiar with the state, but
you’re trying to cut down on your phone

02:17:41.760 --> 02:17:42.300
usage.

02:17:42.300 --> 02:17:47.220
After all, you’re on vacation, why not do
things the old fashioned way and unplug from

02:17:47.220 --> 02:17:47.880
the electronics?

02:17:47.880 --> 02:17:51.120
You spot a brochure rack in the distance,
perfect!

02:17:51.120 --> 02:17:54.180
A paper hub for everything tourist-y in the
area.

02:17:54.180 --> 02:17:59.760
Among the hundreds of jet skiing courses,
beach information, and mini golf pamphlets,

02:17:59.760 --> 02:18:03.000
one brochure in particular stands out to you.

02:18:03.000 --> 02:18:07.979
Maybe it’s your background in the anomalous,
but you just can’t help yourself from picking

02:18:07.979 --> 02:18:10.919
up a booklet on Florida’s urban legends.

02:18:10.920 --> 02:18:15.540
Knowing what’s behind the curtain, working
for the SCP Foundation, really makes these

02:18:15.540 --> 02:18:17.100
types of things more amusing.

02:18:17.100 --> 02:18:21.300
You’ve seen how the sausage was made, and
it’s a lot more terrifying than anything

02:18:21.300 --> 02:18:22.620
known to the general public.

02:18:22.620 --> 02:18:27.420
Heck, you know for a fact that the organization
you work for has more likely than not covered

02:18:27.420 --> 02:18:31.020
up most of the actual incidents that inspired
these local legends.

02:18:31.020 --> 02:18:37.200
Nonetheless, you pick up the brochure, interested
in the self-guided tour of Florida’s paranormal

02:18:37.200 --> 02:18:41.160
hotspots, and you’re impressed to find that
this booklet has it all.

02:18:41.160 --> 02:18:45.780
Everything from Skunk Apes to a cursed doll,
it’s all in here.

02:18:45.780 --> 02:18:48.780
You chuckle, and tuck the pamphlet underneath
your arm.

02:18:48.780 --> 02:18:53.880
But little do you know, you’re about to
experience something more horrifying than

02:18:53.880 --> 02:18:55.800
any urban legend could ever be.

02:18:55.800 --> 02:19:00.479
You see, if you paid attention to your Foundation
briefings before you left the state for Florida,

02:19:00.479 --> 02:19:02.820
you would know that any Foundation personnel&nbsp;

02:19:02.820 --> 02:19:05.460
who encounter tourist&nbsp;
brochure pamphlets advertising

02:19:05.460 --> 02:19:10.080
self-guided paranormal tours in Florida are
to bring said pamphlets to the Foundation’s

02:19:10.080 --> 02:19:11.220
attention immediately.

02:19:11.220 --> 02:19:17.760
Mobile Task Force Lambda-12, nicknamed “Pest
Control”, is primed on-demand for incidents

02:19:17.760 --> 02:19:19.140
related to these brochurces.

02:19:19.140 --> 02:19:20.160
Why?

02:19:20.160 --> 02:19:28.260
Because they’re a part of a phenomenon categorized
by the SCP Foundation as SCP-3640.

02:19:28.260 --> 02:19:31.200
But what is SCP-3640?

02:19:31.200 --> 02:19:36.359
Why is something as innocuous and fun as a
paranormal travel brochure an object of high

02:19:36.359 --> 02:19:38.160
interest for the SCP Foundation?

02:19:38.160 --> 02:19:43.200
Well, you, someone who should have maybe listened
to the regional briefing conferences back

02:19:43.200 --> 02:19:48.179
at Site-19 before you left on your vacation,
are about to find out.

02:19:48.180 --> 02:19:52.979
After pursuing your booklet and ruminating
over the numerous locations at your disposal,

02:19:52.979 --> 02:19:56.459
you decide to visit one after you get settled
into your hotel.

02:19:56.460 --> 02:20:01.800
After all, you’re about to experience a
week of family-friend fun at the House of

02:20:01.800 --> 02:20:05.820
Mouse, why not partake in a little horror
just to get the blood pumping?

02:20:05.820 --> 02:20:10.679
A bit of living life on the edge before the
scariest thing you have to deal with is a

02:20:10.680 --> 02:20:15.180
$10 bottle of water and a three hour waiting
line to ride that giant golf ball.

02:20:15.180 --> 02:20:20.520
You drive all the way out to the location
the pamphlet specified, a bridge by the name

02:20:20.520 --> 02:20:24.780
of Sunshine Skyway, located right outside
of Tampa Bay.

02:20:24.780 --> 02:20:29.219
Visiting the bridge at night might also get
you a visit from a mysterious and beautiful

02:20:29.220 --> 02:20:34.920
hitchhiker woman, who stands on the side of
the bridge and attempts to flag down cars.

02:20:34.920 --> 02:20:39.359
If you happen to take her in, she’ll begin
to weep, growing progressively louder and

02:20:39.359 --> 02:20:43.080
louder in her screaming and crying until you
reach the other side of the bridge.

02:20:43.080 --> 02:20:48.059
And when the driver turns back to ask her
what’s wrong, the woman will have vanished

02:20:48.060 --> 02:20:48.899
without a trace.

02:20:48.899 --> 02:20:50.580
Sounds like a fun time, right?

02:20:50.580 --> 02:20:51.960
Maybe you can find her.

02:20:51.960 --> 02:20:57.000
Heck, maybe she’s single and interested
in an enthusiastic and kind junior researcher

02:20:57.000 --> 02:20:58.319
of the SCP Foundation?

02:20:58.319 --> 02:21:03.059
You would never contain her, you’d promise,
having to raise your voice over the sounds

02:21:03.060 --> 02:21:05.399
of her weeping and crying in the backseat
of your car.

02:21:05.399 --> 02:21:07.200
Or, maybe not.

02:21:07.200 --> 02:21:12.660
This vacation time outside of the lab is making
you think some strange, strange stuff.

02:21:12.660 --> 02:21:18.359
Whatever the case is, you want to see a ghost
girl, so you make your way over to the Sunshine

02:21:18.359 --> 02:21:21.660
Skyway at 11 at night, just like the pamphlet
specified.

02:21:21.660 --> 02:21:26.639
The bridge is strangely empty, especially
for what’s usually a crowded stretch of

02:21:26.640 --> 02:21:26.939
the road.

02:21:26.939 --> 02:21:30.419
In fact, now that you realize it, there’s
no one else here.

02:21:30.420 --> 02:21:35.880
Just you, your car, the black night sky, and
the sound of your humming engine.

02:21:35.880 --> 02:21:41.160
Well, up the road you go, looking for this
supposed ghost hitchhiker.

02:21:41.160 --> 02:21:45.780
The Skyway is quite the drive, and the longer
you ride, the less safe you feel.

02:21:45.780 --> 02:21:47.460
But you’re fine, right?

02:21:47.460 --> 02:21:51.359
It’s a very popular bridge, driven by thousands
of people every day and night.

02:21:51.359 --> 02:21:56.099
It just so happens to be completely empty
at an ordinary time of night, and that you

02:21:56.100 --> 02:22:00.359
can see the dark outline of a figure in the
distance, standing in the middle of the road.

02:22:00.359 --> 02:22:05.880
As you drive closer and closer, you start
to make out the figure a bit more.

02:22:05.880 --> 02:22:13.500
A circular head, a tall, wide body, and two
more circles on top of that round, ball head.

02:22:13.500 --> 02:22:20.340
Closer, a little closer, and… wait, is that-
There’s absolutely no way that’s who you

02:22:20.340 --> 02:22:20.939
think it is.

02:22:20.939 --> 02:22:24.120
Is that a Mickey Mouse costume standing in
the middle of the road?

02:22:24.120 --> 02:22:27.899
It apparently is, and it seems like it’s
not getting out of the way.

02:22:27.899 --> 02:22:32.519
You honk your horn, but the overgrown rat
doesn’t listen, it’s still standing there,

02:22:32.520 --> 02:22:33.600
unmoving.

02:22:33.600 --> 02:22:34.680
You slow down.

02:22:34.680 --> 02:22:39.177
You know what Disney’s legal team is capable
of and you are absolutely not going to go

02:22:39.177 --> 02:22:43.319
to jail for running over Mickey Mouse, so
if he’s not moving out of the way, you will

02:22:43.319 --> 02:22:44.040
instead.

02:22:44.040 --> 02:22:49.080
You try to maneuver around the stationary
mascot, but suddenly, out of nowhere, the

02:22:49.080 --> 02:22:52.080
thing leaps fifteen feet into the air and
jumps onto your hood.

02:22:52.080 --> 02:22:57.300
You scream as the Mickey mascot scitters across
the roof of your car, clawing and tearing

02:22:57.300 --> 02:22:58.620
at the sunroof, trying to get in.

02:22:58.620 --> 02:23:02.340
You push your foot on the gas as hard as you
can, with enough force to propel Mickey from

02:23:02.340 --> 02:23:03.899
the roof, but it’s not enough.

02:23:03.899 --> 02:23:08.519
The mascot hits the ground, but immediately
gets back up and starts running after your

02:23:08.520 --> 02:23:08.760
car.

02:23:08.760 --> 02:23:14.100
Almost instantaneously, it catches up to your
car again, and uses its strength to pry off

02:23:14.100 --> 02:23:18.240
the door on the driver’s side of the car,
exposing you and causing you to lose control

02:23:18.240 --> 02:23:18.960
of your vehicle.

02:23:18.960 --> 02:23:24.420
You swerve, crashing into the side of the
bridge and banging your head off of the steering

02:23:24.420 --> 02:23:24.540
wheel.

02:23:24.540 --> 02:23:29.580
You never thought your life would result in
death by Mickey Mouse, but the rapidly approaching

02:23:29.580 --> 02:23:32.280
costumed creature seems to be saying otherwise.

02:23:32.280 --> 02:23:37.979
The Mickey creature bends down, and uses both
of its gloved hands to grab you from your

02:23:37.979 --> 02:23:42.839
car seat with enough force to break the seatbelt
and give you minor whiplash from being flung

02:23:42.840 --> 02:23:44.399
into the air so quickly.

02:23:44.399 --> 02:23:49.439
This is it, you know it’s over, and you
don’t even know what’s going on or why

02:23:49.439 --> 02:23:50.280
this is happening.

02:23:50.280 --> 02:23:54.599
You’re just another victim of something
you don’t understand, like the countless

02:23:54.600 --> 02:23:56.460
dead you spent your life researching.

02:23:56.460 --> 02:23:57.899
Or so you think.

02:23:57.899 --> 02:24:02.759
Just when you assume that it’s all over,
a shot rings out from across the bridge, and

02:24:02.760 --> 02:24:07.380
you see a salvo of bullets pepper Mickey Mouse’s
back, carefully missing you with impressively

02:24:07.380 --> 02:24:08.340
accurate precision.

02:24:08.340 --> 02:24:13.260
Mickey drops you, banging your head on the
concrete, and runs towards where the bullets

02:24:13.260 --> 02:24:13.859
are coming from.

02:24:13.859 --> 02:24:18.120
Several armored, heavily armed soldiers appear
from the side of the bridge and circle the

02:24:18.120 --> 02:24:18.300
mouse.

02:24:18.300 --> 02:24:22.020
They fire again, but it has little effect
on the mascot.

02:24:22.020 --> 02:24:25.319
Once again, he lunges forward, knocking a
soldier off his feet.

02:24:25.319 --> 02:24:29.280
The mascot dashes off into the distance, leaping
over the side of the bridge.

02:24:29.280 --> 02:24:34.439
Though no splash is heard in the water below,
you don’t see the mascot landing or even

02:24:34.439 --> 02:24:35.099
escaping.

02:24:35.100 --> 02:24:38.160
It’s like he was never there in the first
place.

02:24:38.160 --> 02:24:43.080
But at least it’s gone now, and you have
these unknown soldiers to thank for your,

02:24:43.080 --> 02:24:45.180
wait, is that an SCP Foundation logo?

02:24:45.180 --> 02:24:47.640
Oh no, they’re Foundation Task Force operatives.

02:24:47.640 --> 02:24:51.600
Before you’re able to fully regain your
senses, you can already hear the Task Force

02:24:51.600 --> 02:24:54.960
captain telling his underling to prep you
for amnestics and an interview.

02:24:54.960 --> 02:24:59.580
The soldier approaches you, and you’re thankfully
able to muster out a few choice words.

02:24:59.580 --> 02:25:01.559
Namely, “Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait!

02:25:01.560 --> 02:25:02.580
I’m with you guys!

02:25:02.580 --> 02:25:03.720
I’m a junior researcher!”

02:25:03.720 --> 02:25:06.000
The captain pauses and laughs to himself.

02:25:07.020 --> 02:25:08.220
What are the odds?

02:25:08.220 --> 02:25:12.479
After you’re processed and taken to the
nearest facility, where your identity as a

02:25:12.479 --> 02:25:17.040
card carrying member of the SCP Foundation
is confirmed, you’re let in on what exactly

02:25:17.040 --> 02:25:18.780
it was that you just saw back there.

02:25:18.780 --> 02:25:25.559
As it turns out, you had an encounter with
SCP-3640, an anomaly centering around a set

02:25:25.560 --> 02:25:31.080
of travel brochures that advertise self-guided
tours of all of Florida’s paranormal hotspots.

02:25:31.080 --> 02:25:36.120
If someone reads the brochure and goes to
a location at a set time, just like you did,

02:25:36.120 --> 02:25:42.059
they’ll be preyed upon by a mysterious,
predatory entity or set of entities that resemble

02:25:42.060 --> 02:25:46.080
costumed mascot characters owned by the Walt
Disney Company.

02:25:46.080 --> 02:25:51.780
Mickey, Donald, Goofy, the task force captain
explains that they’re all there, and they’re

02:25:51.780 --> 02:25:52.979
all over the state of Florida.

02:25:52.979 --> 02:25:55.439
Hundreds of mascots, maybe more.

02:25:55.439 --> 02:26:00.479
They’re fast, dangerous, and the Foundation
knows remarkably little about them.

02:26:00.479 --> 02:26:05.759
Including how they grow, reproduce, or even
consume their prey.

02:26:05.760 --> 02:26:10.080
All of the known hotspots advertised in the
pamphlet are routinely watched by members

02:26:10.080 --> 02:26:15.780
of the Pest Control mobile task force, where
operatives are authorized to neutralize SCP-3640

02:26:15.780 --> 02:26:17.340
entities with lethal force.

02:26:17.340 --> 02:26:20.220
Which is how that Task&nbsp;
Force was able to thankfully&nbsp;

02:26:20.220 --> 02:26:22.859
show up at the right moment and save your

02:26:22.859 --> 02:26:23.100
life.

02:26:23.100 --> 02:26:29.880
SCP-3640 only attack those who read the brochures,
and haven’t been seen being hostile or hunting

02:26:29.880 --> 02:26:32.100
outside of the areas specified by the pamphlet.

02:26:32.100 --> 02:26:38.280
After you recollect yourself and thank them,
the captain hands you a file briefing on SCP-3640,

02:26:38.280 --> 02:26:42.719
gives you a stern warning, and tells you to
familiarize yourself with it before you leave

02:26:42.720 --> 02:26:43.500
the facility.

02:26:43.500 --> 02:26:46.020
What a way to start your vacation, you think.

02:26:46.020 --> 02:26:50.340
Just when you thought you were able to escape
the daily horrors of working for the Foundation,

02:26:50.340 --> 02:26:52.740
you stumble onto an anomaly yourself.

02:26:52.740 --> 02:26:57.479
But you undoubtedly have more questions about
SCP-3640.

02:26:57.479 --> 02:27:02.160
After all, anyone would after witnessing as
weird and strange an anomaly as that in the

02:27:02.160 --> 02:27:02.340
wild.

02:27:02.340 --> 02:27:08.280
You ask the captain why the Foundation hasn’t
captured an SCP-3640 instance, especially

02:27:08.280 --> 02:27:10.019
if they’re so common in the Florida area.

02:27:10.020 --> 02:27:15.120
He sits down, sighs, and explains that the
Foundation did try, awhile back.

02:27:15.120 --> 02:27:20.580
It was a standard D-Class test, held in the
St. Johns River, the location of a supposed

02:27:20.580 --> 02:27:21.720
“river monster”.

02:27:21.720 --> 02:27:26.160
The D-Class personnel was dropped off at the
river bank and told to follow the instructions

02:27:26.160 --> 02:27:26.880
in the pamphlet.

02:27:26.880 --> 02:27:31.140
If they spotted a mascot, they were to shoot
at it with a tranquilizer gun.

02:27:31.140 --> 02:27:35.399
After dredging through the river for a few
minutes and being distracted by a neat looking

02:27:35.399 --> 02:27:41.639
alligator, the D-Class eventually came head
to head with none other than Donald Duck himself,

02:27:41.640 --> 02:27:45.840
who emerged from the river and immediately
began moving towards the D-Class.

02:27:45.840 --> 02:27:50.939
The D-Class naturally freaked out completely,
and ran away from the scene, but Donald was

02:27:50.939 --> 02:27:52.080
simply too fast.

02:27:52.080 --> 02:27:57.120
Just when he thought he was safe, the Donald
mascot emerged from the shadows and knocked

02:27:57.120 --> 02:27:59.640
the camera and radio off of the D-Class’s
head.

02:27:59.640 --> 02:28:03.600
There were sounds of a struggle, but the D-Class
never established contact again.

02:28:03.600 --> 02:28:08.520
However, his subdermal tracking transmitters
continued to operate, and before they went

02:28:08.520 --> 02:28:13.020
offline completely, they luckily detected
the location of the D-Class’s body.

02:28:13.020 --> 02:28:16.800
It was just outside of the EPCOT amusement
park.

02:28:16.800 --> 02:28:20.100
Engaged by the captain’s story, you ask
him what happened next.

02:28:20.100 --> 02:28:24.120
Surely, the Foundation launched an assault
on EPCOT to figure out what happened to the

02:28:24.120 --> 02:28:24.840
D-Class, right?

02:28:24.840 --> 02:28:28.200
The captain grunts, and tells you that the
rest is classified.

02:28:28.200 --> 02:28:29.760
But you’re not satisfied.

02:28:29.760 --> 02:28:33.780
You’re refusing to move until you figure
out what happened to this D-Class.

02:28:33.780 --> 02:28:39.540
The captain rolls his eyes, and perhaps feeling
sorry for you, decides to tell you the rest

02:28:39.540 --> 02:28:40.439
of the story.

02:28:40.439 --> 02:28:45.779
Him and his team were deployed just outside
of the EPCOT theme park, right next to a one

02:28:45.780 --> 02:28:49.380
story, concrete hut, where the D-Class’s
location was tracked.

02:28:49.380 --> 02:28:53.700
They were equipped with heavy arms, a net
launcher, and a flamethrower, all perfect

02:28:53.700 --> 02:28:56.040
weapons for subduing these deadly mascots.

02:28:56.040 --> 02:29:01.140
While Lambda-12 was typically used to hunting
anomalous bugs and pests, they figured that

02:29:01.140 --> 02:29:05.700
hunting down Donald Duck and Minnie Mouse
was more or less the same thing, when you

02:29:05.700 --> 02:29:07.740
squint really hard and pretend that they have
wings.

02:29:07.740 --> 02:29:12.479
The task force broke into the hut, revealing
it to be a maintenance shed with a mysterious

02:29:12.479 --> 02:29:13.979
trap door in the middle of the floor.

02:29:13.979 --> 02:29:19.139
Underneath, a ladder led to a tunnel system,
similar to the ones built underneath the Disney

02:29:19.140 --> 02:29:22.260
Parks that the employees use to get around
from park to park.

02:29:22.260 --> 02:29:27.540
The team spotted several dressing rooms and
storage rooms, all empty and devoid of any

02:29:27.540 --> 02:29:27.660
life.

02:29:27.660 --> 02:29:32.819
After some exploration, the team followed
a low rumbling noise to a closed door.

02:29:32.819 --> 02:29:39.120
They slowly opened it, revealing an abandoned
boiler room, with a white mascot costume at

02:29:39.120 --> 02:29:42.720
the foot of the boiler, curled up around an
unknown object.

02:29:42.720 --> 02:29:47.819
An operative approached the costume and poked
it with her rifle, identifying it as an empty

02:29:47.819 --> 02:29:49.200
Daisy Duck costume.

02:29:49.200 --> 02:29:54.120
The team examined it further, and found a
human arm bone inside the suit.

02:29:54.120 --> 02:29:58.260
Disgusting, to be sure, but nothing the task
force hadn’t seen before.

02:29:58.260 --> 02:30:02.700
They turned over the suit to examine the object
it was curled around, discovering it to be

02:30:02.700 --> 02:30:05.639
a purple, plastic egg, with an embryo inside.

02:30:05.640 --> 02:30:08.760
Scattered across the floor were more eggshells.

02:30:08.760 --> 02:30:13.319
The squad gathered them, as well as the bones
of the D-Class in the costume, to bring back

02:30:13.319 --> 02:30:14.040
to the facility.

02:30:14.040 --> 02:30:19.019
Suddenly, the task force heard noises in the
distance, and assumed an attack formation.

02:30:19.020 --> 02:30:24.000
They noticed the floor of the entrance they
came in was now covered in dark fluid and

02:30:24.000 --> 02:30:25.140
polyester stuffing.

02:30:25.140 --> 02:30:29.460
The trail of liquid exactly matched their
path of infiltration into the tunnel.

02:30:29.460 --> 02:30:34.200
After determining the situation to be safe,
the squad carefully left the tunnel the way

02:30:34.200 --> 02:30:37.439
they came, bringing the costume and the egg
with them.

02:30:37.439 --> 02:30:42.780
After several weeks, the egg hatched into
a miniature stuffed donald duck toy.

02:30:42.780 --> 02:30:45.120
The Foundation dissected it, discovering it&nbsp;

02:30:45.120 --> 02:30:48.240
to contain a plastic&nbsp;
endoskeleton and a rudimentary

02:30:48.240 --> 02:30:50.580
polyester stuffing muscular system inside.

02:30:50.580 --> 02:30:53.819
And that was everything the captain had to
say.

02:30:53.819 --> 02:31:00.179
There was never any other leads on the SCP-3640
anomaly, just strangeness and inexplicable

02:31:00.180 --> 02:31:03.180
inability to capture or understand the mascots.

02:31:03.180 --> 02:31:07.560
You thanked the captain for not only saving
you, but explaining what was going on.

02:31:07.560 --> 02:31:12.420
Before you left the facility to go back to
your regular, foundation-less vacation, you

02:31:12.420 --> 02:31:15.420
took another glance at the document the Captain
handed to you.

02:31:15.420 --> 02:31:21.600
On the back page was a chilling letter, dated
from 1979, written to Florida governor Reuben

02:31:21.600 --> 02:31:23.460
Askew by the Walt Disney Company.

02:31:23.460 --> 02:31:24.300
It read:

02:31:25.200 --> 02:31:27.899
The Walt Disney Company thanks you for your&nbsp;

02:31:27.899 --> 02:31:30.960
cooperation in this matter&nbsp;
regarding the unlicensed

02:31:30.960 --> 02:31:32.700
Walt Disney character operators.

02:31:32.700 --> 02:31:37.380
Please pass along the following information,
collected by the outstanding men and women

02:31:37.380 --> 02:31:41.280
of the City of Orlando's Police Department,
to the Florida National Guard:

02:31:41.280 --> 02:31:47.099
If a character is spotted, call to get its
attention and then rapidly flash your flashlights

02:31:47.100 --> 02:31:47.939
at the costume.

02:31:47.939 --> 02:31:50.639
If it does not flinch, fire on sight.

02:31:50.640 --> 02:31:55.560
Aim at the head if possible; else, aim at
the knees to disable them and then finish

02:31:55.560 --> 02:31:56.819
them off with head shots.

02:31:56.819 --> 02:31:59.819
Body shots have been shown to lack effectiveness.

02:31:59.819 --> 02:32:02.519
Deceased characters are to be incinerated.

02:32:02.520 --> 02:32:05.220
No other means of disposal are advised.

02:32:05.220 --> 02:32:10.200
We are currently pursuing alternative legal
means of shutting down these unlicensed operators

02:32:10.200 --> 02:32:13.200
and hope to achieve a settlement within the
end of the year.

02:32:13.200 --> 02:32:16.319
Cordially yours,
The Walt Disney Company

02:32:16.319 --> 02:32:22.080
Take a brief moment to think back to your
younger years, spending long, tiresome hours

02:32:22.080 --> 02:32:26.640
trapped in a classroom, waiting to hear the
noise of that final bell of the day.

02:32:26.640 --> 02:32:32.700
That sound meant freedom, the end of another
grueling six hours at your desk, and the chance

02:32:32.700 --> 02:32:35.580
to get back to the warm sanctuary of home.

02:32:35.580 --> 02:32:40.500
If you were lucky, you might not have had
to go far to get back to the safety and security

02:32:40.500 --> 02:32:44.819
of being in your parents’ house, living
close enough to the school would mean you

02:32:44.819 --> 02:32:46.979
could easily walk home when the day was through.

02:32:46.979 --> 02:32:48.299
But your classmates?

02:32:48.300 --> 02:32:53.760
Well, they weren’t all as lucky, some of
them had miles to travel, all the way across

02:32:53.760 --> 02:32:54.240
town even.

02:32:54.240 --> 02:32:58.920
Fortunately, though, the school bus would
always be waiting outside at the end of each

02:32:58.920 --> 02:33:02.280
day, ready to take a gaggle of rowdy kids
back home.

02:33:02.280 --> 02:33:06.840
And if you were one of those kids that had
to take the bus, you’ll know that the trip

02:33:06.840 --> 02:33:09.240
home after school was hardly a calm drive.

02:33:09.240 --> 02:33:14.519
Paper planes and spitballs firing from all
directions, wads of chewing gum stuck to the

02:33:14.520 --> 02:33:19.439
undersides of the seats, other kids all around
you screaming and yelling at the top of their

02:33:19.439 --> 02:33:19.800
lungs.

02:33:19.800 --> 02:33:21.840
Still, it could be worse, right?

02:33:21.840 --> 02:33:27.660
No, trust us, it could be much, much worse
than you can ever imagine.

02:33:27.660 --> 02:33:33.420
What if, one day, the bus that picked you
up from school wasn’t a bus at all?

02:33:33.420 --> 02:33:38.100
What if, instead, it was SCP-2086?

02:33:38.100 --> 02:33:41.640
Picture this: One day, you get put in detention
at school.

02:33:41.640 --> 02:33:46.800
Maybe you were disrupting a class or got caught
spraying graffiti on the outside wall of the

02:33:46.800 --> 02:33:47.100
gym.

02:33:47.100 --> 02:33:51.540
Whatever the reason, we’re sure you think
it’s unfair that you got held back after

02:33:51.540 --> 02:33:54.420
school, after everyone else had already gone
home.

02:33:54.420 --> 02:33:58.080
But you do your time, until finally, you’re
told you can leave.

02:33:58.080 --> 02:34:02.640
Problem is, your house is on the other side
of town, and you’ve already missed the bus.

02:34:02.640 --> 02:34:06.180
You make your way off the campus, down the
nearest street.

02:34:06.180 --> 02:34:09.359
Maybe there’s a city bus you can catch that’ll
get you home.

02:34:09.359 --> 02:34:14.939
As you stroll away from your school, you realize
that the nearest bus stop, the first one on

02:34:14.939 --> 02:34:18.179
the route home, seems to be further away than
you remember it being.

02:34:18.180 --> 02:34:22.859
Must just be the exhaustion of a long day
getting the better of you, playing tricks

02:34:22.859 --> 02:34:23.460
on your mind.

02:34:23.460 --> 02:34:26.939
It’s not like someone could move the bus
stop, right?

02:34:26.939 --> 02:34:31.319
Finally reaching the stop, you notice lights
coming down the street after a few moments

02:34:31.319 --> 02:34:32.280
of waiting quietly.

02:34:32.280 --> 02:34:34.859
A late bus, just like you hoped for.

02:34:34.859 --> 02:34:39.299
It pulls up next to the stop, the doors folding
open to allow you on board.

02:34:39.300 --> 02:34:41.939
It’s totally empty, save for the driver.

02:34:41.939 --> 02:34:45.359
But straight away, you notice there’s something
odd about him.

02:34:45.359 --> 02:34:51.120
He seems drained of color, his movements are
weird, more like a puppet on strings than

02:34:51.120 --> 02:34:53.399
an actual living, breathing human being.

02:34:53.399 --> 02:34:58.019
Now you think about it, if it wasn’t for
the fact he was clearly moving, driving the

02:34:58.020 --> 02:35:00.780
bus, you might assume that he was a corpse.

02:35:00.780 --> 02:35:03.300
Then again, maybe he just had a long day too.

02:35:03.300 --> 02:35:07.979
Taking a seat, you try not to think about
it, and stare out of the window in boredom.

02:35:07.979 --> 02:35:13.259
You watch as the route takes you past stop
after stop, all of them empty just like the

02:35:13.260 --> 02:35:13.920
bus itself.

02:35:13.920 --> 02:35:16.380
But then something unexpected happens.

02:35:16.380 --> 02:35:20.939
You’ve ridden the bus to and from school
so many times before that you can’t help

02:35:20.939 --> 02:35:24.599
but notice when, for some reason, it takes
a wrong turn.

02:35:24.600 --> 02:35:27.720
Looking out the window you know you aren’t
mistaken.

02:35:27.720 --> 02:35:32.700
The driver has changed direction, instead
of heading towards the nearest stop to home,

02:35:32.700 --> 02:35:35.939
he’s taken the bus towards the furthest
edge of town.

02:35:35.939 --> 02:35:40.799
Desperately you try yelling at him, asking
why he’s taken the wrong turn, but the driver

02:35:40.800 --> 02:35:44.220
stays still, as if he can’t even hear what
you’re saying.

02:35:44.220 --> 02:35:46.380
That’s when you notice the smell.

02:35:46.380 --> 02:35:52.500
You didn’t catch it before, but now it’s
all around you, filling the air inside the

02:35:52.500 --> 02:35:52.680
bus.

02:35:52.680 --> 02:35:57.899
It’s almost like the scent of disinfectant;
the bus now smells the same way a hospital

02:35:57.899 --> 02:35:58.439
does.

02:35:58.439 --> 02:35:59.879
But that’s not all.

02:35:59.880 --> 02:36:06.000
The more you breathe it in, the more you feel
yourself starting to get woozy, arms and legs

02:36:06.000 --> 02:36:06.780
getting heavier.

02:36:06.780 --> 02:36:10.859
Everything around you feels as if it’s spinning
uncontrollably.

02:36:10.859 --> 02:36:16.019
Out of the windows, you can just about make
out the sight of a junkyard, blurring in and

02:36:16.020 --> 02:36:16.680
out of focus.

02:36:16.680 --> 02:36:22.740
It’s meant to be abandoned, and yet you’re
sure you can see movement: Massive, indeterminate

02:36:22.740 --> 02:36:24.420
shapes shifting around in the dark.

02:36:24.420 --> 02:36:28.920
Finally, your vision goes dark and you fall
unconscious onto the floor of the bus.

02:36:28.920 --> 02:36:32.040
Only you were never on the bus to begin with.

02:36:32.040 --> 02:36:37.319
No, although you didn’t know it, you were
prey to something that just looked like a

02:36:37.319 --> 02:36:40.019
bus: SCP-2086.

02:36:40.020 --> 02:36:44.700
And now that it’s caught you, you’ll never
see the light of day again.

02:36:44.700 --> 02:36:50.099
Now, SCP-2086 doesn’t just refer to a single
creature, not by a long shot.

02:36:50.100 --> 02:36:55.800
It’s the designation given to an entire
species of arthropods; think lobsters, crabs,

02:36:55.800 --> 02:36:58.920
and spiders, or insects like centipedes and
millipedes.

02:36:58.920 --> 02:37:01.260
Only much bigger.

02:37:01.260 --> 02:37:06.960
To the untrained eye, and depending on when
you look, an instance of SCP-2086 will normally

02:37:06.960 --> 02:37:12.240
look like any ordinary public transport vehicle,
of any make and model, or belonging to any

02:37:12.240 --> 02:37:13.859
company or transit authority.

02:37:13.859 --> 02:37:18.540
Usually, though, they look like regular old
buses, at least while they’re out foraging

02:37:18.540 --> 02:37:19.080
for food.

02:37:19.080 --> 02:37:25.319
When born, an SCP-2086 specimen will grow
to full juvenile size within a week, usually

02:37:25.319 --> 02:37:27.420
weighing two hundred kilograms or less.

02:37:27.420 --> 02:37:33.720
Fully matured adult instances, however, can
weigh approximately seventeen thousand kilograms.

02:37:33.720 --> 02:37:38.340
The adults are the ones that go out foraging,
leaving the nest to collect food to then bring

02:37:38.340 --> 02:37:41.100
back to the juvenile SCP-2086s.

02:37:41.100 --> 02:37:44.939
And by food, we of course mean humans.

02:37:44.939 --> 02:37:50.879
While out on the roads, matured SCP-2086 creatures
are practically identical to the auto vehicles

02:37:50.880 --> 02:37:52.020
that form their bodies.

02:37:52.020 --> 02:37:57.120
But the materials that this disguise is made
from – the steel, plastic, wood, and glass

02:37:57.120 --> 02:38:01.979
– they’re all actually comprised of specialized
chitin, the kind of outer shell you’ll find

02:38:01.979 --> 02:38:03.540
on most arthropods.

02:38:03.540 --> 02:38:08.100
But underneath that outer shell, that’s
where you’ll find the real horror.

02:38:08.100 --> 02:38:13.439
Within the main chamber, beneath the flooring
of the bus’s long, inner portion, is stored

02:38:13.439 --> 02:38:17.580
the pulsing, beating heart of an SCP-2086
specimen.

02:38:17.580 --> 02:38:22.140
And we don’t mean that in a metaphorical
sense, if you were to lift up the floorboards

02:38:22.140 --> 02:38:27.000
of one of these bus-like creatures you’d
see its heart, along with other vital organs

02:38:27.000 --> 02:38:28.920
like the creature’s brain and stomach.

02:38:28.920 --> 02:38:33.300
What’s more, that figure in the front seat,
that you thought was a living, breathing bus

02:38:33.300 --> 02:38:37.140
driver, actually isn’t living or breathing,
not anymore.

02:38:37.140 --> 02:38:41.939
Preserved in a shellac substance that the
creature is able to produce, this driver is

02:38:41.939 --> 02:38:46.919
actually a human corpse, acting as a decoy
for SCP-2086s.

02:38:46.920 --> 02:38:52.979
From within the bus body, fibrous appendages
reach up into the corpse, almost like incredibly

02:38:52.979 --> 02:38:54.120
thin hairs.

02:38:54.120 --> 02:38:59.399
The creature can then use the cadaver essentially
as a puppet, a puppet with a dead person’s

02:38:59.399 --> 02:38:59.640
body.

02:38:59.640 --> 02:39:06.000
That’s how an SCP-2086 is able to move its
driver around, making it appear more lifelike

02:39:06.000 --> 02:39:07.740
so it can lure its prey aboard.

02:39:07.740 --> 02:39:12.719
Think of it like the bioluminescent light
that anglerfish use to tempt unsuspecting

02:39:12.720 --> 02:39:14.160
fish into their jaws.

02:39:14.160 --> 02:39:20.040
Same principle, but with a dramatically different
result when it comes to SCP-2086.

02:39:20.040 --> 02:39:24.720
But if you thought bus creatures with internal
organs under the floor and dead meat puppets

02:39:24.720 --> 02:39:29.880
in the driver’s seat weren’t creepy enough,
there’s still much more to SCP-2086s than

02:39:29.880 --> 02:39:30.660
meets the eye.

02:39:30.660 --> 02:39:35.760
For example, when they aren’t out foraging,
the adult creatures can unravel the roof of

02:39:35.760 --> 02:39:37.260
their bus-shaped outer shell.

02:39:37.260 --> 02:39:43.560
Underneath is a pair of wings, large enough
and strong enough to carry their entire, several

02:39:43.560 --> 02:39:46.620
thousand kilos of weight off the ground and
up into the air.

02:39:46.620 --> 02:39:47.700
As for eyes?

02:39:47.700 --> 02:39:53.399
The headlights at the front are, in actual
fact, bioluminescent optical organs, allowing

02:39:53.399 --> 02:39:56.219
the creatures to see their prey even in the
dark.

02:39:56.220 --> 02:39:57.899
Still not horrifying enough?

02:39:57.899 --> 02:40:00.960
Well, would knowing about their legs help?

02:40:00.960 --> 02:40:07.080
The wheels underneath an SCP-2086 specimen
are also capable of unraveling, forming long,

02:40:07.080 --> 02:40:09.780
grey, or black legs, like those of a spider.

02:40:09.780 --> 02:40:15.300
Yes, these are bus creatures with wings and
multi-jointed legs.

02:40:15.300 --> 02:40:18.120
These legs aren’t just big, clumsy appendages
either.

02:40:18.120 --> 02:40:21.540
Compared with other arthropods, SCP-2086s&nbsp;

02:40:21.540 --> 02:40:24.000
are able to use their limbs&nbsp;
to perform surprisingly

02:40:24.000 --> 02:40:27.000
intricate actions and finer&nbsp;
levels of manipulations.

02:40:27.000 --> 02:40:32.040
For instance, a number of specimens have been
observed in the wild, by the SCP Foundation,

02:40:32.040 --> 02:40:36.120
building shelters out of any materials that
they can find near their nesting ground.

02:40:36.120 --> 02:40:38.099
And where do they normally nest?

02:40:38.100 --> 02:40:42.479
Wherever there’s plenty of scrap metal,
and hardly any people to notice them.

02:40:42.479 --> 02:40:48.899
Junkyards are the preferred habitats of SCP-2086s,
and where they will normally establish their

02:40:48.899 --> 02:40:49.380
colonies.

02:40:49.380 --> 02:40:55.319
While the juveniles remain within the confines
of the colony, adult SCP-2086 specimens will

02:40:55.319 --> 02:40:56.519
leave to collect humans.

02:40:56.520 --> 02:41:01.200
Although, on occasion, the younger specimens
have been known to travel out from their nest

02:41:01.200 --> 02:41:04.500
and rearrange or relocate signposts for bus
stops.

02:41:04.500 --> 02:41:08.819
They then place them in a route that leads
back towards their nesting ground; it’s

02:41:08.819 --> 02:41:13.019
something worth remembering if your nearest
bus stop ever seems to be a little further

02:41:13.020 --> 02:41:15.240
away from the school than usual.

02:41:15.240 --> 02:41:17.099
Afterward, the older specimens will travel&nbsp;

02:41:17.100 --> 02:41:20.760
along the route laid out&nbsp;
by the juvenile SCP-2086s,

02:41:20.760 --> 02:41:25.620
picking up any human passengers that they
find waiting at the relocated bus stops.

02:41:25.620 --> 02:41:30.000
They have to choose their moments wisely,
with people boarding and disembarking from

02:41:30.000 --> 02:41:32.160
the bus usually every few stops.

02:41:32.160 --> 02:41:38.399
Once an SCP-2086 has as many humans on board
as it can carry, with the certainty it won’t

02:41:38.399 --> 02:41:43.139
lose any at the upcoming stop, it secretes
a substance similar to chloroform.

02:41:43.140 --> 02:41:49.080
This fills the inner chamber of the bus, causing
that noxious smell, like hospital disinfectant.

02:41:49.080 --> 02:41:54.000
The chloroform-like substance incapacitates
all the passengers on board, rendering them

02:41:54.000 --> 02:41:59.340
unconscious and readying them to be taken
back to the local SCP-2086 colony.

02:41:59.340 --> 02:42:04.859
Once the adult SCP-2086 has arrived at the
junkyard, the juveniles will descend on it.

02:42:04.859 --> 02:42:09.839
Given their much, much smaller size, they
will climb inside the mature specimen and

02:42:09.840 --> 02:42:13.740
forcibly remove each and every human passenger
it is carrying within.

02:42:13.740 --> 02:42:17.519
Then comes the truly nasty part: feeding time.

02:42:17.520 --> 02:42:23.220
Each juvenile SCP-2086 will force their captive
human through an orifice that is located under

02:42:23.220 --> 02:42:25.020
the front hood of their vehicle shell.

02:42:25.020 --> 02:42:30.120
This sphincter, a circular formation of muscle
that can expand and contract to perform a

02:42:30.120 --> 02:42:36.059
bodily function, is connected to where the
steering wheel is found on an adult SCP-2086.

02:42:36.060 --> 02:42:40.740
The younger creatures will push their human
prey through this sphincter, consuming them.

02:42:40.740 --> 02:42:45.300
Once this has occurred, those hairy appendages
in the driver’s seat will then latch onto

02:42:45.300 --> 02:42:50.640
the body of the now-dead human, piercing through
their skin, winding up and around their bones.

02:42:50.640 --> 02:42:56.040
These are the same fibrous hairs used to puppet
the deceased corpse and use it to lure others

02:42:56.040 --> 02:43:01.200
aboard the bus, but these appendages have
another function: they’re feeding tubes.

02:43:01.200 --> 02:43:07.200
They will drain every last drop of blood from
the SCP-2086’s prey, until the body is little

02:43:07.200 --> 02:43:08.460
more than a husk.

02:43:08.460 --> 02:43:12.840
At which point, the tubes inject a saline
solution directly into the cadaver.

02:43:12.840 --> 02:43:17.580
Afterwards, the inside of the bus fills with
that same substance that preserves the corpse,

02:43:17.580 --> 02:43:19.800
and the process is complete.

02:43:19.800 --> 02:43:25.380
As horrifying as these creatures are, one
of the few upsides of SCP-2086s is that they

02:43:25.380 --> 02:43:26.340
don’t live very long.

02:43:26.340 --> 02:43:31.260
Female specimens will reproduce after eight
days, and produce twenty offspring after this

02:43:31.260 --> 02:43:31.500
point.

02:43:31.500 --> 02:43:35.399
Each of these newborns reaches full maturity
and size in about a week.

02:43:35.399 --> 02:43:40.139
On average, SCP-2086s live for twelve to fifteen
days.

02:43:40.140 --> 02:43:45.840
Another net positive is, because of their
short lifespans, an SCP-2086 specimen doesn’t

02:43:45.840 --> 02:43:50.880
need to feed on a human more than once, as
the nutrients it absorbs as a juvenile are

02:43:50.880 --> 02:43:52.560
enough to sustain it through adulthood.

02:43:52.560 --> 02:43:59.040
Once it has matured, an SCP-2086 will go out
into the nearest city or town to forage for

02:43:59.040 --> 02:44:01.680
humans, providing food to the next generation.

02:44:01.680 --> 02:44:04.200
And so, the cycle continues.

02:44:04.200 --> 02:44:08.220
In the future, rather than take the bus, maybe
it’s safer to walk.

02:44:08.220 --> 02:44:12.899
It might mean the difference between you making
it home, or becoming food.

02:44:12.899 --> 02:44:14.939
October, 1988.

02:44:15.479 --> 02:44:21.000
SCP Foundation Agents Cyril Novak and Diana
Fischer had been dispatched to Austria’s

02:44:21.000 --> 02:44:26.280
capital city, Vienna, to investigate a series
of mysterious, unexplained disappearances.

02:44:26.280 --> 02:44:31.500
The Foundation was unsure if these events
were connected, or even anomalous in nature,

02:44:31.500 --> 02:44:36.720
but they had reason to believe that something
was lurking beneath the dark streets of Vienna.

02:44:36.720 --> 02:44:41.939
A Foundation operative embedded in law enforcement
informed the organization that the authorities

02:44:41.939 --> 02:44:46.859
were panicking, with an emphasis on withholding
information about these disappearances from

02:44:46.859 --> 02:44:48.479
the public and the media.

02:44:48.479 --> 02:44:54.000
Novak and Fischer conducted a survey of the
city, observing the streets at night and keeping

02:44:54.000 --> 02:44:56.760
a watchful eye on those who they deemed at-risk.

02:44:56.760 --> 02:45:00.540
It was the undesirables of society that were
disappearing in droves.

02:45:00.540 --> 02:45:04.019
Unsupervised children, vagrants, the homeless.

02:45:04.020 --> 02:45:10.080
All those that were indisposed, vulnerable,
and otherwise at risk of being forgotten by

02:45:10.080 --> 02:45:11.819
society were potential victims.

02:45:11.819 --> 02:45:18.059
According to several sources, these disappearances
were taking place near access points to the

02:45:18.060 --> 02:45:19.859
city’s subterranean infrastructure.

02:45:19.859 --> 02:45:23.460
Sewer holes, access tunnels, storm drains.

02:45:23.460 --> 02:45:27.240
Anywhere that led to the underground was a
potential risk-site.

02:45:27.240 --> 02:45:32.580
After a few days of standard exploration and
information gathering around Vienna, Novak

02:45:32.580 --> 02:45:36.479
and Fishcer moved on to interviews with law
enforcement and public officials.

02:45:36.479 --> 02:45:41.700
Using a variety of cover stories, they managed
to pry out a deadly secret from the mouth

02:45:41.700 --> 02:45:42.840
of the police chief.

02:45:42.840 --> 02:45:46.319
Human remains had been recovered near the
disappearance sites.

02:45:46.319 --> 02:45:51.179
The authorities opted to keep them a secret
from the public, so as to not cause any panic

02:45:51.180 --> 02:45:56.580
of a crazed serial killer on the loose, or
inspire fears of something even worse lurking

02:45:56.580 --> 02:45:57.660
the city’s underground.

02:45:57.660 --> 02:46:01.979
The Agents seized the three cadavers, and
alerted the Foundation that their mission

02:46:01.979 --> 02:46:04.019
had been progressing as expected.

02:46:04.020 --> 02:46:06.720
The bodies were transported&nbsp;
to Humanoid Containment&nbsp;

02:46:06.720 --> 02:46:10.319
Site-282 in Graz, Austria, where they were

02:46:10.319 --> 02:46:15.359
immediately examined by Dr. Felix Gärtner,
who performed an autopsy on the three corpses.

02:46:15.359 --> 02:46:20.580
If the Foundation was unsure about anomalous
involvement before, they were certain of it

02:46:20.580 --> 02:46:20.819
now.

02:46:20.819 --> 02:46:26.939
The bodies were in shambles, mutilated beyond
belief and altered into an almost unrecognizable

02:46:26.939 --> 02:46:27.359
state.

02:46:27.359 --> 02:46:32.160
The mere stench of them caused personnel working
with them to rush to the bathroom, and even

02:46:32.160 --> 02:46:36.899
those that could typically keep their lunch
down had a difficult time examining them.

02:46:36.899 --> 02:46:40.679
Cadaver-A was in pieces, and the cause of
death was determined to be from exsanguination,

02:46:40.680 --> 02:46:42.840
or the extreme loss of blood.

02:46:42.840 --> 02:46:48.600
Cadaver-B was missing some important fleshy
components inside and out, some of which had

02:46:48.600 --> 02:46:49.859
been removed entirely.

02:46:49.859 --> 02:46:52.920
The cause of death was presumed to be traumatic
cardiac arrest.

02:46:52.920 --> 02:46:56.100
The third corpse, Cadaver-C, was barely a
body.

02:46:56.100 --> 02:46:59.280
Instead, it was a collection of bones and
fluids.

02:46:59.280 --> 02:47:04.740
The cause of death, because of the opaque
conditions the cadaver was found in, was unknown.

02:47:04.740 --> 02:47:09.840
These grizzly deaths were only the start of
the Foundation’s containment of this anomaly,

02:47:09.840 --> 02:47:13.080
and are far from the worst this file has to
offer.

02:47:13.080 --> 02:47:19.859
This is SCP Explained, and today we’re going
to be looking at SCP-3288, a collection of

02:47:19.859 --> 02:47:22.979
entities otherwise known as The Aristocrats.

02:47:22.979 --> 02:47:28.559
Dr. Gartner’s analysis of the cadavers came
to a single conclusion: a human could not

02:47:28.560 --> 02:47:28.979
do this.

02:47:28.979 --> 02:47:33.599
In fact, he compared the deceased’s injuries
and conditions with the bodies of victims

02:47:33.600 --> 02:47:34.800
of hyena attacks.

02:47:34.800 --> 02:47:40.620
All sustained injuries weren’t the result
of a blunt object, sharpened blade, or a firearm,

02:47:40.620 --> 02:47:45.660
but instead resulted from a combination of
teeth, claws, and raw physical strength.

02:47:45.660 --> 02:47:50.639
The bodies had abnormally large bite marks,
approximately six times the size of adult

02:47:50.640 --> 02:47:56.220
human teeth, yet closer analysis revealed
that the indentations did, in fact, coincide

02:47:56.220 --> 02:47:57.120
with human teeth.

02:47:57.120 --> 02:48:03.240
Whatever did this possessed more than sixty
teeth, unevenly distributed over six distinct

02:48:03.240 --> 02:48:07.679
rows, and required jaws much larger than those
of ordinary humans.

02:48:07.680 --> 02:48:12.720
There were unique patterns among these markings,
suggesting that it wasn’t a single entity

02:48:12.720 --> 02:48:15.420
that ravaged these corpses, but multiple.

02:48:15.420 --> 02:48:19.500
There was no doubt about it, these deaths
were anomalous in nature.

02:48:19.500 --> 02:48:26.220
The Foundation issued a designation for the
entities responsible, SCP-3288, and deployed

02:48:26.220 --> 02:48:31.979
Mobile Task Force Sigma-6 (“Hellsingers”),
a special unit trained to capture deadly anomalies

02:48:31.979 --> 02:48:36.540
in the field, to bring SCP-3288 into Foundation
custody.

02:48:36.540 --> 02:48:41.519
The operatives were tasked with patrolling
the Leopoldstadt District, the area where

02:48:41.520 --> 02:48:43.140
the most disappearances had occurred.

02:48:43.140 --> 02:48:48.660
Secrecy, as usual, was a top priority, and
members of the Task Force took extra care

02:48:48.660 --> 02:48:51.240
to conduct their operations away from the
public eye.

02:48:51.240 --> 02:48:56.580
As the purpose of this mission was to contain
the entities for further study, the operatives

02:48:56.580 --> 02:49:03.000
were also ordered to refrain from lethal force,
and to target SCP-3288 with tracking darts

02:49:03.000 --> 02:49:04.560
to prevent them from escaping.

02:49:04.560 --> 02:49:07.080
The Task Force divided up their assignments.

02:49:07.080 --> 02:49:12.000
Twelve operatives would patrol the district
and search for any suspicious activity, while

02:49:12.000 --> 02:49:16.979
ten others would remain watch in positions
with unrestricted views of sewer holes and

02:49:16.979 --> 02:49:19.019
other underground access areas.

02:49:19.020 --> 02:49:21.600
For the first few hours, things were quiet.

02:49:21.600 --> 02:49:25.979
But then, two operatives stationed near the
Danube Canal made a report to the rest of

02:49:25.979 --> 02:49:26.340
the team.

02:49:26.340 --> 02:49:31.380
Someone near the Canal was screaming, not
loudly, but in a muffled, faint way.

02:49:31.380 --> 02:49:36.240
The operatives took initiative and ran off
to investigate the matter themselves, requesting

02:49:36.240 --> 02:49:37.620
backup at the same time.

02:49:37.620 --> 02:49:42.899
Reinforcements arrived less than three minutes
later, but their teammates could not be found.

02:49:42.899 --> 02:49:47.759
Moments later, their bodies were discovered
by another operative, mangled beyond belief.

02:49:47.760 --> 02:49:52.979
Both operatives were killed, and alongside
them was the half-consumed corpse of a local

02:49:52.979 --> 02:49:54.000
civilian as well.

02:49:54.000 --> 02:49:58.200
One operative’s body was recovered from
the canal, while the other was found after

02:49:58.200 --> 02:50:00.899
following a trail of blood and fluids into
an alleyway.

02:50:00.899 --> 02:50:04.740
But despite the loss of life, the mission
was still deemed a success.

02:50:04.740 --> 02:50:10.620
Before being mauled by the SCP-3288 instance,
the Task Force operative managed to shoot

02:50:10.620 --> 02:50:15.000
the entity with a tracking bullet, a piece
of technology utilizing satellite location,

02:50:15.540 --> 02:50:19.319
which allowed the rest of the team to follow
the entity into the sewers.

02:50:19.319 --> 02:50:24.359
The tracking was working perfectly, and the
entity was shown to be fleeing into Vienna’s

02:50:24.359 --> 02:50:29.759
sewer system, until the signal faded somewhere
near the Hofburg, a palace constructed centuries

02:50:29.760 --> 02:50:34.920
ago that was once host to the Hapsburg Dynasty,
and presently serves as the seat of power

02:50:34.920 --> 02:50:36.660
for the President of Austria.

02:50:36.660 --> 02:50:41.639
The team was confused, as the fading nature
of the signal suggested that the tracking

02:50:41.640 --> 02:50:46.200
bullet had been brought into a location far
deeper than the Viennese sewers were believed

02:50:46.200 --> 02:50:46.979
to accommodate.

02:50:46.979 --> 02:50:53.339
The mission moved onward, into the depths
of the sewers in pursuit of SCP-3288.

02:50:53.340 --> 02:50:58.380
The following day, the Task Force had assembled
a strategy for mapping and exploring the Viennese

02:50:58.380 --> 02:50:58.979
sewer system.

02:50:58.979 --> 02:51:02.160
Constructed in the mid 19th century, these&nbsp;

02:51:02.160 --> 02:51:04.559
sewers were part of a larger&nbsp;
network of subterranean

02:51:04.560 --> 02:51:09.359
tunnels that included catacombs, abandoned
wine cellars, and underground rivers.

02:51:09.359 --> 02:51:14.819
Without proper planning and clear communication,
death could be a very real possibility, and

02:51:14.819 --> 02:51:17.759
not even one caused by SCP-3288.

02:51:17.760 --> 02:51:21.000
The task force was divided into four teams
of five.

02:51:21.000 --> 02:51:24.720
Three to investigate the sewers and one to
remain on standby.

02:51:24.720 --> 02:51:29.640
By triangulating the location of the tracked
instance, the Foundation was able to pinpoint

02:51:29.640 --> 02:51:31.800
the general area they would need to explore.

02:51:31.800 --> 02:51:36.720
By blocking off certain exits and surface
access points, they hoped to minimize the

02:51:36.720 --> 02:51:39.840
possibility of the entity’s escape or exposure
to the public.

02:51:39.840 --> 02:51:45.600
While the primary objective remained containing
an SCP-3288 instance for scientific research,

02:51:45.600 --> 02:51:49.200
lethal force was authorized to be used in
case of emergencies.

02:51:49.200 --> 02:51:54.120
The Foundation valued the lives of its trained
soldiers, and put them above nearly anything.

02:51:54.120 --> 02:51:59.760
Still, the authorization of lethal force spelled
impending doom for many experienced veterans

02:51:59.760 --> 02:52:00.840
of the task force.

02:52:00.840 --> 02:52:05.399
They knew all too well about what kind of
entity they were up against when the Foundation

02:52:05.399 --> 02:52:09.240
opted to skip the containment step and prioritize
getting out alive.

02:52:09.240 --> 02:52:11.939
A team of operatives reached their destination&nbsp;

02:52:11.939 --> 02:52:14.700
safely but didn’t discover&nbsp;
anything of significance

02:52:14.700 --> 02:52:18.840
during their trek through the sewers of Vienna,
at least not at first.

02:52:18.840 --> 02:52:23.939
After several hours of investigation, they
encountered human skeletal remains while making

02:52:23.939 --> 02:52:25.799
their way through waist deep sewage.

02:52:25.800 --> 02:52:30.000
One member of the task force pointed out a
loose brick in the wall, and then another

02:52:30.000 --> 02:52:31.260
did the same minutes later.

02:52:31.260 --> 02:52:33.960
Inspection of the area found&nbsp;
a number of loose-fitting&nbsp;

02:52:33.960 --> 02:52:36.180
bricks that were able to be removed with ease,

02:52:36.180 --> 02:52:38.399
as if they were put there to hide something.

02:52:38.399 --> 02:52:43.979
When the entryway was fully unearthed, it
revealed a previously unseen chamber, whose

02:52:43.979 --> 02:52:47.160
walls were engraved with the House of Habsburg’s
coat of arms.

02:52:47.160 --> 02:52:50.819
Operatives inside the chamber immediately
knew what they were looking at.

02:52:50.819 --> 02:52:54.899
A family crypt of royal bloodline, never uncovered
before.

02:52:54.899 --> 02:52:59.460
The forgotten atmosphere made them feel like
they were discovering a secret they were never

02:52:59.460 --> 02:53:00.359
supposed to know.

02:53:00.359 --> 02:53:03.240
24 sarcophagi were found within the chamber,&nbsp;

02:53:03.240 --> 02:53:05.819
and historical records of&nbsp;
the sewers and surrounding

02:53:05.819 --> 02:53:08.639
area mentioned nothing about a crypt beneath
the palace.

02:53:08.640 --> 02:53:14.040
Multiple statues were recovered from the chamber
as well, depicting veiled women with hushed

02:53:14.040 --> 02:53:16.620
expressions, holding a finger to their lips.

02:53:16.620 --> 02:53:19.260
Almost as if to say that this place was a&nbsp;

02:53:19.260 --> 02:53:22.620
royal secret, and trespassing&nbsp;
had grave consequences

02:53:22.620 --> 02:53:23.519
- get it?

02:53:23.520 --> 02:53:24.900
“Grave” Consequences…No?

02:53:27.540 --> 02:53:34.319
Ooookay…moving on - The tombs themselves
were intricate, decorated with ornate jewelry

02:53:34.319 --> 02:53:39.299
and various expensive embellishments, but
did not include placards, markings, or any

02:53:39.300 --> 02:53:41.640
indication as to who was entombed within.

02:53:41.640 --> 02:53:45.300
When the operatives opened the sarcophagi,
they were disgusted.

02:53:45.300 --> 02:53:49.080
The skeletal remains of over 300 bodies, all&nbsp;

02:53:49.080 --> 02:53:52.019
displaying severe and likely&nbsp;
fatal birth deformities.

02:53:52.020 --> 02:53:54.240
The team was at a loss.

02:53:54.240 --> 02:53:56.219
What was the meaning of this room?

02:53:56.220 --> 02:54:00.960
The entrance had been destroyed some time
ago, with stairs shattered and buried among

02:54:00.960 --> 02:54:01.439
the stone.

02:54:01.439 --> 02:54:06.599
Near the other side of the row of tombs was
a vault door, coated in bronze and bearing

02:54:06.600 --> 02:54:08.340
the coat of arms of the Habsburgs.

02:54:08.340 --> 02:54:11.580
A seal, written in latin, was engraved beneath
the coat.

02:54:11.580 --> 02:54:14.340
Translated, it read: “For Purity of Blood”.

02:54:14.340 --> 02:54:18.000
The task force tried to pry the door open,
but it wouldn’t budge.

02:54:18.000 --> 02:54:22.680
Opening it would require special equipment,
and after what they had witnessed inside the

02:54:22.680 --> 02:54:26.939
sarcophagus, some members of the team were
even hesitant to continue trying.

02:54:26.939 --> 02:54:31.319
The team was ordered by the supervising team
to hold their location and await the arrival

02:54:31.319 --> 02:54:33.000
of another team that would open the door.

02:54:33.000 --> 02:54:38.220
Foundation agents on the surface organized
a temporary evacuation of the Hofburg building.

02:54:38.220 --> 02:54:40.500
The team waited for backup throughout the
night.

02:54:40.500 --> 02:54:43.439
They made attempts to open the vault, but
to no avail.

02:54:43.439 --> 02:54:48.660
Once the surface had been properly evacuated
and an infiltration team arrived inside the

02:54:48.660 --> 02:54:53.340
chamber to assist with the vault door, the
gate was able to be opened using oxygen-fuel

02:54:53.340 --> 02:54:56.040
cutting torches over a period of two hours.

02:54:56.040 --> 02:55:02.220
Once opened, the team was met with an ominous,
descending staircase, leading to an unknown,

02:55:02.220 --> 02:55:04.439
dark location underneath the palace.

02:55:04.439 --> 02:55:09.960
An eight-man squad, heavily armed and equipped
with recording devices, ventured down the

02:55:09.960 --> 02:55:10.439
staircase.

02:55:10.439 --> 02:55:13.319
Radio transmissions from&nbsp;
the squad grew increasingly&nbsp;

02:55:13.319 --> 02:55:14.340
faint over time.

02:55:14.340 --> 02:55:19.859
When they reached the estimated 65 meter mark
underground, their communications arrays were

02:55:19.859 --> 02:55:20.580
barely audible.

02:55:20.580 --> 02:55:23.519
At the bottom of the stairwell was an ornate
foyer.

02:55:23.520 --> 02:55:29.040
Instead of decaying, gray stone walls and
oceans of sewage, there were marble floors,

02:55:29.040 --> 02:55:32.580
with felted carpets and white painted walls
and ceilings.

02:55:32.580 --> 02:55:37.260
This chamber was found to be architecturally
identical to a certain wing of the Hofburg

02:55:37.260 --> 02:55:37.800
Palace.

02:55:37.800 --> 02:55:42.600
Furthermore, the chamber was clearly built
in the 18th century, as many aesthetic choices

02:55:42.600 --> 02:55:45.180
popular during that era were clearly present.

02:55:45.180 --> 02:55:50.220
Much like the crypt, there were sculptures
and statues, but this time there were also

02:55:50.220 --> 02:55:53.040
columns, paintings, and tattered tapestries.

02:55:53.040 --> 02:55:57.000
Some of the operatives admiring the beauty
of the room overlooked that on every piece

02:55:57.000 --> 02:56:01.560
of art, any and all depictions of the human
form were defaced and altered.

02:56:01.560 --> 02:56:07.020
The air was rancid, with operatives describing
the odor as similar to rotten meat and stale

02:56:07.020 --> 02:56:07.439
sweat.

02:56:07.439 --> 02:56:11.399
The floor and walls were discolored with what
appeared to be dried, old blood.

02:56:11.399 --> 02:56:13.559
Regardless, they moved forward.

02:56:13.560 --> 02:56:18.420
In between the space’s equivalent of the
Hofburg Imperial Library was a laboratory,

02:56:18.420 --> 02:56:20.399
not found in the palace above.

02:56:20.399 --> 02:56:25.439
An operative collected numerous documents
related to alchemy, biology, and the occult,

02:56:25.439 --> 02:56:29.580
as well as a journal of transactions, contracts,
and private writings.

02:56:29.580 --> 02:56:34.439
These documents were delivered to the above
personnel, and were later translated by Foundation

02:56:34.439 --> 02:56:35.099
personnel.

02:56:35.100 --> 02:56:40.500
All along this chamber were human remains,
decomposing and strewn around the palace.

02:56:40.500 --> 02:56:46.620
Suddenly, a bell tolled, and the music of
a pipe organ began playing discordantly for

02:56:46.620 --> 02:56:47.640
over three minutes.

02:56:47.640 --> 02:56:52.439
Operatives hid themselves and deactivated
their flashlights, some hiding behind the

02:56:52.439 --> 02:56:56.219
curtains of a large opera hall and others
behind large instruments.

02:56:56.220 --> 02:56:58.140
They heard footsteps in the distance.

02:56:58.140 --> 02:57:02.279
Minutes later, a group of figures emerged
into the palace hall.

02:57:02.279 --> 02:57:08.399
The entities the Foundation had classified
as SCP-3288 were now fully visible.

02:57:08.399 --> 02:57:14.040
Their outfits were typical of the 18th century,
containing deep shades of red that contrasted

02:57:14.040 --> 02:57:19.019
with their stark white skin, porcelain masquerade
masks, and powdered wigs.

02:57:19.020 --> 02:57:25.560
Their bodies were monstrous, with arms dragging
across the floor, uneven faces, long fingers,

02:57:25.560 --> 02:57:29.340
some possessing more than 10 of, and hunched
backs.

02:57:29.340 --> 02:57:34.319
A pair of smaller instances entered behind
the hoard of the others, and one blew a rusted

02:57:34.319 --> 02:57:37.799
trumpet while the other held a banner depicting
the Hapsburg’s crest.

02:57:37.800 --> 02:57:43.380
The trumpeter began speaking, but its words
were unintelligible, and raw, guttural moans.

02:57:43.380 --> 02:57:47.880
They ran out of the way, their stunted legs
causing them to trip across the floor.

02:57:47.880 --> 02:57:53.640
There were now over several hundred SCP-3288
instances inside the ballroom.

02:57:53.640 --> 02:57:58.680
Multiple operatives activated silent distress
calls, requesting backup to deal with the

02:57:58.680 --> 02:58:00.720
mass of entities they would have to contain.

02:58:00.720 --> 02:58:06.540
The instances bowed their heads, and another
mass of footsteps were heard as a group of

02:58:06.540 --> 02:58:11.880
SCP-3288 instances carried a morbidly obese
instance atop a throne.

02:58:11.880 --> 02:58:17.760
It wore a cape, a red veil in place of a mask,
and a crown too small for its head.

02:58:17.760 --> 02:58:20.700
It was evident that this was their leader.

02:58:20.700 --> 02:58:23.160
A large cauldron was presented before the
king.

02:58:23.160 --> 02:58:27.899
A small instance climbed atop the king’s
shoulder and lifted the entity’s veil to

02:58:27.899 --> 02:58:28.500
speak to it.

02:58:28.500 --> 02:58:34.080
The cauldron was uncovered, and the king lurched
forward, grabbing the tub and pouring its

02:58:34.080 --> 02:58:35.880
contents down its massive mouth.

02:58:35.880 --> 02:58:40.680
Some of the king’s disgusting meal spilled
from its mouth, revealing a small human child

02:58:40.680 --> 02:58:42.120
with severe deformities.

02:58:42.120 --> 02:58:48.720
The SCP-3288 instances roared in applause
and began to feast, all while the cacophony

02:58:48.720 --> 02:58:53.160
of noise brought on by the various instruments
inside the ballroom raged on.

02:58:53.160 --> 02:58:59.399
An operative hiding behind a harpsichord was
discovered by an SCP-3288 instance, and quickly

02:58:59.399 --> 02:59:03.359
consumed by it in the feeding frenzy the entities
were engaged in.

02:59:03.359 --> 02:59:09.000
Still barely alive before being entirely digested
by the entity, the consumed task force operative

02:59:09.000 --> 02:59:12.180
triggered an explosive device from within
the entity’s stomach.

02:59:12.180 --> 02:59:17.460
With a look of immediate uncomfort, the entity
suddenly exploded, taking out several other

02:59:17.460 --> 02:59:20.399
nearby 3288 instances with the blast.

02:59:20.399 --> 02:59:25.200
The entities were distraught, and while they
were distracted, the task force lept into

02:59:25.200 --> 02:59:31.260
action and rendered the remaining SCP-3288
instances not killed by the explosion unconscious

02:59:31.260 --> 02:59:33.479
using devices loaded with a gas.

02:59:33.479 --> 02:59:39.479
As Foundation reinforcements arrived, the
surviving SCP-3288 entities were contained

02:59:39.479 --> 02:59:42.899
and moved to Site-282, including the massive&nbsp;

02:59:42.899 --> 02:59:46.139
king, whose body was&nbsp;
transported using a specialized

02:59:46.140 --> 02:59:46.560
crane.

02:59:46.560 --> 02:59:52.080
After the removal of all remaining entities,
the palace was filled with cement and reburied,

02:59:52.080 --> 02:59:55.920
with the Foundation making sure that no one
would ever discover it again.

02:59:55.920 --> 03:00:01.260
After the King was contained, Foundation personnel
were shocked to discover that the entity could

03:00:01.260 --> 03:00:01.560
speak.

03:00:01.560 --> 03:00:06.660
In an interview with the hulking monstrosity,
it revealed that its name was Maximillian

03:00:06.660 --> 03:00:09.779
the Great, a patriarch of the House Habsburg.

03:00:09.779 --> 03:00:14.580
The entity’s eyesight was severely damaged
from centuries of living underground, and

03:00:14.580 --> 03:00:18.840
the Foundation was able to get the King to
comply by shining powerful lights in its eyes.

03:00:18.840 --> 03:00:24.540
The entity was delusional, believing itself
still to be inside the palace, and referring

03:00:24.540 --> 03:00:28.620
to the doctor as nothing more than mere meat,
which it wanted to consume.

03:00:28.620 --> 03:00:33.240
When the doctor was able to convince the King
that he too was noble blood, which the king

03:00:33.240 --> 03:00:38.219
believed due to his unstable mental state,
the entity uttered a chilling statement:

03:00:38.220 --> 03:00:41.460
“We are of the same noble blood.

03:00:41.460 --> 03:00:45.479
But some are more noble than others.

03:00:45.479 --> 03:00:51.479
Our bloodline is pure - untainted by outsiders.

03:00:51.479 --> 03:00:53.879
We do not eat human.

03:00:53.880 --> 03:00:55.979
We eat peasants.

03:00:55.979 --> 03:00:58.799
We eat undesirables.

03:00:58.800 --> 03:01:02.700
We devour life undeserving of life.

03:01:02.700 --> 03:01:06.179
That is the nature of nobility.

03:01:06.180 --> 03:01:08.520
What else would be the point?”

03:01:08.520 --> 03:01:14.100
DNA testing revealed that the king was, in
fact, descended from the House of Habsburgs,

03:01:14.100 --> 03:01:17.460
as all SCP-3288 instances were.

03:01:17.460 --> 03:01:20.760
But what of the journal entries discovered
inside the palace?

03:01:20.760 --> 03:01:25.680
After translation, the Foundation found that
they contained the writings of Leopold I,

03:01:25.680 --> 03:01:31.140
a Holy Roman Emperor and member of the Habsburg
house in the early 1700s.

03:01:31.140 --> 03:01:36.180
His writings detailed his desire to claim
power over the royal family, as well as his

03:01:36.180 --> 03:01:40.620
fears of an increased number of inbred, deformed
members of the Habsburg House.

03:01:40.620 --> 03:01:46.200
Leopold details meeting a woman of unknown
origin, who promised him that his family name

03:01:46.200 --> 03:01:47.340
could live forever.

03:01:47.340 --> 03:01:51.660
She taught him arcane knowledge involving
experimentations of the flesh.

03:01:51.660 --> 03:01:57.120
Small animals, and eventually humans were
subject to Leopold’s disgusting, unholy

03:01:57.120 --> 03:01:57.840
experiments.

03:01:57.840 --> 03:02:02.040
Even his mystical teacher became disgusted
with what her tutelage had wrought.

03:02:02.040 --> 03:02:07.620
As payment, she demanded that Leopold cease
his reign, deliver his land and wealth to

03:02:07.620 --> 03:02:10.920
common people, and destroy his various deeds
and titles.

03:02:10.920 --> 03:02:15.240
Leopold refused, and had the woman burned
at the stake for witchcraft.

03:02:15.240 --> 03:02:20.160
Eventually, Leopold’s experiments to make
his bloodline perpetual resulted in the creation

03:02:20.160 --> 03:02:22.080
of SCP-3288.

03:02:22.080 --> 03:02:28.080
Years of inclusive family ties mutated over
one another, generation after generation,

03:02:28.080 --> 03:02:33.840
until a horde of SCP-3288, living underneath
the palace and feasting on a diet of human

03:02:33.840 --> 03:02:35.220
meat, were created.

03:02:35.220 --> 03:02:41.100
For years, the surface Habsburgs catered to
SCP-3288’s depraved and disgusting needs,

03:02:41.100 --> 03:02:46.500
providing them with a slew of humans to feast
on and a lavish lifestyle akin to the one

03:02:46.500 --> 03:02:48.180
lived by the nobility above.

03:02:48.180 --> 03:02:53.939
One other document revealed to the Foundation
that there were multiple hives of SCP-3288

03:02:53.939 --> 03:02:55.439
existing throughout Europe.

03:02:55.439 --> 03:03:00.240
Most were discovered and neutralized, but
the original writing was heavily damaged by

03:03:00.240 --> 03:03:04.920
mold, meaning that there were some locations
the Foundation was unable to uncover.

03:03:04.920 --> 03:03:11.399
Colonies of SCP-3288 instances buried underground,
snatching humans without any care.

03:03:11.399 --> 03:03:16.319
Mutating their own deformities and living
horribly, unable to be stopped.

03:03:16.319 --> 03:03:22.799
A captured SCP-3288 instance in Germany revealed
that there was another entity, similar to

03:03:22.800 --> 03:03:25.920
the King in authority, by the name of the
Empress.

03:03:25.920 --> 03:03:29.819
It had this to say to the Foundation, upon
being contained:

03:03:29.819 --> 03:03:32.819
“The meek will beget the strong.

03:03:32.819 --> 03:03:36.599
The doomed will beget the chosen.

03:03:36.600 --> 03:03:38.160
Don't you see?

03:03:38.160 --> 03:03:45.120
The greedy will devour the charitable and
the merciless will ravage the peaceful.

03:03:45.120 --> 03:03:48.960
We will make the world as perfect as us.

03:03:48.960 --> 03:03:52.920
We will all be aristocrats in the end.

03:03:52.920 --> 03:03:57.540
And our Dynasty will never die.”

03:03:57.540 --> 03:03:59.040
Happy birthday!

03:03:59.040 --> 03:04:04.740
It’s your day to enjoy however you want,
with lots of gifts and sweets.

03:04:04.740 --> 03:04:08.460
And look - a little friend is here to help
you celebrate.

03:04:08.460 --> 03:04:12.720
It’s the birthday monkey, and he has a song
to sing…

03:04:12.720 --> 03:04:19.560
Dating back to the 1940s, SCP-983 is one of
the most harmless-looking objects in the SCP

03:04:19.560 --> 03:04:20.819
Foundation’s possession.

03:04:20.819 --> 03:04:25.799
It’s an old-fashioned mechanical monkey,
a common wind-up toy from the old days.

03:04:25.800 --> 03:04:31.380
It’s dressed in a sharp little vest, and
holds a tiny bell and striking rod for making

03:04:31.380 --> 03:04:31.859
music.

03:04:31.859 --> 03:04:37.439
It seems to be a simple toy, the kind that
would annoy a tired parent as it plays its

03:04:37.439 --> 03:04:40.259
little tune over and over, but nothing more.

03:04:40.260 --> 03:04:44.160
But this is no ordinary wind-up toy.

03:04:44.160 --> 03:04:50.279
SCP-983 is capable of sounds and even speech
that doesn’t seem to match up with its design,

03:04:50.279 --> 03:04:55.559
and an investigation reveals it doesn’t
have any signs as to how it was constructed.

03:04:55.560 --> 03:05:01.560
No screws, seams, or markings that would be
common on a toy, and no voice box or other

03:05:01.560 --> 03:05:04.560
mechanical feature that would allow for speech.

03:05:04.560 --> 03:05:10.380
But despite these oddities, it seems to be
a normal toy that can be handled safely and

03:05:10.380 --> 03:05:10.920
played with.

03:05:10.920 --> 03:05:14.520
On every day but one... that is.

03:05:14.520 --> 03:05:23.279
Because SCP-983 has a secondary purpose, and
on one special day it has a gift for its handler.

03:05:23.279 --> 03:05:27.599
It can be a gift of joy - or a gift of terror.

03:05:27.600 --> 03:05:31.800
Nicknamed the Birthday Monkey, SCP-983 activates&nbsp;

03:05:31.800 --> 03:05:34.100
when it is handled by someone&nbsp;
within the twenty-four

03:05:34.100 --> 03:05:35.819
hour period of their birthday.

03:05:35.819 --> 03:05:41.099
It seems to be able to tell when this period
of time happens automatically, and as soon

03:05:41.100 --> 03:05:47.520
as it becomes aware, a series of surprises
begin to surface for the lucky - or unlucky

03:05:47.520 --> 03:05:48.600
- handler.

03:05:48.600 --> 03:05:51.060
It all starts with a little leap.

03:05:51.060 --> 03:05:57.120
As soon as SCP-983 becomes aware of the birthday
boy or girl, it’ll do a charming little

03:05:57.120 --> 03:05:57.899
backflip.

03:05:57.899 --> 03:06:03.420
It’ll then lift its bell and start singing
the same song - “A Ring Ding Ding Ding It’s

03:06:03.420 --> 03:06:03.899
Your Birthday!”

03:06:03.899 --> 03:06:09.179
To this day, the Foundation has not been able
to figure out exactly where this voice comes

03:06:09.180 --> 03:06:12.060
from, and it follows this by ringing its bell.

03:06:12.060 --> 03:06:17.160
The tone of the bell varies wildly - in ways
that the instrument should not be able to

03:06:17.160 --> 03:06:21.300
create, ranging from low tones to painfully
high-pitched tones.

03:06:21.300 --> 03:06:24.120
And that’s where the horror begins.

03:06:24.120 --> 03:06:29.460
The Birthday Monkey doesn’t just want to
sing a song - it wants to play a game.

03:06:29.460 --> 03:06:34.500
The song will repeat every three to four seconds,
marked by rings of the bell.

03:06:34.500 --> 03:06:40.560
And for every ring of the bell, the birthday
boy or girl will age a year - continuing until

03:06:40.560 --> 03:06:44.279
they die of old age, or win the game.

03:06:44.279 --> 03:06:47.580
But how does one win the game before it’s
too late?

03:06:47.580 --> 03:06:53.160
No one is sure, but studies of this strange
toy in action indicate that it involves singing

03:06:53.160 --> 03:06:55.620
along - and timing it correctly.

03:06:55.620 --> 03:07:00.720
It’s probably a little hard to do that while
aging to death in seconds, but no one said

03:07:00.720 --> 03:07:02.640
SCPs play fair.

03:07:02.640 --> 03:07:07.319
But in the event that someone actually does
manage to survive the Birthday Monkey’s

03:07:07.319 --> 03:07:09.719
game, it has a prize for them.

03:07:09.720 --> 03:07:15.660
When the sing-along is complete, SCP-983 will
let out an enthusiastic shout of “Birthday!”,

03:07:15.660 --> 03:07:19.680
ring its bell, and drop a single gumdrop from
its bell.

03:07:19.680 --> 03:07:24.420
But which gumdrop depends on just how well
the birthday victim did.

03:07:24.420 --> 03:07:28.620
A perfect sing-along will result in a clear
candy that seems to glow.

03:07:28.620 --> 03:07:33.000
If it’s a little less than perfect, the
candy won’t glow, but it’ll work the same

03:07:33.000 --> 03:07:36.060
- and both candies have a very valuable property.

03:07:36.060 --> 03:07:41.220
When eaten, the candy will immediately reverse
any age lost during the “game”.

03:07:41.220 --> 03:07:44.520
But does the perfect score give another prize?

03:07:44.520 --> 03:07:49.200
Studies of the rare glowing candy led the
Foundation to believe that it may also provide

03:07:49.200 --> 03:07:54.420
a bonus effect, making the person who eats
it younger and giving them a longer lifespan

03:07:54.420 --> 03:07:55.620
or better health.

03:07:55.620 --> 03:08:01.319
But this is largely guesswork, because the
candy is produced so rarely and the effects

03:08:01.319 --> 03:08:04.620
would only become clear after years or decades
of study.

03:08:04.620 --> 03:08:07.859
But not all candies are to be eaten.

03:08:07.859 --> 03:08:11.639
Many candies of different appearance and quality
have been produced.

03:08:11.640 --> 03:08:18.899
All can be eaten safely - except the black
ones, which represent a failed sing-along.

03:08:18.899 --> 03:08:24.660
The effects of this candy were discovered
the hard way - because the first time SCP-983

03:08:24.660 --> 03:08:30.720
was activated, it was activated in the wild,
before the Foundation had secured it.

03:08:30.720 --> 03:08:35.640
And everyone knows that an SCP in the wild
can be a terrible thing.

03:08:35.640 --> 03:08:40.260
It was a local flea market, when the buyer
noticed the sharp-dressed little monkey.

03:08:40.260 --> 03:08:44.880
The buyer, having a friend who loved monkeys,
thought this would be a perfect gift.

03:08:44.880 --> 03:08:49.979
The seller was not as enthusiastic, and warned
the buyer that it shouldn’t be handled or

03:08:49.979 --> 03:08:51.660
even seen by anyone on their birthday.

03:08:51.660 --> 03:08:56.340
But even the seller didn’t really believe
this, saying that it might have just been

03:08:56.340 --> 03:08:58.859
an old legend that had been passed down for
years.

03:08:58.859 --> 03:09:03.839
It didn’t dissuade the buyer, and off the
monkey went to its new home.

03:09:03.840 --> 03:09:09.899
SCP-983 was activated at an office party,
where the monkey was presented as a gift.

03:09:09.899 --> 03:09:14.279
The guest of honor loved it at first - until
it started singing.

03:09:14.279 --> 03:09:19.559
The staff noticed that as the monkey kept
singing, their co-worker became more and more

03:09:19.560 --> 03:09:20.279
upset.

03:09:20.279 --> 03:09:25.259
The monkey kept singing, and he started to
search for a way to turn it off - but there

03:09:25.260 --> 03:09:28.080
was no button or any other way to deactivate
it.

03:09:28.080 --> 03:09:31.620
And that’s when the coworkers noticed something
disturbing.

03:09:31.620 --> 03:09:36.660
The honoree seemed to be getting weaker and
weaker, and there were even streaks of grey

03:09:36.660 --> 03:09:37.920
appearing in his hair.

03:09:37.920 --> 03:09:40.859
His skin was getting more wrinkled and weathered.

03:09:40.859 --> 03:09:46.799
Soon his hair was entirely grey, and he simply
returned the monkey to where it was as it

03:09:46.800 --> 03:09:47.880
continued to sing.

03:09:47.880 --> 03:09:53.880
He seemed to give up, begged for someone to
turn it off, and waited to expire.

03:09:53.880 --> 03:09:58.319
By the time the Foundation arrived on scene,
it was already too late.

03:09:58.319 --> 03:10:03.540
There was nothing left of the birthday boy
but a desiccated, skeletal corpse.

03:10:03.540 --> 03:10:05.819
The monkey had been able to sing at least&nbsp;

03:10:05.819 --> 03:10:09.240
thirty more verses, and no&nbsp;
one had truly understood

03:10:09.240 --> 03:10:10.620
what was going on.

03:10:10.620 --> 03:10:16.200
They reacted with confusion and inaction,
unable to contain the monkey’s dangerous

03:10:16.200 --> 03:10:16.560
game.

03:10:16.560 --> 03:10:22.920
Even the Foundation didn’t understand SCP-983
at first, so they let the object continue

03:10:22.920 --> 03:10:27.060
singing until the body degraded into a simple
skeleton.

03:10:27.060 --> 03:10:32.580
That’s when the monkey exclaimed its finishing
phrase and released a single black gumdrop.

03:10:32.580 --> 03:10:37.620
While no one ate the gumdrop, the Foundation
observed that it seemed to hypnotize people

03:10:37.620 --> 03:10:41.220
around it, as if it was compelling them to
do something.

03:10:41.220 --> 03:10:47.520
What is lurking within the black gumdrops
- and do they want to be consumed?

03:10:47.520 --> 03:10:53.160
The birthday monkey was taken into SCP custody,
and it became clear that it was harmless to

03:10:53.160 --> 03:10:56.040
everyone for 364 days of the year.

03:10:56.040 --> 03:11:01.680
The foundation wanted to understand more about
this odd toy, so they fell back on their best

03:11:01.680 --> 03:11:07.200
resource for testing - D-class personnel,
who got the chance to show off their singing

03:11:07.200 --> 03:11:10.800
skills with much higher stakes than your average
round of karaoke.

03:11:10.800 --> 03:11:16.560
Most of the tests were routine, with controlled
activations showing how to deactivate the

03:11:16.560 --> 03:11:20.880
monkey - or providing up-close studies of
its devastating effects.

03:11:20.880 --> 03:11:25.680
But one test hinted that this specimen could
be more dangerous than thought.

03:11:25.680 --> 03:11:31.080
Few people volunteer for testing duty at the
SCP Foundation, but that wasn’t the case

03:11:31.080 --> 03:11:33.180
for one now-classified subject.

03:11:33.180 --> 03:11:39.060
Her birthday was approaching, and she surprisingly
volunteered for the test that could only be

03:11:39.060 --> 03:11:40.500
done on your birthday.

03:11:40.500 --> 03:11:45.779
She had an oddly upbeat attitude and seemed
oddly excited about her birthday.

03:11:45.779 --> 03:11:49.259
The test was approved, and she was given limited
information.

03:11:49.260 --> 03:11:54.840
She was given the monkey as a wrapped gift,
told it would sing, and encouraged to sing

03:11:54.840 --> 03:11:55.920
along for a video.

03:11:55.920 --> 03:11:59.880
But her reaction indicated she might know
more than expected.

03:11:59.880 --> 03:12:04.319
As soon as the gift was unwrapped, the SCP
began singing.

03:12:04.319 --> 03:12:08.580
After missing the first verse, the subject
picked up the words and started singing along

03:12:08.580 --> 03:12:13.319
- not just competently, but perfectly and
enthusiastically.

03:12:13.319 --> 03:12:18.359
Soon enough, she started aging rapidly, but
didn’t seem distressed by this at all.

03:12:18.359 --> 03:12:24.240
She maintained her high level of enthusiasm,
even as the monkey sang for over forty verses

03:12:24.240 --> 03:12:26.760
and aged her over forty years.

03:12:26.760 --> 03:12:31.920
She seemed unaware of these drastic changes,
and never missed a beat of the song until

03:12:31.920 --> 03:12:34.620
the monkey issued its finishing exclamation.

03:12:34.620 --> 03:12:38.220
And now, it was time for her prize.

03:12:38.220 --> 03:12:43.740
The gumdrop that fell from the bell was a
new one, completely white and almost shockingly

03:12:43.740 --> 03:12:44.160
bright.

03:12:44.160 --> 03:12:48.599
It glowed, and the subject was immediately
enchanted by it.

03:12:48.600 --> 03:12:53.640
Even the attending scientists and staff couldn’t
help but comment on how impressive it was.

03:12:53.640 --> 03:12:58.740
The subject was allowed to consume it to see
its effects, and was monitored for an hour

03:12:58.740 --> 03:12:59.340
afterward.

03:12:59.340 --> 03:13:04.560
When nothing unusual happened besides the
reversal of the aging, the subject was excused

03:13:04.560 --> 03:13:06.060
to return to her quarters.

03:13:06.060 --> 03:13:09.240
And that’s when things took a shocking turn.

03:13:09.240 --> 03:13:15.059
In an effect never seen before, the subject
suddenly exploded with a brilliant burst of

03:13:15.060 --> 03:13:15.660
white light.

03:13:15.660 --> 03:13:20.639
Whatever this light was, it was strong enough
to knock out all the cameras in the vicinity.

03:13:20.640 --> 03:13:26.100
Everyone in her presence was temporarily blinded,
with it taking five minutes for their eyesight

03:13:26.100 --> 03:13:26.819
to return.

03:13:26.819 --> 03:13:31.979
No long-term ill effects were shown, but the
staff that entered the room after the blast

03:13:31.979 --> 03:13:34.379
noticed that an odd glow remained in the room.

03:13:34.380 --> 03:13:37.380
And that wasn’t the only odd thing.

03:13:37.380 --> 03:13:43.140
The test subject was nowhere to be found - and
has never been seen again.

03:13:43.140 --> 03:13:48.359
The Foundation is on high alert for this test
subject, but she seems to be staying below

03:13:48.359 --> 03:13:51.479
the radar - if she’s even human at all anymore.

03:13:51.479 --> 03:13:54.359
While there is no physical sign of her, the&nbsp;

03:13:54.359 --> 03:13:57.120
Foundation has observed odd&nbsp;
patterns of electromagnetic

03:13:57.120 --> 03:14:02.099
activity in the area and is following reports
of light fixtures needing to be replaced.

03:14:02.100 --> 03:14:06.479
It was clear that SCP-983&nbsp;
was much more unpredictable&nbsp;

03:14:06.479 --> 03:14:07.559
than expected.

03:14:07.560 --> 03:14:13.620
While still classified as safe, the Foundation
is keeping SCP-983 under tighter lock and

03:14:13.620 --> 03:14:14.519
key these days.

03:14:14.520 --> 03:14:19.260
All technicians who handle it are carefully
vetted to ensure they are nowhere near their

03:14:19.260 --> 03:14:19.500
birthday.

03:14:19.500 --> 03:14:25.560
In case of accidental exposure, the Foundation
has prepared emergency kits with detailed

03:14:25.560 --> 03:14:29.760
instructions for how to complete the Birthday
Monkey’s deadly sing-along game.

03:14:29.760 --> 03:14:34.680
But as with all things, the Foundation is
prepared for anything.

03:14:34.680 --> 03:14:39.540
In the event of a failure, the remains will
be disposed of by vetted staff.

03:14:39.540 --> 03:14:44.700
Any candies produced are to be taken into
custody by the Foundation and studied for

03:14:44.700 --> 03:14:50.760
unusual properties, but are not to be consumed
without full containment procedures and approval

03:14:50.760 --> 03:14:52.020
from senior staff.

03:14:52.020 --> 03:14:59.399
The only exception is D-class testing - but
even in those cases, one rule remains intact.

03:14:59.399 --> 03:15:03.359
No one is ever to consume the black candies.

03:15:03.359 --> 03:15:09.120
And caution is encouraged around the Birthday
Monkey - lest you wind up in a sing-along

03:15:09.120 --> 03:15:10.080
for your life.

03:15:10.080 --> 03:15:15.479
From The Garden of Eden to the top corner
of your English teacher’s desk, apples have

03:15:15.479 --> 03:15:20.939
played an equal role in history’s most remarkable
days and also its most mundane.

03:15:20.939 --> 03:15:25.979
The sounds of teeth snapping through the skin,
sinking into flesh, and spitting out seeds

03:15:25.979 --> 03:15:28.379
echo through space forever and onward.

03:15:28.380 --> 03:15:33.120
And for most of our earthly hours consumed
by appetite, it has been documented to be

03:15:33.120 --> 03:15:37.500
a lopsided relationship between these two
things, man and apple.

03:15:37.500 --> 03:15:40.620
Man getting the sweet taste&nbsp;
and abundant nutrients,&nbsp;

03:15:40.620 --> 03:15:43.439
apples getting nothing but pain and stomach

03:15:43.439 --> 03:15:43.979
acids.

03:15:43.979 --> 03:15:46.740
But this story is found not in our history.

03:15:46.740 --> 03:15:52.319
Buried in the lawful patterns of predator
and prey, we stumble upon an irregularity,

03:15:52.319 --> 03:15:56.399
an inversion, an instance of apples biting
back.

03:15:56.399 --> 03:16:04.799
SCP-4608, also known as APPLESEED, was a 60-acre
apple orchard containing over 22,000 trees,

03:16:04.800 --> 03:16:10.979
located just on the outskirts of Milan, Indiana
– a town so small it strains your eyes as

03:16:10.979 --> 03:16:14.639
you squint to find it with a microscope hovering
just over a map.

03:16:14.640 --> 03:16:20.279
And to see what was actually happening within
the curious fringes of society took even greater

03:16:20.279 --> 03:16:24.179
exploration, not just of the eyes but also
of the mind.

03:16:24.180 --> 03:16:29.340
Because what would eventually be seen would
not so easily be comprehended.

03:16:29.340 --> 03:16:33.779
Physical senses are just the surface, and
we need to go deeper.

03:16:33.779 --> 03:16:38.880
Our story begins with a logging company looking
to take ownership of the most fertile land

03:16:38.880 --> 03:16:43.979
they could find in the Great Lake Region,
ideally land that overproduces conifer growth

03:16:43.979 --> 03:16:47.399
so that the return on their investment would
be plentiful and perpetual.

03:16:47.399 --> 03:16:49.859
These lumberjacked men knew what they wanted.

03:16:49.859 --> 03:16:55.080
Beneath their red flannel shirts and muddy
boots was a deep intelligence and understanding

03:16:55.080 --> 03:16:55.680
of nature.

03:16:55.680 --> 03:16:59.819
Their process of assessing the land’s value
was meticulously calculated.

03:16:59.819 --> 03:17:04.559
They knew the soil, both by the experience
of their callused hands and the literature

03:17:04.560 --> 03:17:05.460
of their study.

03:17:05.460 --> 03:17:09.899
They tracked various bird species’ migration
patterns in the area to assess what kind of

03:17:09.899 --> 03:17:13.620
seeds they’d be carrying and contributing
to soil by way of their stool.

03:17:13.620 --> 03:17:18.660
They understood the local laws relating to
clear cutting and conservation and how both

03:17:18.660 --> 03:17:20.460
would affect their profit margins.

03:17:20.460 --> 03:17:23.880
This is all to say, it wasn’t just a speculative
purchase.

03:17:23.880 --> 03:17:27.479
This was planned, thought through, and dwelled
on.

03:17:27.479 --> 03:17:33.299
And yet, even then, with scrupulous eyes and
a careful crew, they missed the warning signs.

03:17:33.300 --> 03:17:37.620
SCP-4608 checked all their boxes…and then
some.

03:17:37.620 --> 03:17:38.819
What could go wrong?

03:17:38.819 --> 03:17:44.040
And so they acquired the land, unwittingly
purchasing the peril that came with it.

03:17:44.040 --> 03:17:48.840
On the first day of owning the property, one
crew member noticed the branches did not sway

03:17:48.840 --> 03:17:50.819
in the same direction as the wind blew.

03:17:50.819 --> 03:17:55.380
He noticed the leaves didn’t float down
in agreement with their feathery weight, but

03:17:55.380 --> 03:17:59.700
rather crashed to the soil like two-dimensional
anvils and grand pianos.

03:17:59.700 --> 03:18:05.099
The roots were not ones you simply trip over,
instead, it seemed as if they stuck their

03:18:05.100 --> 03:18:06.240
leg out to trip you.

03:18:06.240 --> 03:18:11.340
When birds perched themselves up high and
sang their songs, their cadence carried all

03:18:11.340 --> 03:18:12.779
the eeriness of an SOS.

03:18:12.779 --> 03:18:17.580
With all of this said, he was happy to have
acquired the land, and having already picked

03:18:17.580 --> 03:18:22.019
up and moved his family from the West Coast
to now live and work out in Milan, Indiana,

03:18:22.020 --> 03:18:25.620
he decided it best to look past his concerns.

03:18:25.620 --> 03:18:30.300
After all, it was the first day on the new
site, and excitement was in the air…but

03:18:30.899 --> 03:18:33.839
with it also an amorphous, anxious energy.

03:18:33.840 --> 03:18:40.319
During the first logging expedition within
SCP-4608, this same member of the crew hiked

03:18:40.319 --> 03:18:44.099
the grounds to better familiarize himself
with the environment he’d be working on,

03:18:44.100 --> 03:18:48.720
hopeful that if he managed the land properly
and extracted the lumber as efficiently as

03:18:48.720 --> 03:18:53.520
his late father did, he would be able to help
build the business and give his children the

03:18:53.520 --> 03:18:55.020
life he always promised them.

03:18:55.020 --> 03:18:59.220
He brought with him his notepad and took detailed
records of his surroundings.

03:18:59.220 --> 03:19:04.080
He figured to achieve his goals and sustain
long-term yields, he’d have to cooperate

03:19:04.080 --> 03:19:04.920
with his environment.

03:19:04.920 --> 03:19:09.300
But he never questioned if his environment
wanted to cooperate with him.

03:19:09.300 --> 03:19:12.000
Would this question have changed the course
of action?

03:19:12.000 --> 03:19:16.979
Or is brooding on the preference of plants
an empty gesture, best left for hippies at

03:19:16.979 --> 03:19:17.519
Woodstock?

03:19:17.520 --> 03:19:22.200
Either way, the orchard let it be known how
it felt about a collaboration when hours later

03:19:22.200 --> 03:19:24.000
the man was found dead.

03:19:24.000 --> 03:19:28.560
It was first believed by his coworkers to
be a result of a safety equipment malfunction.

03:19:28.560 --> 03:19:33.060
Maybe it was a simple matter of thinking the
skidder was in park when really it was in

03:19:33.060 --> 03:19:33.420
neutral.

03:19:33.420 --> 03:19:37.859
Maybe the Knuckle-boom Loader went on the
fritz how it does when the humidity ramps

03:19:37.859 --> 03:19:37.979
up.

03:19:37.979 --> 03:19:43.080
Maybe machinery really was to blame, in which
case you call it a fluke and ask no more.

03:19:43.080 --> 03:19:46.979
After all, there’s only so many questions
you can ask a robot.

03:19:46.979 --> 03:19:51.599
But initial belief is a fickle thing… and
it wasn’t long until first impressions were

03:19:51.600 --> 03:19:54.120
called into question by the courts of critical
thinking.

03:19:54.120 --> 03:19:57.000
The questions of the crew, however, only rang
briefly.

03:19:57.000 --> 03:20:00.359
Because shortly after the first death fell
a sequence of others.

03:20:00.359 --> 03:20:04.799
In a matter of days, all of the remaining
crew members were declared dead or missing,

03:20:04.800 --> 03:20:10.080
a word reserved for search parties still clinging
to hope, a hot potato they would have been

03:20:10.080 --> 03:20:11.160
wise to abandon.

03:20:11.160 --> 03:20:15.899
For while it was hope that brought these search
parties together, it was hope that sent them

03:20:15.899 --> 03:20:17.879
off… never to be seen again.

03:20:17.880 --> 03:20:24.240
The Foundation was then alerted to the occurrences
surrounding SCP-4608 by police reports accompanied

03:20:24.240 --> 03:20:32.279
by a photograph…a photograph of an SCP-4608-1,
an organism consisting of unidentified plant-like

03:20:32.279 --> 03:20:37.139
muscular structures and a periderm resembling
those found on common hardwoods.

03:20:37.140 --> 03:20:41.939
From the photograph alone, it was clear that
this 3-meter-tall organism was capable of

03:20:41.939 --> 03:20:44.040
committing the violence recently endured.

03:20:44.040 --> 03:20:49.319
Forceful in its demeanor, aggressive in its
presence, and territorial in its perception,

03:20:49.319 --> 03:20:56.160
the photograph of SCP-4608-1 led to an even
bigger question… is this plant-like creature

03:20:56.160 --> 03:20:58.740
grown by nature…or sown by man?

03:20:58.740 --> 03:21:03.960
After extensive research by The Foundation,
records were retrieved that indicate the entirety

03:21:03.960 --> 03:21:09.540
of the sixty-acre land was sown into life
by John Chapman in 1826.

03:21:09.540 --> 03:21:14.340
Chapman was the type of man you could mistake
for a scarecrow, both for reasons of preferred

03:21:14.340 --> 03:21:15.540
garb and body language.

03:21:15.540 --> 03:21:17.580
He was treated as such too.

03:21:17.580 --> 03:21:21.180
His personal space was respected…maybe too
much.

03:21:21.180 --> 03:21:25.920
He spent his life alone, only accompanied
and comforted by the things he planted.

03:21:25.920 --> 03:21:32.279
He maintained these acres all by himself until
his eventual death in 1845, and it’s then

03:21:32.279 --> 03:21:39.840
that it’s believed SCP-4608 became unstable,
reassigning its objective from comfort to

03:21:39.840 --> 03:21:40.319
chaos.

03:21:40.319 --> 03:21:45.719
When the newspaper came out the next Sunday,
John Chapman's obituary painted him as a priest

03:21:45.720 --> 03:21:47.100
of the Allen county church.

03:21:47.100 --> 03:21:49.800
But was this just the art of illusion?

03:21:49.800 --> 03:21:56.040
For as far as we know, no records of a chapel
or congregation exist… a quiet choir indeed.

03:21:56.040 --> 03:22:00.899
Come to think of it, it seems that everything
within this sixty-acre orchard was destined

03:22:00.899 --> 03:22:06.719
to be silenced one way or another, by violent
force or even by conscious decision making.

03:22:06.720 --> 03:22:12.600
See, while the SCP has a long track record
of subduing anomalies by methods of capture

03:22:12.600 --> 03:22:16.500
and containment, not all things are suited
for locks and chains.

03:22:16.500 --> 03:22:21.180
SCP 4608 is better covered with a story than
a tarp.

03:22:21.180 --> 03:22:26.279
A fruitless field that once produced at an
unmanageable pace is now rendered incapable

03:22:26.279 --> 03:22:27.660
of supporting growth.

03:22:27.660 --> 03:22:30.300
Most will think it’s due to a toxic spill.

03:22:30.300 --> 03:22:36.000
In truth, the spill wasn’t that of chemicals
on soil… but rather corpses on crops.

03:22:36.000 --> 03:22:42.300
A week after receiving the photograph of 4608-1,
Site-81 sent a three-man investigation team

03:22:42.300 --> 03:22:43.260
to Milan.

03:22:43.260 --> 03:22:48.180
Their adventure was equally abrupt: a story
with no reportable beginning or middle but

03:22:48.180 --> 03:22:49.740
simply a predictable end.

03:22:49.740 --> 03:22:52.620
After four days of no&nbsp;
communication, the Foundation&nbsp;

03:22:52.620 --> 03:22:54.660
presumed the three agents no different than

03:22:54.660 --> 03:22:56.580
their steak dinner, dead meat.

03:22:56.580 --> 03:23:01.859
And only then, after The Foundation’s failure
to solve the case, was it understood that

03:23:01.859 --> 03:23:06.960
what we were to be looking for wasn’t people
at all…but rather answers to more nebulous

03:23:06.960 --> 03:23:09.540
questions.
What’s really happening here?

03:23:09.540 --> 03:23:12.000
And why is this happening?

03:23:12.000 --> 03:23:17.399
Following the loss of communication with the
investigation team, Site-81 dispatched a high-risk

03:23:17.399 --> 03:23:21.960
response team, Mobile Strike Force Bravo-7,
aka Hometown Heroes.

03:23:21.960 --> 03:23:26.520
These men had all the makings of heroes, and
they were determined to prove themselves worthy

03:23:26.520 --> 03:23:27.300
of that title.

03:23:27.300 --> 03:23:32.939
While Alpha squad moved north toward the incident
site, BETA squad headed east and GAMMA squad

03:23:32.939 --> 03:23:38.040
hurried west – the crews covering all directions
of the compass but south, a coincidentally

03:23:38.040 --> 03:23:41.939
symbolic gesture as if to say we will not
be taken down!

03:23:41.939 --> 03:23:43.859
The mission was simple in theory.

03:23:43.859 --> 03:23:46.620
Find out what happened to the previous team
and why.

03:23:46.620 --> 03:23:51.239
But, alas, missions never are as easy as their
objective statement reads.

03:23:51.239 --> 03:23:54.779
In practice, some might even call them…impossible.

03:23:54.779 --> 03:23:59.099
As ALPHA headed near the incident site, they
noticed the shadows on the ground beneath

03:23:59.100 --> 03:24:02.160
them did not resemble the shape of the leaves
in the canopy above.

03:24:02.160 --> 03:24:06.000
They heard small drops of liquid tap tap tap
on their helmets.

03:24:06.000 --> 03:24:08.640
Yet, it wasn’t raining… was it?

03:24:08.640 --> 03:24:13.080
ALPHA-1 ran his finger across the top of his
helmet and then examined the residue left

03:24:13.080 --> 03:24:13.620
on his skin.

03:24:13.620 --> 03:24:16.500
It was raining…just not water.

03:24:16.500 --> 03:24:17.939
“Oh, god!”

03:24:17.939 --> 03:24:21.299
Upon looking up, he witnessed the reasons
for both irregularities.

03:24:21.300 --> 03:24:26.399
Bodies hung from branches by their intestines,
casting shadow puppets with their lifeless

03:24:26.399 --> 03:24:27.239
limbs.

03:24:27.239 --> 03:24:29.580
Blood dripped down like a leaky faucet.

03:24:29.580 --> 03:24:30.720
“What did this?”

03:24:30.720 --> 03:24:35.640
But before he could even ponder the answer,
he heard a loud shriek from his radio, so

03:24:35.640 --> 03:24:40.140
loud that the radio itself vibrated, shaking
its way loose from his hand and falling to

03:24:40.140 --> 03:24:40.439
the dirt.

03:24:40.439 --> 03:24:45.179
He bent down and picked it up and this time
gripped tighter, as if to tell whoever is

03:24:45.180 --> 03:24:48.779
responsible for that noise that they will
not get away that easily.

03:24:48.779 --> 03:24:53.639
He and his crew followed the sound like a
game of Marco Polo, blind to what may be ahead.

03:24:53.640 --> 03:24:58.200
They extended their guns and pointed them
into the distant tree line, like zombie arms

03:24:58.200 --> 03:25:03.779
reaching outward in the pool toward the resonates
of “Polo”, a small comfort in a giant

03:25:03.779 --> 03:25:04.679
game of distress.

03:25:04.680 --> 03:25:09.960
As they pressed forward, ALPHA Squad proceeded
past all signs that pointed them back, stepping

03:25:09.960 --> 03:25:12.060
over dead bodies like puddles on a rainy day.

03:25:12.060 --> 03:25:16.680
Soon they found themselves crouching down
next to human remains, attending brief and

03:25:16.680 --> 03:25:22.080
hurried funerals for all their closest comrades,
torn between staying to pay respect and marching

03:25:22.080 --> 03:25:23.100
along to earn it.

03:25:23.100 --> 03:25:27.239
The chest cavities of the fallen had been
ripped open and filled with apples.

03:25:27.239 --> 03:25:29.639
A grim foresight into what they were up against.

03:25:29.640 --> 03:25:34.140
But nothing they could ever imagine would
prepare them for what they were about to see.

03:25:34.140 --> 03:25:36.060
And they wouldn’t have to wait long.

03:25:36.060 --> 03:25:38.340
Another loud shriek from ALPHA–1’s radio!

03:25:38.340 --> 03:25:40.979
It shot free from his grip and again landed
in the dirt.

03:25:40.979 --> 03:25:45.540
The squad tried to ignore the metaphorical
implications of this recurrence, quickly picking

03:25:45.540 --> 03:25:49.859
up the radio and shrugging it off as if the
five-second rule applied equally to communication

03:25:49.859 --> 03:25:51.540
systems as candy bars.

03:25:51.540 --> 03:25:55.680
They pressed forward, maybe out of bravery,
maybe out of shame of going back.

03:25:55.680 --> 03:26:00.239
And while moving through trees, they began
to notice something alarming etched on their

03:26:00.239 --> 03:26:01.439
bark.
What was it?

03:26:01.439 --> 03:26:05.339
There were unnaturally deep grooves on the
base of almost every one of the trees.

03:26:05.340 --> 03:26:07.260
But what exactly were they from?

03:26:07.260 --> 03:26:09.540
Scratches from an animal or beast?

03:26:09.540 --> 03:26:10.260
Infection?

03:26:10.260 --> 03:26:11.279
Decay?

03:26:11.279 --> 03:26:12.779
Their eyes drew closer.

03:26:12.779 --> 03:26:15.059
But proximity brought them no clarity.

03:26:15.060 --> 03:26:20.279
These sigils and symbols could be dated back
to occult Norse religion, but in that moment

03:26:20.279 --> 03:26:25.739
they were incomprehensible to the men, yet
the message, even if misinterpreted, was very

03:26:25.739 --> 03:26:27.300
clear: beware!

03:26:27.300 --> 03:26:29.399
Another shrieking cry over the radio.

03:26:29.399 --> 03:26:31.259
“The bullets…the bullets aren’t…

03:26:31.260 --> 03:26:32.220
they aren’t working.

03:26:32.220 --> 03:26:33.180
They can’t.

03:26:33.180 --> 03:26:34.620
They can’t penetrate the bark!”

03:26:34.620 --> 03:26:39.359
The grass is no greener over on the eastside
of the orchard, where BETA SQUAD gets lunged

03:26:39.359 --> 03:26:41.339
at by an 4608-1.

03:26:41.340 --> 03:26:46.979
Their defenses are futile, but they fight,
nonetheless, sending rounds to the attacker’s

03:26:46.979 --> 03:26:48.599
chest - leading to…

03:26:48.600 --> 03:26:49.319
Nothing.

03:26:49.319 --> 03:26:54.359
If SCP – 4608 had a health meter, it wouldn’t
have budged in the slightest.

03:26:54.359 --> 03:26:59.040
Understanding the negligible impact of their
efforts and assessing their injuries, BETA

03:26:59.040 --> 03:27:03.540
SQUAD scurries to retreat to an abandoned
chapel, taking a brief refuge from war only

03:27:03.540 --> 03:27:04.859
later to be named.

03:27:04.859 --> 03:27:06.420
Quickly, they barricade the door.

03:27:06.420 --> 03:27:11.160
In the chapel, Beta-9 tends to BETA-6’s
wounds, who is in the worst shape of them

03:27:11.160 --> 03:27:13.680
all: cut, bloody, and beaten.

03:27:13.680 --> 03:27:17.520
As he lays there grimacing, he shines his
flashlight up and down the chapel’s walls

03:27:17.520 --> 03:27:20.520
until he finds a reason to stop and hold it
steady.

03:27:20.520 --> 03:27:23.520
Illuminated is an assortment of human skulls.

03:27:23.520 --> 03:27:28.800
And if this wasn’t traumatic enough, he
then spotted apple seeds embedded in BETA-6’s

03:27:28.800 --> 03:27:31.739
wounds - Apple seeds that were starting to
sprout.

03:27:31.739 --> 03:27:33.420
Beta-9 gave it to him straight.

03:27:33.420 --> 03:27:35.100
“This is going to hurt.”

03:27:35.100 --> 03:27:38.640
He drew his knife from his belt and lowered
it into his comrades' wounds.

03:27:38.640 --> 03:27:42.779
Beta-9 dug into flesh and bone, picking the
seeds out, one by one.

03:27:42.779 --> 03:27:46.259
Beta-6’s scream shook the chapel’s stained-glass
windows.

03:27:46.260 --> 03:27:51.479
As BETA-1 stood guard, he saw a blur rip past
him, as if life had suddenly been turned up

03:27:51.479 --> 03:27:52.439
to three times speed.

03:27:52.439 --> 03:27:55.319
He spun around in a circle to try to keep
his eyes on it.

03:27:55.319 --> 03:27:58.679
But as his vision refocused, he saw BETA-9
was now dead.

03:27:58.680 --> 03:28:02.939
He then shifted his gaze to BETA-6, who was
looking less and less human by the second.

03:28:02.939 --> 03:28:07.200
Branches began sprouting out of his body like
an all-consuming magic beanstalk.

03:28:07.200 --> 03:28:08.399
Out of his chest.

03:28:08.399 --> 03:28:09.359
Out of his eyes.

03:28:09.359 --> 03:28:10.200
Out of his mouth.

03:28:10.200 --> 03:28:15.899
And when there were no more orifices to exit,
his body exploded, making way for the new

03:28:15.899 --> 03:28:17.460
form that had overtaken him.

03:28:17.460 --> 03:28:19.907
The barrage of branches broke through the
windows, and the squads fell like dominos.

03:28:19.907 --> 03:28:19.979
Dominos not just tapped over gently but kicked
by a toddler on full tilt.

03:28:19.979 --> 03:28:22.919
Only two were lucky enough to be on the outskirts
of inertia.

03:28:22.920 --> 03:28:27.359
Outside, GAMMA-1 was on his knees thanking
his dead comrade for the grenade he stole

03:28:27.359 --> 03:28:28.319
from his back pocket.

03:28:28.319 --> 03:28:30.359
“I could always count on you to have my
back.

03:28:30.359 --> 03:28:31.559
Even in death.”

03:28:31.560 --> 03:28:37.260
One hand holding a grenade and the other on
his radio, Gamma-1 called off Alpha-7: “Alpha-7.

03:28:37.260 --> 03:28:39.000
Request for backup rescinded.

03:28:39.000 --> 03:28:40.020
Go grab a burger.

03:28:40.020 --> 03:28:41.460
I’ll take it from here.”

03:28:41.460 --> 03:28:48.359
Gamma-1 slowly glanced up and locked eyes
with SCP-4608-2, a large apple tree with 13

03:28:48.359 --> 03:28:54.000
human faces embedded into it, a perennial
plant with great powers, a gymnosperm that

03:28:54.000 --> 03:28:55.140
has found a voice.

03:28:55.140 --> 03:28:59.460
Blood poured from SCP – 4608 – 2’s empty
eye sockets.

03:28:59.460 --> 03:29:02.460
Gamma-One smirks: “Get some eye drops, sicko.”

03:29:02.460 --> 03:29:03.960
He crawled over to the beast.

03:29:03.960 --> 03:29:07.020
The faces begin yelling at him in indescribable
tongues.

03:29:07.020 --> 03:29:11.700
“Let me refer you to a speech therapist,”
he jokes as he pulls the pin of the grenade

03:29:11.700 --> 03:29:14.519
and throws it toward the largest of the thirteen
mouths.

03:29:14.520 --> 03:29:20.819
SCP – 4608-2 chokes on the grenade, forcing
it to inhale deeply… the strength of its

03:29:20.819 --> 03:29:23.279
lungs pulling Gamma – 1 toward it and sucking
him in.

03:29:23.279 --> 03:29:24.599
The grenade goes off.

03:29:24.600 --> 03:29:27.840
SCP-4608-2 explodes.

03:29:27.840 --> 03:29:30.180
The surrounding trees scream and combust.

03:29:30.180 --> 03:29:35.220
The orchard goes up in flames, the bodies
of the fallen are given an appropriate cremation.

03:29:35.220 --> 03:29:37.739
Gamma–1’s radio lay face up on the dirt.

03:29:37.739 --> 03:29:39.239
A voice rattles it awake.

03:29:39.239 --> 03:29:40.019
It’s Alpha–7.

03:29:40.020 --> 03:29:42.060
“Gamma–1.
Gamma-1, you there?

03:29:42.060 --> 03:29:43.380
Can you hear me?

03:29:43.380 --> 03:29:44.220
Please.

03:29:44.220 --> 03:29:48.180
Please, Gamma -1?”

03:29:48.180 --> 03:29:54.660
On October 16, 1947 ALPHA-7 was recovered
by the Allen County Fire Department, unconscious

03:29:54.660 --> 03:29:57.180
and suffering from exhaustion&nbsp;
and smoke inhalation.

03:29:57.180 --> 03:30:01.739
The Site-81 Concealment Team took control
of the situation and quarantined the area

03:30:01.739 --> 03:30:04.249
using the cover story of a toxic chemical
hazard.

03:30:04.249 --> 03:30:04.301
Following debriefing and a&nbsp;
psychological evaluation,&nbsp;

03:30:04.301 --> 03:30:04.380
ALPHA-7 was administered amnestics and switched
to low-risk recovery assignment.

03:30:04.380 --> 03:30:09.300
The members of MTF Bravo-7 were posthumously
awarded the Foundation Star for their efforts

03:30:09.300 --> 03:30:13.200
during the neutralization of SCP-4608.

03:30:13.200 --> 03:30:16.319
And so, the one question that remains is…
how?

03:30:16.319 --> 03:30:23.639
How did SCP -4608-1 become so dangerous, and
how did its danger slip by for so many years?

03:30:23.640 --> 03:30:27.060
Is its volatility by nature,&nbsp;
design, or consequence?

03:30:27.060 --> 03:30:31.020
Could it be that the Foundation failed to
understand the complexity of this creation?

03:30:31.020 --> 03:30:36.899
During Chapman’s lifetime, there were no
accidents or fatalities coming from SCP – 4608.

03:30:36.899 --> 03:30:43.019
Yet, there is no reason to believe that SCP
– 4608 -1 wasn’t always capable of harm.

03:30:43.020 --> 03:30:48.000
Maybe it always was capable of mass murders,
but simply had no reason to kill.

03:30:48.000 --> 03:30:51.300
What if the logging company never stepped
foot on that land?

03:30:51.300 --> 03:30:54.300
Never brought out their sharp blades and heavy
machinery?

03:30:54.300 --> 03:30:58.200
What if this perilous orchard was in fact
docile, but provoked?

03:30:58.200 --> 03:31:03.000
What if the proverbial tree only falls in
the woods when we force our philosophy on

03:31:03.000 --> 03:31:03.120
it.

03:31:03.120 --> 03:31:09.420
Though SCP -4608-2 spoke in unidentifiable
sounds, the noises were always recognized

03:31:09.420 --> 03:31:10.920
and recorded as language.

03:31:10.920 --> 03:31:14.160
It spoke with intent, even if misunderstood.

03:31:14.160 --> 03:31:16.559
What it screamed is still unclear.

03:31:16.560 --> 03:31:17.939
Were they pleas for help?

03:31:17.939 --> 03:31:19.379
Or messages of hate?

03:31:19.380 --> 03:31:21.600
And would one even be worse than the other?

03:31:21.600 --> 03:31:27.120
John Chapman might argue, when facing heavy
machinery and trained artillery, would raising

03:31:27.120 --> 03:31:29.939
your voice even be a moral decision at all?

03:31:29.939 --> 03:31:34.439
Is fight or flight imbued not just in blood…
but also in bark?

03:31:34.439 --> 03:31:40.139
The ‘devil on your shoulder’, your ‘guardian
angel’; these are expressions that we’ve

03:31:40.140 --> 03:31:41.520
all heard countless times.

03:31:41.520 --> 03:31:44.160
Of course, they’re not supposed to be taken
literally.

03:31:44.160 --> 03:31:49.559
None of us have a heavenly spirit looking
over us and protecting us from harm, in the

03:31:49.560 --> 03:31:52.920
same way that nobody really&nbsp;
has a little red-skinned&nbsp;

03:31:52.920 --> 03:31:55.739
imp whispering encouragement to commit atrocious

03:31:55.739 --> 03:31:57.239
deeds in someone’s ear.

03:31:57.239 --> 03:32:02.939
They’re metaphors: guardian angel refers
to any instance of seemingly divine intervention,

03:32:02.939 --> 03:32:07.500
but is more often a coincidence that ends
up benefitting a person when they need it

03:32:07.500 --> 03:32:07.800
most.

03:32:07.800 --> 03:32:13.140
And the devil on your shoulder, that’s temptation,
the little voice in the back of your head

03:32:13.140 --> 03:32:16.800
that sometimes eggs you on to do something
you know you shouldn’t.

03:32:16.800 --> 03:32:22.500
But what if there was a being that was both,
a demonic, malicious creature that also acted

03:32:22.500 --> 03:32:25.859
as a guardian for someone unable to protect
themselves?

03:32:25.859 --> 03:32:30.239
Is it even possible for a being to be both
angel and devil?

03:32:30.239 --> 03:32:34.739
And who out there could ever qualify for such
holy and hellish protection?

03:32:34.739 --> 03:32:38.460
Ombre Rouge was once a fairly normal place
to live.

03:32:38.460 --> 03:32:43.319
A small Louisiana town in one of the smallest
of these fifty United States.

03:32:43.319 --> 03:32:49.500
Its name was derived from the French language,
translating to ‘Red Shadow’, an ominous

03:32:49.500 --> 03:32:53.880
name for a township that was otherwise so
uninteresting and forgettable.

03:32:53.880 --> 03:32:59.399
In fact, if things had never panned out the
way they had, Ombre Rouge would have stayed

03:32:59.399 --> 03:33:03.179
that way, just a place where nothing interesting
ever happened.

03:33:03.180 --> 03:33:06.779
All of that changed, of&nbsp;
course, when the disappearances&nbsp;

03:33:06.779 --> 03:33:07.439
started.

03:33:07.439 --> 03:33:12.960
For anyone who might be too young to remember
them, the mid-2000s were a turbulent time.

03:33:12.960 --> 03:33:18.479
The Iraq War was in full swing, and a nationwide
financial crisis was rapidly approaching.

03:33:18.479 --> 03:33:24.179
But, in the midst of all this global chaos
and instability, the residents of Ombre Rouge

03:33:24.180 --> 03:33:28.080
were soon to be caught in the thralls of their
very own shared torment.

03:33:28.080 --> 03:33:31.920
At first, like with most bad things, it started
small.

03:33:31.920 --> 03:33:35.340
One person went missing,&nbsp;
an unfortunate occurrence,&nbsp;

03:33:35.340 --> 03:33:37.319
but not exactly unheard of.

03:33:37.319 --> 03:33:43.019
Sadly, these things happen, especially when
you live so close to the swamplands of Louisiana.

03:33:43.020 --> 03:33:46.020
People wander out into the marsh, under the&nbsp;

03:33:46.020 --> 03:33:49.020
searing heat of the sun,&nbsp;
only to suffer heatstroke,

03:33:49.020 --> 03:33:54.000
collapse, and end up buried in the dark, dank
mud, never to be seen again.

03:33:54.000 --> 03:33:58.260
Few of those living in the town took much
notice of the first disappearance.

03:33:58.260 --> 03:34:03.300
Apart from the missing person’s relatives,
many just shrugged off the news; as sad as

03:34:03.300 --> 03:34:07.859
it was, most of the townsfolk were just grateful
it hadn’t happened to any of their own family

03:34:07.859 --> 03:34:08.639
or friends.

03:34:08.640 --> 03:34:15.420
Maybe it was that ignorance, that lack of
vigilance or reaction, that meant a second

03:34:15.420 --> 03:34:19.739
resident would also be reported missing, not
long after the first.

03:34:19.739 --> 03:34:25.800
But this time was different: unlike the previous
disappearance, this one had an eyewitness.

03:34:25.800 --> 03:34:31.979
Clement Donovan – known to locals as ‘Clem’
– had spotted a passer-by while taking out

03:34:31.979 --> 03:34:32.879
bags of garbage.

03:34:32.880 --> 03:34:36.600
This unassuming pedestrian was the second
disappearance victim.

03:34:36.600 --> 03:34:41.160
Thinking little of the man, who just seemed
to be walking home, Clem went back inside.

03:34:41.160 --> 03:34:46.500
A split second later, he heard a scream from
outside and rushed back to his dimly-lit porch.

03:34:46.500 --> 03:34:52.439
It was there that Clem claimed he saw… something
retreating towards the nearby woods.

03:34:52.439 --> 03:34:57.000
However, Clem’s wild story of something
not quite human wasn’t taken seriously by

03:34:57.000 --> 03:34:57.660
local police.

03:34:57.660 --> 03:35:03.720
He’d even managed to snap a grainy photo
on his clamshell cell phone, but back in 2005,

03:35:03.720 --> 03:35:07.439
phone cameras were nowhere near as advanced
as they are today.

03:35:07.439 --> 03:35:12.120
Most Ombre Rouge locals wrote Clem off as
a crazy old man at best.

03:35:12.120 --> 03:35:17.580
But at worse, it made him look like someone
who was trying to exploit or make light of

03:35:17.580 --> 03:35:22.140
the disappearances, something that garnered
him a lot of dirty looks from his neighbors.

03:35:22.140 --> 03:35:26.700
That was, until a number of other residents
started reporting they had also witnessed

03:35:26.700 --> 03:35:27.899
a humanoid creature.

03:35:27.899 --> 03:35:32.519
It’s hard to say if any of these eyewitnesses
were genuine, and how many were just people

03:35:32.520 --> 03:35:34.140
latching on to Clem’s story.

03:35:34.140 --> 03:35:36.960
Regardless, the disappearances hadn’t stopped&nbsp;

03:35:36.960 --> 03:35:39.779
and it didn’t take long&nbsp;
for an unknown organization

03:35:39.779 --> 03:35:44.279
to roll into Ombre Rouge after hearing the
rumors of a creature sighting.

03:35:44.279 --> 03:35:49.380
A few residents, even the local sheriff’s
department, thought these shady figures were

03:35:49.380 --> 03:35:54.239
a division of forensic specialists here to
aid in the investigations into the missing

03:35:54.239 --> 03:35:54.899
persons.

03:35:54.899 --> 03:36:00.120
The more conspiratorial folks living in the
town had a different explanation, that the

03:36:00.120 --> 03:36:05.220
newcomers were a deep state-controlled, top-secret
government group, there to assess the possibility

03:36:05.220 --> 03:36:08.460
that there really was some kind of monster
on the loose.

03:36:08.460 --> 03:36:13.800
Not long after this group had arrived in Ombre
Rouge, the number of residents going missing

03:36:13.800 --> 03:36:14.819
seemed to dwindle.

03:36:14.819 --> 03:36:20.939
On the eighteenth of December 2005, they packed
up and left town, giving no explanation to

03:36:20.939 --> 03:36:21.660
the local police.

03:36:21.660 --> 03:36:27.300
Nobody knew if this secretive ‘Foundation’
had actually uncovered the perpetrator responsible

03:36:27.300 --> 03:36:32.160
for all the disappearances, if there even
was any creature like the rumors said.

03:36:32.160 --> 03:36:38.700
But whatever had transpired in that Louisiana
swamp town, one thing was clear: the moment

03:36:38.700 --> 03:36:42.479
the Foundation left, nobody else went missing
from Ombre Rouge.

03:36:42.479 --> 03:36:45.419
Or at least, not for over a decade.

03:36:45.420 --> 03:36:49.979
Before then, however, little else of note
happened in Ombre Rouge after the initial

03:36:49.979 --> 03:36:52.080
spate of missing person cases.

03:36:52.080 --> 03:36:56.279
That is, apart from a car accident that took
place just under a year after the various

03:36:56.279 --> 03:36:57.719
disappearances ended.

03:36:57.720 --> 03:37:03.300
A heavily-injured man by the name of Simon
Hays was taken to a local hospital, suffering

03:37:03.300 --> 03:37:04.680
from a severe concussion.

03:37:04.680 --> 03:37:10.080
Simon had been involved in a collision with
a car on the eleventh of November 2006.

03:37:10.080 --> 03:37:15.000
The doctors that examined him determined that
Simon had been left with short-term retrograde

03:37:15.000 --> 03:37:19.500
amnesia, a condition that affected all his
memories from prior to the accident.

03:37:19.500 --> 03:37:25.380
It was due to this that he was unable to recall
events that occurred in the years before he’d

03:37:25.380 --> 03:37:26.640
sustained his injuries.

03:37:26.640 --> 03:37:30.359
Now, what is it that makes&nbsp;
a random, if unfortunate&nbsp;

03:37:30.359 --> 03:37:32.759
car accident victim so significant?

03:37:32.760 --> 03:37:38.040
Well, Simon Hays actually became the first
person in Ombre Rouge to be declared missing

03:37:38.040 --> 03:37:39.180
in almost a decade.

03:37:39.180 --> 03:37:45.840
In 2016, ten years after his accident and
eleven after the original slew of disappearances,

03:37:45.840 --> 03:37:51.060
Simon vanished when returning to his hometown
in Louisiana to visit his family.

03:37:51.060 --> 03:37:55.560
Naturally, Simon Hays wouldn’t be the last
familiar face to return to the town.

03:37:55.560 --> 03:37:58.800
A repetition of such similar&nbsp;
and strange occurrences&nbsp;

03:37:58.800 --> 03:38:01.859
as before also brought the mysterious Foundation

03:38:01.859 --> 03:38:02.939
rolling back in.

03:38:02.939 --> 03:38:07.979
Little did the townsfolk know, in the year
that had followed the group’s original exodus

03:38:07.979 --> 03:38:10.500
from Ombre Rouge, they had lost something.

03:38:10.500 --> 03:38:16.260
On the exact same day Simon suffered his accident,
whatever it was the Foundation had left town

03:38:16.260 --> 03:38:17.880
with had managed to escape.

03:38:17.880 --> 03:38:22.380
Perhaps this was a purely coincidental occurrence,
but what if it wasn’t?

03:38:22.380 --> 03:38:27.120
After all, road traffic collisions take place
all the time, all over the world.

03:38:27.120 --> 03:38:32.880
But an accident happening in a town with a
history of people going missing, on the exact

03:38:32.880 --> 03:38:36.359
same day that this… thing escaped captivity?

03:38:36.359 --> 03:38:39.359
Maybe there was a link between these two events.

03:38:39.359 --> 03:38:42.120
At the very least, the Foundation seemed to
think so.

03:38:42.120 --> 03:38:46.920
Some of the more astute people living in the
swamp-side town noticed black, armored transport

03:38:46.920 --> 03:38:52.800
vehicles moving into their neighborhoods,
men in body armor locking down the whole of

03:38:52.800 --> 03:38:53.580
Ombre Rouge.

03:38:53.580 --> 03:38:59.160
These didn’t seem like local police, they
weren’t even the National Guard, although

03:38:59.160 --> 03:39:02.460
they were certainly heavily armed enough to
cause concern.

03:39:02.460 --> 03:39:07.020
This unit of specially trained operatives
quickly took control of the entire township,

03:39:07.020 --> 03:39:09.779
their authority never questioned by the sheriff’s
department.

03:39:09.779 --> 03:39:13.080
The place was small enough,&nbsp;
isolated by surrounding&nbsp;

03:39:13.080 --> 03:39:15.540
swamps and marshland, that it was easy for

03:39:15.540 --> 03:39:19.500
Mobile Task Force Epsilon-6 to get away with
an operation like this.

03:39:19.500 --> 03:39:24.239
Before the people of Ombre Rouge had time
to argue, the Task Force had already begun

03:39:24.239 --> 03:39:25.139
their investigation.

03:39:25.140 --> 03:39:31.319
The newest series of disappearances had started
in 2016 with Simon Hays mysteriously vanishing,

03:39:31.319 --> 03:39:33.960
and had continued two years later in 2018.

03:39:33.960 --> 03:39:40.920
Just like the first spate back in 2005, there
were sporadic and unconfirmed eyewitness accounts

03:39:40.920 --> 03:39:43.859
of a creature, shaped like&nbsp;
a human but considerably&nbsp;

03:39:43.859 --> 03:39:46.439
taller, almost two meters in height.

03:39:46.439 --> 03:39:51.960
Most witnesses reported only ever seeing this
local bogeyman at night time, making it much

03:39:51.960 --> 03:39:58.260
harder to see in detail, although a few seemed
to state its skin was deep red, unlike any

03:39:58.260 --> 03:39:59.880
natural human skin tone.

03:39:59.880 --> 03:40:04.620
While before, residents of the Louisiana swamp
town had brushed off stories like this as

03:40:04.620 --> 03:40:09.540
nothing more than rumors and urban legends,
the Foundation seemed pretty receptive to

03:40:09.540 --> 03:40:13.080
the idea of some kind of monster on the loose
in the marshland.

03:40:13.080 --> 03:40:18.840
And after all, they had good reason to believe
such an outlandish story… because it was

03:40:18.840 --> 03:40:23.220
the same creature that had already escaped
from them in 2006.

03:40:23.220 --> 03:40:28.260
Continuing their investigation into the link
between Simon Hays and this creature, Mobile

03:40:28.260 --> 03:40:33.600
Task Force Epsilon-6 – also known by the
codename the ‘Village Idiots’ – arrived

03:40:33.600 --> 03:40:34.979
at Hays’ place of residence.

03:40:34.979 --> 03:40:40.200
Kicking the door down, breaching the house,
they began a room-by-room sweep, looking for

03:40:40.200 --> 03:40:44.399
any clues that would explain why the monster
they’d captured escaped on the same day

03:40:44.399 --> 03:40:45.540
as Simon’s accident.

03:40:45.540 --> 03:40:51.000
One of the MTF operatives uncovered something,
an envelope stashed in the home Simon had

03:40:51.000 --> 03:40:51.540
grown up in.

03:40:51.540 --> 03:40:56.880
He opened it cautiously, a collection of papers
that were contained inside came spilling out.

03:40:56.880 --> 03:41:01.979
They were a series of simple drawings on paper
that seemed to be more than a few years old.

03:41:01.979 --> 03:41:07.319
The crudeness of the hand-scrawled pictures
and age of the paper seemed to imply they

03:41:07.319 --> 03:41:08.819
had been created by a child.

03:41:08.819 --> 03:41:14.460
A number of the drawings depicted the same
thing: a red-skinned creature, just like the

03:41:14.460 --> 03:41:16.500
one the townsfolk had reported seeing.

03:41:16.500 --> 03:41:19.859
With them was a note, written by Simon’s
mother, which read:

03:41:19.859 --> 03:41:21.960
“Found these old drawings of yours.

03:41:21.960 --> 03:41:23.819
Thought you might like to see them again.

03:41:23.819 --> 03:41:25.139
Welcome home.”

03:41:25.140 --> 03:41:30.899
There was a link, an unclear, maybe tangential
connection but one that was growing the more

03:41:30.899 --> 03:41:32.819
information the Foundation uncovered.

03:41:32.819 --> 03:41:38.939
Whatever this being was, a very young Simon
Hays had seen it while growing up in Ombre

03:41:38.939 --> 03:41:39.359
Rouge.

03:41:39.359 --> 03:41:44.279
Due to the short-term retrograde amnesia that
he’d sustained after his accident, he wouldn’t

03:41:44.279 --> 03:41:48.960
have remembered it, but perhaps this… thing
remembered him.

03:41:48.960 --> 03:41:52.080
Did that mean the pair of them might be linked
somehow?

03:41:52.080 --> 03:41:56.939
Not just by coincidence, but some kind of
connection that allowed the creature to escape

03:41:56.939 --> 03:42:00.540
its captivity on the exact day Simon had his
car accident.

03:42:00.540 --> 03:42:06.720
A connection that had drawn Hays back home
to Ombre Rouge, or drawn the beast to Simon

03:42:06.720 --> 03:42:07.739
to kidnap him.

03:42:07.739 --> 03:42:13.439
Moving fast, MTF Epsilon-6 began to rapidly
sweep the remainder of the town, searching

03:42:13.439 --> 03:42:17.639
for any further signs that would lead them
to the whereabouts of either Simon Hays or

03:42:17.640 --> 03:42:19.979
this elusive, crimson-skinned bogeyman.

03:42:19.979 --> 03:42:24.839
They interviewed residents and chased cold
leads, before eventually backing their target

03:42:24.840 --> 03:42:26.040
into a corner.

03:42:26.040 --> 03:42:30.479
The Foundation’s MTF operatives mapped the
location of every eyewitness report of the

03:42:30.479 --> 03:42:34.979
creature, using that information to track
it back to a possible point of origin.

03:42:34.979 --> 03:42:40.679
It was a barn, left abandoned, practically
falling apart as it stood in a state of disrepair

03:42:40.680 --> 03:42:43.080
just outside the small Louisiana town.

03:42:43.080 --> 03:42:48.420
Under the cover of darkness, the task force
approached the wooden structure, weapons locked

03:42:48.420 --> 03:42:50.880
and loaded, keeping them trained on the barn.

03:42:50.880 --> 03:42:55.920
Cautiously moving closer, remaining on high
alert, the squad activated their night vision.

03:42:55.920 --> 03:43:00.899
There was the low, almost undetectable sound
of movement coming from within the barn.

03:43:00.899 --> 03:43:05.580
Slowly, the MTF’s leader pushed open the
wooden door and peeked inside.

03:43:05.580 --> 03:43:11.279
It was there he saw what they had been looking
for, the thing that had escaped the Foundation

03:43:11.279 --> 03:43:17.759
over ten years before: SCP-3631, a Man and
his Monster.

03:43:17.760 --> 03:43:23.819
The beast was just over six feet tall, its
skin a bloody shade of crimson just as some

03:43:23.819 --> 03:43:25.620
of the eyewitnesses had described.

03:43:25.620 --> 03:43:30.180
It sported a pair of arms and bipedal legs,
giving it a humanoid shape.

03:43:30.180 --> 03:43:34.439
However, that was exactly where its likeness
to human beings ended.

03:43:34.439 --> 03:43:42.899
The creature, later designated as SCP-3631-1,
lacked eyes, ears, or a nose, only a wide,

03:43:42.899 --> 03:43:44.700
gaping maw of sharp teeth.

03:43:44.700 --> 03:43:50.160
Its face was covered in holes that twitched
and puckered like smaller, miniature mouths.

03:43:50.160 --> 03:43:56.760
In actuality, it used these orifices for various
senses; it smelled, saw, and detected sounds

03:43:56.760 --> 03:43:59.880
through the holes in its otherwise mostly
featureless face.

03:43:59.880 --> 03:44:05.460
As the members of MTF Epsilon-6 entered the
barn stealthily, making sure not to alert

03:44:05.460 --> 03:44:09.239
SCP-3631-1, they sighted something else.

03:44:09.239 --> 03:44:15.359
Someone else was in the barn with it, a man,
not a dead victim or another monster like

03:44:15.359 --> 03:44:20.759
SCP-3631-1, but an actual, living, breathing
human man.

03:44:20.760 --> 03:44:24.600
MTF Epsilon-6’s commander gave his squad
the signal to engage.

03:44:24.600 --> 03:44:29.700
Hearing the sounds of weapons cocking around
it, the creature turned and snarled, crawling

03:44:29.700 --> 03:44:31.800
on all fours like an animalistic predator.

03:44:31.800 --> 03:44:36.479
At first, it reared back, It wasn’t until
one member of the task force approached that

03:44:36.479 --> 03:44:42.239
SCP-3631-1 retaliated, attacking the Foundation
operatives in a frenzy.

03:44:42.239 --> 03:44:48.179
Following a prolonged and bloody exchange,
MTF Epsilon-6 managed to subdue the creature

03:44:48.180 --> 03:44:50.460
and were able to once again return it to&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:44:50.460 --> 03:44:51.840
Foundation
captivity.

03:44:51.840 --> 03:44:58.739
But this time, unlike back in 2005, they had
SCP-3631-2 as well.

03:44:58.739 --> 03:45:03.660
As the red monster was prepped for transport,
a survivor of the task force noticed something:

03:45:03.660 --> 03:45:07.920
an ID, perhaps a driver’s license, on the
man’s person.

03:45:07.920 --> 03:45:12.960
The Epsilon-6 operative picked the card up,
wiping away smears of blood with a gloved

03:45:12.960 --> 03:45:17.340
finger, enough to reveal a single, familiar
name printed on it…

03:45:17.340 --> 03:45:18.779
Simon Hays.

03:45:18.779 --> 03:45:24.960
Before long, just like last time, the Foundation
rolled back out of Ombre Rouge, leaving the

03:45:24.960 --> 03:45:28.020
Louisiana townsfolk none the wiser about what
had happened there.

03:45:28.020 --> 03:45:32.520
Little did they know the ‘Red Shadow’
hanging over their home had been lifted.

03:45:32.520 --> 03:45:37.620
But it had come at the cost of a number of
disappearances that would remain unsolved,

03:45:37.620 --> 03:45:43.260
people who would never be found, families
forced to go on without ever getting answers.

03:45:43.260 --> 03:45:45.359
When he was returned to the Foundation’s&nbsp;

03:45:45.359 --> 03:45:50.160
labs, SCP-3631-2 was sent&nbsp;
for extensive examination.

03:45:50.160 --> 03:45:53.279
Given the severity of the&nbsp;
invasive organ transplants&nbsp;

03:45:53.279 --> 03:45:55.620
he’d undergone, it was impossible to tell

03:45:55.620 --> 03:45:57.720
if he was, in fact, Simon.

03:45:57.720 --> 03:46:01.800
The creature had been regularly replacing
the man’s internal organs, on a monthly

03:46:01.800 --> 03:46:05.100
basis whenever they showed signs of decay
or failing.

03:46:05.100 --> 03:46:10.200
Somehow, despite the high risk of blood loss
and infection posed by this crude form of

03:46:10.200 --> 03:46:12.540
surgery, the subject had remained alive.

03:46:12.540 --> 03:46:18.540
But he was unable to speak, conscious but
showing very limited responses to stimuli.

03:46:18.540 --> 03:46:25.200
Nobody knows why the carnivorous, nocturnal
monster SCP-3631-1 took this man captive.

03:46:25.200 --> 03:46:30.720
In the same vein, it is unclear why the creature
felt such a need to protect him, going to

03:46:30.720 --> 03:46:34.680
such lengths as hunting for replacement organs
from unwilling donors.

03:46:34.680 --> 03:46:41.880
Perhaps, in a grisly, twisted way, SCP-3631-1
was the man’s guardian angel.

03:46:41.880 --> 03:46:45.120
Or maybe more a devil on his shoulder.

03:46:45.120 --> 03:46:49.439
I wonder, is it really possible for something
to be both?

